{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd","id":774491,"title":"[2nd] What you guys liked or disliked in MtAw 2nd ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-25T19:55:03-08:00","id":774491,"title":"[2nd] What you guys liked or disliked in MtAw 2nd ?","content":"Like the title say, what you guys liked or disliked of what we already know from DaveB development posts ?<br /> <br /> <b>PRO</b>:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The <b>new REACH system</b>. I really like the philosophy of <b>more Paradox, more power. Good work DaveB ! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b></li> <li><b>Praticies putting the limits of what every dot of arcanum can do</b> (the reach system looks like a good idea to make the game balancing) + <b>Unmaking spells destroying instead of causing damage</b>;</li> <li><b>Legacy with a downgrade of Gnosis requeriment</b>;</li> <li><b>Arcanum Attainments</b>;</li> <li><b>Prime new Purview;</b></li> <li><b>Yantras and rotes/praxis;</b></li> <li><b>Order merits</b><b>;</b></li> <li><b>Order flaws </b>(I really like the idea, even disliking the execution);</li> </ol><br /> <b>CON</b>:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>No relevant changes in Orders</b>.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Orders looks like a bunch of random ideas put together and continue not making any sense to me;</li> <li><b>6 dots of Arcanum to new mage</b> !!!!!!! C'mon DaveB, why the hell everyone template of Nwod and oWod begin the game with 3 dots of magical power (discipline, gift, etc) and Magebegin the game overpowered? Arcanum already are more powerfull thaan other power, <b>why not put every template in the same league of 3 dot of power</b> (this problem already exist in Ascension, cant believe that they dont change that)?</li> <li><b>Supernal Summon Attainment</b> !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! Hell, worst idea ever !!!! <b>Every 3 dot mage is pokemon master</b>, c'mon this kill the Wod mood to me. If you want to be a summoner buy some Spirit.</li> <li><b>Death Arcanum</b>, I really dislike tha idea of this Arcanum, Spirit Arcana dont make sense when you can go to other world with Mind(Astral)/Death(Underworld) and summon Ghost/Goetia without Spirit Arcana (lets face the true, you can summon any ephemeral being that you need as a ghost or goetia). In other words, having 3 Arcana to summon ephemeral beings is like split the Forces Arcana into Fire/Wind/Freeze/Kinetic Arcana;</li> <li><b>XP cost of Arcana is to low</b>...</li> <li><b>Lex Magica </b>and <b>Adamantine Hand</b>. AA give the idea that AA are only &quot;fighter class&quot;, it would be better to give <b>Oath </b>to AA in my opinion. Lex Magica I dont like because the idea that SL is a pseudo-Invictus, really dont like the concept that SL create the laws and SL judge.);</li> </ol><b>NEUTRAL:</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>ART. Its one hundred times better than Kaluta (dont want to see Kaluta in a MtAw book, never again !), but its a boring piece of art. C'mon, shown some obvious magic ! This is a problem from nearly every book of WW, because they try to shown what a mage look instead of what a mage do.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Free council cover art is what I consider a good and inspired piece of art.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> <li>Want to see a increase in Gnosis requeriment to buy Arcana. I like the Ascension rule of no Arcana with more dots than Arete;</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T20:42:48-08:00","id":774513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd#post774491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like the title say, what you guys liked or disliked of what we already know from DaveB development posts ?<br /> <br /> <b>CON</b>:<br /> <b>No relevant changes in Orders</b>.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Orders looks like a bunch of random ideas put together and continue not making any sense to me;</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I've found the Orders have fairly cohesive ideologies:<ul><li>Free Council: Humanity is Magical. Destroy servants of the Lie</li> <li>Adamantine Arrow: Life is Conflict. Learn to fight.</li> <li>Guardians of the Veil: Magic is a Privilege, not a Right.</li> <li>Mysterium: Knowledge is worth finding for its own sake.</li> <li>Silver Ladder: Mages must rule Humanity.</li> <li>Seers: The Exarchs already won, might as well serve them and get something out of it.</li> </ul><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>6 dots of Arcanum to new mage</b> !!!!!!! C'mon DaveB, why the hell everyone template of Nwod and oWod begin the game with 3 dots of magical power (discipline, gift, etc) and Magebegin the game overpowered? Arcanum already are more powerfull thaan other power, <b>why not put every template in the same league of 3 dot of power</b> (this problem already exist in Ascension, cant believe that they dont change that)? </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that starting Arcana still have a dot limit. so you're not whipping out advanced magics from character creation. Plus, Mages are supposed to be on a high power level. The World of Darkness was designed for mechanical compatibility, not power balance between splats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Death Arcanum</b>, I really dislike tha idea of this Arcanum, Spirit Arcana dont make sense when you can go to other world with Mind(Astral)/Death(Underworld) and summon Ghost/Goetia without Spirit Arcana (lets face the true, you can summon any ephemeral being that you need as a ghost or goetia). In other words, having 3 Arcana to summon ephemeral beings is like split the Forces Arcana into Fire/Wind/Freeze/Kinetic Arcana; </div> </div> </div>Death covers more than just ghosts, you realize. It covers <i>all of death</i>. It's entropy, change and shadows as much as is it spooky scary skeletons. Plus, Spirits and Astrals are different. a Spirit is a reflection of a concept as it is. Astrals are reflections of human perceptions of those concepts. A love spirit may have traits that reflect parts of love that most people don't associate with love. Plus, controlling a spirit is easier and safer than coalescing an Astral into reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Lex Magica </b>and <b>Adamantine Hand</b>. AA give the idea that AA are only &quot;fighter class&quot;, it would be better to give <b>Oath </b>to AA in my opinion. Lex Magica I dont like because the idea that SL is a pseudo-Invictus, really dont like the concept that SL create the laws and SL judge.); </div> </div> </div>There's no &quot;fighter class.&quot; Yeah, AA is the most focused on combat, but they aren't just about combat. They are about <i>conflict</i>. Conflict can be found in the ring and battlefield, but you can also find it in the courtroom or the boardroom just as easily.<br /> <br /> The whole point of Silver Ladder is that they want to be the Mage-Kings of the world. Of course they're going to be making rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T21:42:18-08:00","id":774540,"title":"","content":"I wonder why people are still so stuck up in Ascension territory and bring it in to Awakening discussions. Its not like you cannot still play that game if you like it. Hey it even has a new book out. I hear this almost every day or at least once a week.<br /> <br /> I won't go over every argument, just two of them.<br /> <br /> <b>The 6 dots Argument: </b>Despite having lots of flexibility, other supernaturals have some of their most useful powers built right in and have no need to cast spells to activate them. Vampires are my favorite example. Before taking Disciplines into account, a vampire has access to: instantaneously regenerating or boosting physical stats with Vitae, downgrading damage, fuel stat is far easier to replenish than Mana, hightened senses, capacity to assert dominance / seduce / terrorize targets simply by spending willpower, and also being motherfucking blood drinking immortals. Mages get... Mage Sight, and it costs Mana. Other attainments come into play if you have the correct Arcana dots only. What makes a Mage is being able to use a variety of spells, and thus you need some dots to play around and make that happen. Furthermore Disciplines combine 3 stats into a roll, but most spell only combine 2, thus Mages have less success rate with magic despite the flexibility. So, don't take the flexibility away, it is kinda core to the game experience.<br /> <br /> <b>The Death argument: </b>Well, you could say the same about Spirit in Ascension. It never made sense to me why you needed to combine Spirit + Entropy to do ghost stuff. Also, in Ascension you would need Spirit + Mind if you want to do something like the Goetics from Awakening too. CWoD already had some kind of nebulous division between ephemerals, and nWoD simply made the categorization clearer. I agree that the Core book presentation of Spirit/Death wasn't 100% clear, but it has become much better over the years and there are some great supplements for all the basic ephemeral types now. Furthermore, each ephemeral type has a very different flavor to it. Ghosts have anchors, Spirits do not. Spirits have Influences over a variety of things, Ghosts only through Anchors. Astral Realms details a bunch of Goetic / Astral things that are unlike Ghosts and Spirits. In essence (no pun intended) having more different kinds of ephemerals to play around with can enhance the feeling of depth in the world. In fact, as a Mage ST I love that they keep adding new books with new strange things and entity categories, every book adds new stuff that a Mage can investigate. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T01:05:11-08:00","id":774600,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Spirit is much more than just Spirits, and Death is much more than just Ghosts. While Life is the Thyrsus Arcana that allows you to interact with animated, living world, Spirit is not only the &quot;mental&quot; part of the Watchtower, but also &quot;material, unliving, unanimated&quot; part of it. Pretty much every single item has a Spirit. By focusing just on Spirits in Spirit, you are willingly throwing out half of your options.<br /> <br /> As for Order Merits - honestly, I hope that you anyone fulfilling the Requirements can train in them. Giving people reasons to have Status in multiple organisations is always good, because it creates conflicts of loyalties and interests, *and* gives you reason to seek friendship with organisations other than your homebase. <br /> At least, that's for Lex Magica and Adamantine Hand. I have harder time imagining Mask and Mysterium Merit being open for shopping. But first two? Sure, just get a dot of status, train under us for some time, and then let's keep being friends. We will count on you, too. I know this is probably not how it will be in the book, but this is the way I'm going to GM it, unless book convices me otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 11-26-2015, 04:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T02:53:17-08:00","id":774637,"title":"","content":"It's a 2nd edition; not a completely new game. I agree with some of your points but they're largely inherent in the game already. Generally, the two WoDs haven't used new editions to create wildly different settings. They refine what's already there.<br /> <br /> Plus most of them are workable enough that I don't really care too much. I mean, I kinda agree that the Death/spirit divide feels kinda artificial but, it works interestingly into the setting that taking it out would require a huge amount of rewriting and reconceptualisation; and I doubt it would be worth the effort.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it would be better to give <b>Oath </b>to AA in my opinion. </div> </div> </div>That's not a bad idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Order Merits - honestly, I hope that you anyone fulfilling the Requirements can train in them. Giving people reasons to have Status in multiple organisations is always good, because it creates conflicts of loyalties and interests, *and* gives you reason to seek friendship with organisations other than your homebase. </div> </div> </div>I get the reasoning, but I don't really agree. I think the point of both is that you're internalising and embodying the ethos of the Order. To me it seems reasonable that you can't embody two different castes. To work, I think you'd need to change how the Orders work; get rid of the Atlantean symbolism (you might be fine with that, but I can see why the writers aren't).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T02:55:09-08:00","id":774638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd#post774491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like the title say, what you guys liked or disliked of what we already know from DaveB development posts ?<br /> <br /> <b>PRO</b>:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The <b>new REACH system</b>. I really like the philosophy of <b>more Paradox, more power. Good work DaveB ! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b></li> <li><b>Praticies putting the limits of what every dot of arcanum can do</b> (the reach system looks like a good idea to make the game balancing) + <b>Unmaking spells destroying instead of causing damage</b>;</li> <li><b>Legacy with a downgrade of Gnosis requeriment</b>;</li> <li><b>Arcanum Attainments</b>;</li> <li><b>Prime new Purview;</b></li> <li><b>Yantras and rotes/praxis;</b></li> <li><b>Order merits</b><b>;</b></li> <li><b>Order flaws </b>(I really like the idea, even disliking the execution);</li> </ol><b>CON</b>:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>No relevant changes in Orders</b>.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Orders looks like a bunch of random ideas put together and continue not making any sense to me;</li> <li><b>6 dots of Arcanum to new mage</b> !!!!!!! C'mon DaveB, why the hell everyone template of Nwod and oWod begin the game with 3 dots of magical power (discipline, gift, etc) and Magebegin the game overpowered? Arcanum already are more powerfull thaan other power, <b>why not put every template in the same league of 3 dot of power</b> (this problem already exist in Ascension, cant believe that they dont change that)?</li> <li><b>Supernal Summon Attainment</b> !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! Hell, worst idea ever !!!! <b>Every 3 dot mage is pokemon master</b>, c'mon this kill the Wod mood to me. If you want to be a summoner buy some Spirit.</li> <li><b>Death Arcanum</b>, I really dislike tha idea of this Arcanum, Spirit Arcana dont make sense when you can go to other world with Mind(Astral)/Death(Underworld) and summon Ghost/Goetia without Spirit Arcana (lets face the true, you can summon any ephemeral being that you need as a ghost or goetia). In other words, having 3 Arcana to summon ephemeral beings is like split the Forces Arcana into Fire/Wind/Freeze/Kinetic Arcana;</li> <li><b>XP cost of Arcana is to low</b>...</li> <li><b>Lex Magica </b>and <b>Adamantine Hand</b>. AA give the idea that AA are only &quot;fighter class&quot;, it would be better to give <b>Oath </b>to AA in my opinion. Lex Magica I dont like because the idea that SL is a pseudo-Invictus, really dont like the concept that SL create the laws and SL judge.);</li> </ol><b>NEUTRAL:</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>ART. Its one hundred times better than Kaluta (dont want to see Kaluta in a MtAw book, never again !), but its a boring piece of art. C'mon, shown some obvious magic ! This is a problem from nearly every book of WW, because they try to shown what a mage look instead of what a mage do.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Free council cover art is what I consider a good and inspired piece of art.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> <li>Want to see a increase in Gnosis requeriment to buy Arcana. I like the Ascension rule of no Arcana with more dots than Arete;</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>Other supernaturals don't need dots in power sets as much as mages given they have big time inherent powers while mages get mage sight and attainments which cost mana per use. With mage sight likely just tempting you to really get yourself in bad situations, like a cat.<br /> <br /> Death is not just about ghosts it's about all definitions of Death....entropy, shadows, lies, ghosts, souls etc.<br /> <br /> Fuck exponential experience costs What use is being a navel gazing hipster in a game about power, wisdom, corruption and the balance between them if you can't actually be a person with cosmic power that literally is above the law as far as anyone not in the club accepts? Mages work from a completely different baseline hence paradox. <br /> <br /> Summoning is classic wizardry deal with it. Because it's straight dangerous and requires favor trading so you damn well bet a mage should get huge benefits for taking the risk. <br /> <br /> I'm so tired of people thinking the Free Council is all that. Awesome they're rebels that focus on culture for power, a culture defiled and twisted by the Lie. Great move right? They have serious flaws and this isn't Mage the Ascension. Every order and path can do the science and technomagic thing if they want to. There are legacies devoted to it in fact. If I were a mage that saw the supernal everywhere, yet forever beyond my reach the last thing I'd do is immerse myself into some particular culture while knowing it's a defiled, twisted version of itself like a sewer. I'd rather mix and match the parts that haven't been defiled or twisted whenever possible. <br /> <br /> I have no idea why....<br /> <br /> 1. Magic is conflict<br /> 2. Magic is humanity's birthright<br /> 3. Magic is fragile and not for the ignorant<br /> 4. Magic is knowledge, knowledge is magic<br /> 5. Magic is found in humanity and their endeavour s <br /> 6. I got my mine so fuck you ignorant dogs. It's not that bad to be eating at The Outback while you fools eat at McDonald's. We're all in the same jail anyway <br /> <br /> Isn't damn clear.<br /> <br /> As for order merits? What makes you think that some mages don't pick up several of them from different orders if they can get away with it? It's how the GoV exist for god sake. Just don't get caught. But at a certain point you have to go all in to get the real benefits just like the Seers. There's always a point of no return no matter which order is involved. Much like how and when you use magic just know the risks and be prepared for which path you choose when paradox occurs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 11-26-2015, 06:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T03:37:25-08:00","id":774647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd#post774491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Supernal Summon Attainment</b> !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! Hell, worst idea ever !!!! <b>Every 3 dot mage is pokemon master</b>, c'mon this kill the Wod mood to me. If you want to be a summoner buy some Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Supernal Summon Attainment does not make you a &quot;pokemon master&quot; in any sense. Supernal beings are immaterial, made of living symbolism. You can bargain with them, and get them to perform spell like effects, but they can't fight your enemies physically like a materialized Spirit can. Also, being able to summon them does not mean that you are able to control them. While a mage with the Spirit Arcanum can just force a spirit to do his bidding, a supernal summoning always needs bargaining, or at least it did in first edition.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The other negative points have already been adressed sufficiently by other posters I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T04:00:58-08:00","id":774659,"title":"","content":"Come now, let's not make this solely a thread about arguing against a single person's disliked details.<br /> <br /> I'll need to check back through the blogs and previews to see if there is anything that is not to my fancy; I'm sure there has to be at least something.<br /> <br /> Watch this space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T05:06:22-08:00","id":774686,"title":"","content":"I understand why these merits are great from writer stand point. I don't like their restriction from player and game perspective, because it basically punishes you for creating characters that can't or don't want to use their Order Merit. If you want to make combat mage from Mysterium, who is punching people and then casting spells at them, you are suffering opportunity costs from not being Adamantine Arrow. If you are a Silver Ladderite who doesn't care about being Magical Magistrate and does not want to pour points into Consilium/Silver Ladder status, you are suffering because your &quot;Order Merit perk&quot; is useless for you. Your Adamantine Arrow lawyer who carries a gun for self defense and acts as a magical policeman won't even look at Adamantine Hand. <br /> By opening up them for anyone meeting requirements (which, again, requires them to have Order Status - which is *at least* being respected ally and friend of the Order), your Mysterium adventurous archeologist can whip up some awesome Adamantine Hand manuevers while kicking these temple snakes away, and your Adamantine Arrow lawyer can be THE LAW. And again, for both of these, I can see these orders actually *agreeing* to share these &quot;secrets&quot; - Adamantine Arrow being there to serve, and if someone is *capable* of learning it and surviving, then well, so be it.<br /> Lex Magica being taught is probably most in character, because it means that maybe while Silver Ladder person won't hold the office, Ladder thinking will still be there. You basically infect someone with your ideas on magical law and they spread it. Silver Ladder don't want everyone to be them, but to make everyone think like them and agree with them; and if for some reason person holding local &quot;magical law enforcement office&quot; isn't Silver Ladder but Guardian, if you taught him this, it doesn't really matter; because he is following the Silver Ladder thinking. It's their victory. <br /> Also, from another perspective: you give members of Orders reason to interact with other Orders. They have something you want and could use. It creates dynamics, needs and wants, economics of favors...basically, a living community that has reasons to go and play with each other, instead of being hermits in their own societies.<br /> From game perspective, its' more viable archetypes and more variety, plus making each merit more &quot;worth the paper&quot; it's printed on. <br /> <br /> Mysterium order merit and Masks are much, much harder for me to see taught out of order, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T05:19:31-08:00","id":774697,"title":"","content":"It should be noted we don't know exactly what the Mysterium merit looks like right now. There was mention of changing it a bit after the backlash from what was previewed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T06:19:34-08:00","id":774728,"title":"","content":"@3. If you try treating a supernal entity as a pokemon your in for big, Big, BIG trouble. Though i must say I'm partly dissapointed in attainments. Some are cool but i don't like the lack of variety in certain cases (1st and 3rd dot attainments are the same all over the board) and some just don't feel like they matter much.<br /> <br /> I also feel the Yantra limit per Gnosis is too restricting but I understand why it's there. Also Yantras feel a bit limited in the scope of what can be one.<br /> <br /> Though in general from what i read in the development blogs there is much more things i like but this thread is about complaining so....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T08:20:15-08:00","id":774814,"title":"","content":"I'd have preferred one yantra per Gnosis because it would be that much simpler to remember. The idea to limit them was a good idea though or we'd be in the same spot as the Dresen Files game wracking our brains for ways to get just that one more +2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T09:49:03-08:00","id":774873,"title":"","content":"There's very little I don't like of what we've been shown so far, and it's unfair to judge things we've only heard about, but let's see:<ul><li>I don't like how the presentation of the Atlantis myth has changed in some parts. In particular I <i>hate </i>that one example character in the Mysterium preview called the Awakened city a &quot;Lie&quot; with the capital letter. I know, I know, I've already heard every argument for it, and read DaveB's position on it on several forums, but still raises my hackles, and <i>no, </i>I'm not interested in someone trying to argue it with me, so please don't.</li> <li>Some of the spoiled order merits: the new Adamantine Hand is very likely much more useful and balanced the 1e AH (which had that dumb last dot, which required Archmastery to be usable), but it's also incredibly boring; the Masque merit is the same, with being a lot more mechanically engaging and worth the XP, but I loved the 49 archetypal Masques and their chapter in the GotV orderbook, so new merit leaves me un-enthusiastic; it's mostly the same refrain with the new Prelacy (except for one thing that I'm going to outright change: Mystery Command is something that any Seer should be able to have, not just Prelates): more concise and direct, but also more uniform, with pretty much only the Crown (and the Sword a bit) really differentiating between a Prelate of the Father and one of the Eye. Now, I know why all this is this way: they wanted to get all the Order's unique merits and tricks right in the core, and DaveB has often said that they had issues with wordcount because they wanted to fit everything they could. The new Masque is of course an artifact of the Virtue/Vice system of the GMC, and the old Prelacy were arguably too powerful (but fittingly so, IMO) and were harder to homebrew than Legacies, while the new one simply requires you come come up with a single Attainment to create say the Prelacy of someone dedicated to the Prophet. I'm still going to miss it.</li> </ul><br /> And that's it, I think. Pretty much everything else we've been spoiled or that Dave has hinted at has ranged from &quot;Awesome!&quot; to &quot;I'm interested, but I'll wait and see before I say more&quot;. The only other thing I don't like is the Free Council, but I don't like them in 1e either, so no real change there.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty excited for the 2nd edition of my favourite WoD gameline, and I hope it goes on to have as many supplements as 1e did!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","user":"BlueBiscuit","date":". 11-26-2015, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T10:09:07-08:00","id":774887,"title":"","content":"Everything is awesome other than Wisdom, IMO. Massively improvement across the board, and it's not like Wisdom is worse than it was before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T10:45:59-08:00","id":774904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=774540#post774540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The 6 dots Argument: </b>Despite having lots of flexibility, other supernaturals have some of their most useful powers built right in and have no need to cast spells to activate them. Vampires are my favorite example. Before taking Disciplines into account, a vampire has access to: instantaneously regenerating or boosting physical stats with Vitae, downgrading damage, fuel stat is far easier to replenish than Mana, hightened senses, capacity to assert dominance / seduce / terrorize targets simply by spending willpower, and also being motherfucking blood drinking immortals. Mages get... Mage Sight, and it costs Mana. Other attainments come into play if you have the correct Arcana dots only. What makes a Mage is being able to use a variety of spells, and thus you need some dots to play around and make that happen. Furthermore Disciplines combine 3 stats into a roll, but most spell only combine 2, thus Mages have less success rate with magic despite the flexibility. So, don't take the flexibility away, it is kinda core to the game experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>And mage can have spells (unless i miss some preview) running 24/7. I dont see what flexibility has to do with getting forces 6 and blowing a city with a radiation blast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd#post774491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>Legacy with a downgrade of Gnosis requeriment</b>;[*]<b>Arcanum Attainments</b>;[*]<b>Yantras and rotes/praxis;</b>[*]<b>Order flaws </b>(I really like the idea, even disliking the execution);</div> </div> </div> </div>This is all pro for me, i love that yantras as a way to add some flavor to how bland mages then to be while i would preffer that they be a must instead of optional its good.<br /> <br /> Another pro for me is rotes, thanks you getting rid of the whole &quot;attribute + skill + arcanum&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd#post774491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>No relevant changes in Orders</b>.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Orders looks like a bunch of random ideas put together and continue not making any sense to me;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is con for me. While they fixed the free council from its 1st democracy propaganda they didnt fix the guardian of the veil with their jebus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd#post774491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>6 dots of Arcanum to new mage</b> !!!!!!! C'mon DaveB, why the hell everyone template of Nwod and oWod begin the game with 3 dots of magical power (discipline, gift, etc) and Magebegin the game overpowered? Arcanum already are more powerfull thaan other power, <b>why not put every template in the same league of 3 dot of power</b> (this problem already exist in Ascension, cant believe that they dont change that)?</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by this? That a starting PC can potentially buy arcanum 6? Or that a mage can get it at chargen?<br /> <br /> Also this is something i think they havent fixed, that power creep on the lines some needed (Werewolf) some didnt (Vampire) and i think mage was in the latter. It ties with the flawed argument that mage is not a game in which player struggle to overcome obstacles but one which they will pass obstacles but its on the hands of the DM to put unforseen consequences. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd#post774491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>Supernal Summon Attainment</b> !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! Hell, worst idea ever !!!! <b>Every 3 dot mage is pokemon master</b>, c'mon this kill the Wod mood to me. If you want to be a summoner buy some Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>They dont work the same way and that was something in 1ed. At arcanum 3 you could summon your path pokemon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd#post774491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>Death Arcanum</b>, I really dislike tha idea of this Arcanum, Spirit Arcana dont make sense when you can go to other world with Mind(Astral)/Death(Underworld) and summon Ghost/Goetia without Spirit Arcana (lets face the true, you can summon any ephemeral being that you need as a ghost or goetia). In other words, having 3 Arcana to summon ephemeral beings is like split the Forces Arcana into Fire/Wind/Freeze/Kinetic Arcana;</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhmm, how exactly do i summon a fire spirit or a spirit of the city with mind or death?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd#post774491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>Lex Magica </b>and <b>Adamantine Hand</b>. AA give the idea that AA are only &quot;fighter class&quot;, it would be better to give <b>Oath </b>to AA in my opinion. Lex Magica I dont like because the idea that SL is a pseudo-Invictus, really dont like the concept that SL create the laws and SL judge.);</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda dislike this, i would preffer a more in dept merit system for the orders to make them different but i guess that dont fit in the core.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd#post774491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/LIST]<b>NEUTRAL:</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>ART. Its one hundred times better than Kaluta (dont want to see Kaluta in a MtAw book, never again !), but its a boring piece of art. C'mon, shown some obvious magic ! This is a problem from nearly every book of WW, because they try to shown what a mage look instead of what a mage do.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Free council cover art is what I consider a good and inspired piece of art.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>This is a dislike for me, i love kaluta for mage his art make me come back to mage time and time again.</li> <li>Want to see a increase in Gnosis requeriment to buy Arcana. I like the Ascension rule of no Arcana with more dots than Arete;</li> </ol>[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=774814#post774814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd have preferred one yantra per Gnosis because it would be that much simpler to remember. The idea to limit them was a good idea though or we'd be in the same spot as the Dresen Files game wracking our brains for ways to get just that one more +2.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pro for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=774513#post774513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, Mages are supposed to be on a high power level. The World of Darkness was designed for mechanical compatibility, not power balance between splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a big con for me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T11:06:47-08:00","id":774919,"title":"","content":"To be fair, to people who don't know Summoners mechanics &quot;Attainment: Summoning&quot; is pretty misleading. If anything, it's more like &quot;Commune/Contact Symbolic Being&quot; than what is usually summoned to the mind when you hear &quot;summon&quot;.<br /> It's hard to tell without looking at the spellcasting system in it's full glory, but I feel that Yantras are kinda necessary if you want to have big strong effects running around. Common yantras seem to be +1, uncommon and somehow resource expending (be it time, sacrament, opportunity or something else) seem to be +2, and iconic unique means give you +3 (for example, Lex Magica at pinnacle of it's power will give you +3).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T11:27:31-08:00","id":774928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd#post774491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like the title say, what you guys liked or disliked of what we already know from DaveB development posts ?<br /> <br /> <b>PRO</b>: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The <b>new REACH system</b>. I really like the philosophy of <b>more Paradox, more power. Good work DaveB ! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b></li> <li><b>Praticies putting the limits of what every dot of arcanum can do</b> (the reach system looks like a good idea to make the game balancing) + <b>Unmaking spells destroying instead of causing damage</b>;</li> <li><b>Legacy with a downgrade of Gnosis requeriment</b>;</li> <li><b>Arcanum Attainments</b>;</li> <li><b>Prime new Purview;</b></li> <li><b>Yantras and rotes/praxis;</b></li> <li><b>Order merits</b><b>;</b></li> <li><b>Order flaws </b>(I really like the idea, even disliking the execution);</li> </ol><br /> <br /> <b>CON</b>: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>No relevant changes in Orders</b>.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Orders looks like a bunch of random ideas put together and continue not making any sense to me;</li> <li><b>6 dots of Arcanum to new mage</b> !!!!!!! C'mon DaveB, why the hell everyone template of Nwod and oWod begin the game with 3 dots of magical power (discipline, gift, etc) and Magebegin the game overpowered? Arcanum already are more powerfull thaan other power, <b>why not put every template in the same league of 3 dot of power</b> (this problem already exist in Ascension, cant believe that they dont change that)?</li> <li><b>Supernal Summon Attainment</b> !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! Hell, worst idea ever !!!! <b>Every 3 dot mage is pokemon master</b>, c'mon this kill the Wod mood to me. If you want to be a summoner buy some Spirit.</li> <li><b>Death Arcanum</b>, I really dislike tha idea of this Arcanum, Spirit Arcana dont make sense when you can go to other world with Mind(Astral)/Death(Underworld) and summon Ghost/Goetia without Spirit Arcana (lets face the true, you can summon any ephemeral being that you need as a ghost or goetia). In other words, having 3 Arcana to summon ephemeral beings is like split the Forces Arcana into Fire/Wind/Freeze/Kinetic Arcana;</li> <li><b>XP cost of Arcana is to low</b>...</li> <li><b>Lex Magica </b>and <b>Adamantine Hand</b>. AA give the idea that AA are only &quot;fighter class&quot;, it would be better to give <b>Oath </b>to AA in my opinion. Lex Magica I dont like because the idea that SL is a pseudo-Invictus, really dont like the concept that SL create the laws and SL judge.);</li> </ol><br /> <b>NEUTRAL:</b> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>ART. Its one hundred times better than Kaluta (dont want to see Kaluta in a MtAw book, never again !), but its a boring piece of art. C'mon, shown some obvious magic ! This is a problem from nearly every book of WW, because they try to shown what a mage look instead of what a mage do.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Free council cover art is what I consider a good and inspired piece of art.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> <li>Want to see a increase in Gnosis requeriment to buy Arcana. I like the Ascension rule of no Arcana with more dots than Arete;</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>A) It is a bit early to judge, you haven't read much of anything.<br /> B) In case you haven't noticed any 3+3 Mage is ALREADY a &quot;Pokemon master&quot; this just means those other 3 don't have to be both your major ones. (You can now take your so much beloved Spirit, yuck)<br /> C) Death arcana is not the problem here, you know what is a bigger problem? Your Spirit Arcana (Swiss knife = &quot;I summon a spirit of Death&quot;,&quot;It is a spirit of Fire now&quot; &quot;I am the Rainbow Mage!&quot;)<br /> <br /> Important Note: Spirits stink","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9813-blankbadger","name":"blankbadger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T12:43:03-08:00","id":774969,"title":"","content":"@up: slightly offtopic but yeah i find spirit problematic. It either feels very limited or extremely broad and very dependant on GM fiat and ends kinda tedious when your playes routinely interact with various spirits and u have to come up with their descriptions on the fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","user":"Menace","date":". 11-26-2015, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T13:13:46-08:00","id":774991,"title":"","content":"It's limited in that you unless you provide for your spirit minions to survive in Twilight then it's most operable in the Shadow...which is a whole other realm and removed to some degree from the Fallen.<br /> <br /> At 4 dots any spirit you can get your hands on manages to become a swiss army knife spirit since you can twist it into anything. It might not be appreciative of that though, because unless you're exerting mystical resources to maintain a leash on a spirit then it's a diplomatic enterprise to work with one and they're so single-minded that could easily end in disaster.<br /> <br /> To be fair though, you run into similar things with Mind and Death and to a lesser extent all of the other arcana.<br /> <br /> As to the ST problem of having to make up new NPCs on the fly, well that's a problem as old as the game itself. There's not really any getting around it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T13:51:06-08:00","id":775007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And mage can have spells (unless i miss some preview) running 24/7. I dont see what flexibility has to do with getting forces 6 and blowing a city with a radiation blast. </div> </div> </div>Do you even core book? XD You have a cap of three dots on your highest arcana on character creation, and two on the rest for a total of six. You can't start with Forces 6 and I never said you could or should, that's silly. The caps are fine as they are now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Want to see a increase in Gnosis requeriment to buy Arcana. I like the Ascension rule of no Arcana with more dots than Arete; </div> </div> </div>Curiously, this was possibly the thing I most disliked about Ascension and I was so happy they removed it the first time I read the core. But of course this is a matter of taste.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Yantra count... I am torn, not sure if I like or dislike the yantra limits per Gnosis. So far I've been using them and they play OK, maybe it could have been simplified, but right now it's not too hard for remember, just note your yantra cap on your sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T15:18:23-08:00","id":775057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=774904#post774904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And mage can have spells (unless i miss some preview) running 24/7. I dont see what flexibility has to do with getting forces 6 and blowing a city with a radiation blast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what he was trying to get at was that in 1e, vampires got a total of 3 points to put into Disciplines, werewolves got 3 points to put into Gifts, but mages got 6 total dots to spread across their arcana. That said, that really isn't a valid complaint anymore since I don't think the others have the same amount of stuff to spend on things in 2e. While I think vampires might still have 3 dots to put in Disciplines, werewolves have something like 4 different Gift facets at character creation, I'm not even sure if that includes rites. <br /> <br /> That said, trying to even up the numbers even in 1e would be a misguided affair because it doesn't take into consideration the outside factors such as innate traits and the difference in power gained per point in each of the splats magical capabilities with which those dots could buy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T15:47:25-08:00","id":775072,"title":"","content":"Actually, starting Werewolves have 3 dots of Renown, 4 Gift Facets and also 2 dots of Rites.<br /> <br /> Vampires have 3 dots of Disciplines. 2 must be in-Clan, 1 dot free choice. This dot could be spent on Cruac or Theban Sorcery and using the BS:S&amp;B rules that would net you 3 dots of Themes (Blood Sorcery Arcana look-alike of wich there's only 5 against the 10 Arcana).<br /> <br /> Mages have 6 dots of Arcana spread like: 2/2/2, 3/2/1, 2/2/1/1 or now in second edition also 2/1/1/1/1<br /> <br /> Unfair?<br /> <br /> Let's see what each of them gets for free, without spending a single dot in the powers department (I'll consider werewolves without any dots of Renown even if that's imposible):<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolves get, for free:</b><br /> <br /> 1) Auspice ability usable once per chapter<br /> <br /> 2) Predators Aspect usable at will<br /> <br /> 3) Passive Free Regeneration. Boosted Regeneration for a cost<br /> <br /> 4) 5 different forms, each with an especial ability, 4 with bonuses to physical Attributes and natural weapons, 3 with increased Defense against firearms, 3 causing Lunacy, 1 with uber-Regeneration. 4 of them can be used freely while the most potent one is limited in its <i>controlled</i> use to a few turns once per Scene.<br /> <br /> 5) 2 sets of improved senses, with bonuses to perception tied to the forms, above.<br /> <br /> 6) Moderate Damage reduction (Aggravated to Lethal)<br /> <br /> 7) Access to the Shadow (only at a Locus)<br /> <br /> <b>Vampires get, for free:</b><br /> <br /> 1) Regeneration for a cost<br /> <br /> 2) Great Damage Reduction (Most damage to Bashing)<br /> <br /> 3) Unaging<br /> <br /> 4) Predators Aura usable at will or at a cost<br /> <br /> 5) The Kiss, Its source of power also means damaging the enemy<br /> <br /> 6) Vitae adiction and Vinculum<br /> <br /> 7) Ghoul and Vampire creation<br /> <br /> 8) Physical Augmentation<br /> <br /> <b>Mages get, for free:</b><br /> <br /> 1) Mage Sight at will and improved version at a cost<br /> <br /> 2) Pattern Restortation (Regeneration at a cost, most likely worse than any of the others)<br /> <br /> 3) Tilt-inflicting Nimbus, likely at will, maybe at a cost<br /> <br /> 4) Access to the Astral (only at a Hallow or Demesne)<br /> <br /> Mages get more dots of &quot;learned powers&quot;, mostly because the others have a lot of innate template ones making up for it. A Mage without access to Arcana is just a human with a broad Unseen Sense a supernatural aura and a ineficient alternate method of healing*.<br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>At least in 1st edition it was a kinda underwhelming 3 Mana for each Lethal</i></span>.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":".  Added access to otherworlds as template abilities possesed by Werewolves and Mages 11-26-2015, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T15:48:32-08:00","id":775075,"title":"","content":"Saying you could get Forces 6 and still be playing Mage is also incredibly uninformed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T16:44:52-08:00","id":775094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775007#post775007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you even core book? XD You have a cap of three dots on your highest arcana on character creation, and two on the rest for a total of six. You can't start with Forces 6 and I never said you could or should, that's silly. The caps are fine as they are now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah thats in first edition. The OP was complaining that apparently in 2nd newly mage can start with 6 in an arcanum.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd#post774491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>6 dots of Arcanum to new mage</b> !!!!!!! C'mon DaveB, why the hell everyone template of Nwod and oWod begin the game with 3 dots of magical power (discipline, gift, etc) and Magebegin the game overpowered? Arcanum already are more powerfull thaan other power, <b>why not put every template in the same league of 3 dot of power</b> (this problem already exist in Ascension, cant believe that they dont change that)?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=774904#post774904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by this? That a starting PC can potentially buy arcanum 6? Or that a mage can get it at chargen?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775072#post775072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, starting Werewolves have 3 dots of Renown, 4 Gift Facets and also 2 dots of Rites.<br /> <br /> Vampires have 3 dots of Disciplines. 2 must be in-Clan, 1 dot free choice. This dot could be spent on Cruac or Theban Sorcery and using the BS:S&amp;B rules that would net you 3 dots of Themes (Blood Sorcery Arcana look-alike of wich there's only 5 against the 10 Arcana).<br /> <br /> Mages have 6 dots of Arcana spread like: 2/2/2, 3/2/1, 2/2/1/1 or now in second edition also 2/1/1/1/1<br /> <br /> Unfair?<br /> <br /> - cut it short for simplicity</div> </div> </div> </div>Arcanums arent disciplines. They cannot be compared because 1 dot in a discipline/gift face is 1 power. 1 point in an arcanum is all the spell one can think off or check in the book that fit the arcanum. Example a werewolf with the facet of tongue of flames (fire control) is not the same as a mage with forces. The werewolf can control 1 element, the mage can control 3, maybe more if one get imaginative.<br /> <br /> Im neutral to that, to me mage shine best when is not set in the world of darkness with the rest of the splats so i never ever run crossovers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T16:51:36-08:00","id":775096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=774969#post774969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@up: slightly offtopic but yeah i find spirit problematic. It either feels very limited or extremely broad and very dependant on GM fiat and ends kinda tedious when your playes routinely interact with various spirits and u have to come up with their descriptions on the fly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Something i have done, as i struggle with this and my ineptitude in symbolism is compiling all the spirits in all the books to make sorta like a D&amp;D &quot;Monster manual&quot; as to not have to made up spirit on the spot. Im gonna see if i can clean it up as index instead and uploading it on the forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T17:04:21-08:00","id":775100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775094#post775094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah thats in first edition. The OP was complaining that apparently in 2nd newly mage can start with 6 in an arcanum.<br /> <br /> Arcanums arent disciplines. They cannot be compared because 1 dot in a discipline/gift face is 1 power. 1 point in an arcanum is all the spell one can think off or check in the book that fit the arcanum. Example a werewolf with the facet of tongue of flames (fire control) is not the same as a mage with forces. The werewolf can control 1 element, the mage can control 3, maybe more if one get imaginative.<br /> <br /> Im neutral to that, to me mage shine best when is not set in the world of darkness with the rest of the splats so i never ever run crossovers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever gave you that idea that the cap is higher than 3? The major change is that you can have 1 dot in 6 arcana or basically have any spread allowable with a cap of 3 in any single arcanum. <br /> <br /> 1. 3/3<br /> 2. 3/2/1<br /> 3. 2/2/2<br /> 4.2/2/1/1<br /> 5. 2/1/1/1/1<br /> 6.1/1/1/1/1/1<br /> 7. 3/1/1/1<br /> <br /> Those are the possible spreads unless there's another possibility with 3 in any single arcanum as the cap I overlooked?<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bYou are correct in saying there is no comparison between a given dot level of an arcanum and a discipline or gift. The mage with a dot in Forces can affect any possible force not just the classic elemental types","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 11-26-2015, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T17:06:22-08:00","id":775101,"title":"","content":"...This hasn't been released yet, we don't know how it is going to turn out.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think it is shaping up to be something fantastic but at this point I feel like one of those blind men trying to describe an elephant; I'm only dealing with a small section (the spoilers) and without the bigger context I won't know what it looks like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T18:53:50-08:00","id":775156,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but we've seen a lot of different pieces and can comment on how we feel about those specific pieces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T19:08:04-08:00","id":775163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775094#post775094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah thats in first edition. The <b>OP was complaining that apparently in 2nd newly mage can start with 6 in an arcanum</b>.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>C'mon, why &quot;spin&quot; my argument ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You're trolling, right ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> t's absolutaly clear that I reversed the Arcana (plural) with Arcanum (singular), just look to the context of the comparison about how many dots of power new players begin the game in all Wod &quot;creature of night&quot; templates and &quot;this problem already exist in Ascension&quot;.<br /> <br /> Plus, you know that ONLY mages with 6 dots of Gnosis can buy the first dot of Imperial Arcanum (singular)/Archsphere and a mage with ONLY 3 dots of Gnosis cannot buy more than 3 dots of one Arcanum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775094#post775094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcanums arent disciplines. They cannot be compared because 1 dot in a discipline/gift face is 1 power. 1 point in an arcanum is all the spell one can think off or check in the book that fit the arcanum. Example a werewolf with the facet of tongue of flames (fire control) is not the same as a mage with forces. The werewolf can control 1 element, the mage can control 3, maybe more if one get imaginative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely right, that's why I think that a new mage dont need 6 dots of Arcana, only 3 is fine. Arcanum are already gives more options than other powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775094#post775094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im neutral to that, to me mage shine best when is not set in the world of darkness with the rest of the splats so i never ever run crossovers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, but not everyone need to have the same opinion. The developers need to build the game for everyone that whant to use the creatures of night in their games. This is one of the selling points from nWod, dont expect a 100% balanced crossover system, but giving more dots of &quot;power&quot; to the overpower Arcanum dont make sense to a World that live creatures of night.<br /> <br /> It's so easy to DaveB change the rules to create new mage to give only 3 dots of Arcana with the spread limited to Gnosis than to continue with that bad tradition of Ascension.<br /> <br /> Like I said this problem already exist in Ascension line, in the beggining I could understand the 6 dots of Spheres in Ascension 1st edition because some Spheres only works together with other Sphere (like Forces 3 and 5 only working with Prime 2 in 1st edition, amarite?), but this becomes a problem in Ascension 2nd and revised.<br /> <br /> Easy to house rule, but dont make sense a Wod with so many overgpower mage walking together with creatures of night without a open war scenario.<br /> Changin","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","user":"Sp4rt01","date":". 11-26-2015, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T19:17:41-08:00","id":775166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775163#post775163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> C'mon, why &quot;spin&quot; my argument ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You're trolling, right ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> t's absolutaly clear that I reversed the Arcana (plural) with Arcanum (singular), just look to the context of the comparison about how many dots of power new players begin the game in all Wod &quot;creature of night&quot; templates and &quot;this problem already exist in Ascension&quot;.<br /> <br /> Plus, you know that ONLY mages with 6 dots of Gnosis can buy the first dot of Imperial Arcanum (singular)/Archsphere and a mage with ONLY 3 dots of Gnosis cannot buy more than 3 dots of one Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, i got confuse because as it was &quot;things i dont like in 2nd&quot; and in 1st you got 5 points of arcanum to assign i didnt see that much difference and when you went on the whole &quot;why mages must begin so OP&quot;, it got me thinking that i missed some huge preview :P My bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T19:43:41-08:00","id":775180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775072#post775072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, starting Werewolves have 3 dots of Renown, 4 Gift Facets and also 2 dots of Rites.<br /> <br /> Vampires have 3 dots of Disciplines. 2 must be in-Clan, 1 dot free choice. This dot could be spent on Cruac or Theban Sorcery and using the BS:S&amp;B rules that would net you 3 dots of Themes (Blood Sorcery Arcana look-alike of wich there's only 5 against the 10 Arcana).<br /> <br /> Mages have 6 dots of Arcana spread like: 2/2/2, 3/2/1, 2/2/1/1 or now in second edition also 2/1/1/1/1<br /> <br /> Unfair?<br /> <br /> Let's see what each of them gets for free, without spending a single dot in the powers department (I'll consider werewolves without any dots of Renown even if that's imposible):<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolves get, for free:</b><br /> <br /> 1) Auspice ability usable once per chapter<br /> <br /> 2) Predators Aspect usable at will<br /> <br /> 3) Passive Free Regeneration. Boosted Regeneration for a cost<br /> <br /> 4) 5 different forms, each with an especial ability, 4 with bonuses to physical Attributes and natural weapons, 3 with increased Defense against firearms, 3 causing Lunacy, 1 with uber-Regeneration. 4 of them can be used freely while the most potent one is limited in its <i>controlled</i> use to a few turns once per Scene.<br /> <br /> 5) 2 sets of improved senses, with bonuses to perception tied to the forms, above.<br /> <br /> 6) Moderate Damage reduction (Aggravated to Lethal)<br /> <br /> 7) Access to the Shadow (only at a Locus)<br /> <br /> <b>Vampires get, for free:</b><br /> <br /> 1) Regeneration for a cost<br /> <br /> 2) Great Damage Reduction (Most damage to Bashing)<br /> <br /> 3) Unaging<br /> <br /> 4) Predators Aura usable at will or at a cost<br /> <br /> 5) The Kiss, Its source of power also means damaging the enemy<br /> <br /> 6) Vitae adiction and Vinculum<br /> <br /> 7) Ghoul and Vampire creation<br /> <br /> 8) Physical Augmentation<br /> <br /> <b>Mages get, for free:</b><br /> <br /> 1) Mage Sight at will and improved version at a cost<br /> <br /> 2) Pattern Restortation (Regeneration at a cost, most likely worse than any of the others)<br /> <br /> 3) Tilt-inflicting Nimbus, likely at will, maybe at a cost<br /> <br /> 4) Access to the Astral (only at a Hallow or Demesne)<br /> <br /> Mages get more dots of &quot;learned powers&quot;, mostly because the others have a lot of innate template ones making up for it. A Mage without access to Arcana is just a human with a broad Unseen Sense a supernatural aura and a ineficient alternate method of healing*.<br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>At least in 1st edition it was a kinda underwhelming 3 Mana for each Lethal</i></span>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. Good work showing to us the main &quot;genetic power&quot; for the bigger templates. Thanks<br /> 2. The comparison is unfair because the Vampire and Werewolf have serious &quot;genetic flaws&quot; (Silver/Lunacy/Fire/Sun/Beast/Rotschreck, need to drink blood, etc) when mages are normal people that can do some magic. If mages dont have the same number of advantages is because they dont have a relevant number of disadvantages like the &quot;monster of night&quot;.<br /> Paradox is a mage flaw, but it dont hurt much. C'mon, it works more like a setting device to explain why mages dont abuse of obvious magic in crowd and why they hide magic from normal people/sleepers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T19:47:36-08:00","id":775182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775163#post775163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> C'mon, why &amp;quot;spin&amp;quot; my argument ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You're trolling, right ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> t's absolutaly clear that I reversed the Arcana (plural) with Arcanum (singular), just look to the context of the comparison about how many dots of power new players begin the game in all Wod &amp;quot;creature of night&amp;quot; templates and &amp;quot;this problem already exist in Ascension&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Plus, you know that ONLY mages with 6 dots of Gnosis can buy the first dot of Imperial Arcanum (singular)/Archsphere and a mage with ONLY 3 dots of Gnosis cannot buy more than 3 dots of one Arcanum.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Absolutely right, that's why I think that a new mage dont need 6 dots of Arcana, only 3 is fine. Arcanum are already gives more options than other powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Fair, but not everyone need to have the same opinion. The developers need to build the game for everyone that whant to use the creatures of night in their games. This is one of the selling points from nWod, dont expect a 100% balanced crossover system, but giving more dots of &amp;quot;power&amp;quot; to the overpower Arcanum dont make sense to a World that live creatures of night.<br /> <br /> It's so easy to DaveB change the rules to create new mage to give only 3 dots of Arcana with the spread limited to Gnosis than to continue with that bad tradition of Ascension.<br /> <br /> Like I said this problem already exist in Ascension line, in the beggining I could understand the 6 dots of Spheres in Ascension 1st edition because some Spheres only works together with other Sphere (like Forces 3 and 5 only working with Prime 2 in 1st edition, amarite?), but this becomes a problem in Ascension 2nd and revised.<br /> <br /> Easy to house rule, but dont make sense a Wod with so many overgpower mage walking together with creatures of night without a open war scenario.<br /> Changin</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm starting to think you're trolling. You have been told that EVERY other supernatural has serious in built advantages before their power set. And that of all the supernatural types only mages are fully baseline human. So they get an ability to see the world and it's denizens as they truly are but to actually know anything factual about them they have to scrutinize them and spend mana. In the hopes that that they aren't already in the shit and too late to use their power set. So color me unimpressed about your concern of level of power that mages start with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T20:00:20-08:00","id":775187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775180#post775180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 1. Good work showing to us the main &quot;genetic power&quot; for the bigger templates. Thanks<br /> 2. The comparison is unfair because the Vampire and Werewolf have serious &quot;genetic flaws&quot; (Silver/Lunacy/Fire/Sun/Beast/Rotschreck, need to drink blood, etc) when mages are normal people that can do some magic. If mages dont have the same number of advantages is because they dont have a relevant number of disadvantages like the &quot;monster of night&quot;.<br /> Paradox is a mage flaw, but it dont hurt much. C'mon, it works more like a setting device to explain why mages dont abuse of obvious magic in crowd and why they hide magic from normal people/sleepers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox doesn't hurt? Get serious and know what you're talking about. You do know that mages have a choice concerning paradox? Either contain it as unhealable bashing damage while grounding it into your pattern, which takes time to fully expel with conditions beyond the bashing damage you take Or you can release it which guarantees everyone else gets screwed, while your spell goes off fine and then gets twisted for the worst against you but after the fact.<br /> <br /> No problem right? Sheesh. I figure if you know you're invoking paradox it's past time to play around and to start getting serious and prepare to pay the Piper before that isn't possible. Basically if you arrogant enough not to prepare and plan you deserve the price for arrogance and ignorance. It's pretty steep for your information. <br /> <br /> No other supernatural has that concern ever. Quiensense is a mage's version of Lunacy or similar. Paradox is an extra disadvantage just to make it even more fun.<br /> <br /> The reasons why mages don't just use their spells to maximum effect 24/7 is threefold. In order....<br /> <br /> 1. Quiensense, people recoil against magic at a soul deep level and suffer breaking points. <br /> <br /> 2. Paradox, the universe (abyss) hates you. Deal with it. Maybe not hate but the Abyss is a fact and it's in EVERY sleeper soul. And it will strike back directly given any possible avenue.<br /> <br /> 3. DIssonance, certain things you do if they are fantastical will not last under sleeper scrutiny unless you're either not obvious or pay the cost for the reach that's required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 11-27-2015, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T20:08:46-08:00","id":775194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775180#post775180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 1. Good work showing to us the main &quot;genetic power&quot; for the bigger templates. Thanks<br /> 2. The comparison is unfair because the Vampire and Werewolf have serious &quot;genetic flaws&quot; (Silver/Lunacy/Fire/Sun/Beast/Rotschreck, need to drink blood, etc) when mages are normal people that can do some magic. If mages dont have the same number of advantages is because they dont have a relevant number of disadvantages like the &quot;monster of night&quot;.<br /> Paradox is a mage flaw, but it dont hurt much. C'mon, it works more like a setting device to explain why mages dont abuse of obvious magic in crowd and why they hide magic from normal people/sleepers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except going by the list of innate powers, even subtracting the negatives, even with the addition of those 3 dots things are still looking relatively even. So what about the additional dots is overpowered?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 11-26-2015, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T20:48:11-08:00","id":775218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775163#post775163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Easy to house rule, but dont make sense a Wod with so many overgpower mage walking together with creatures of night without a open war scenario.<br /> Changin</div> </div> </div> </div>Purely speculation not backed up by anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T00:02:06-08:00","id":775298,"title":"","content":"You know, I run a LARP with 30 mages and my friends run LARPs with 30 vampires, 20 werewolves and 35 Changelings. They are part of the same shared chronicle. So far after years of playing, there has never been an open war between the supernaturales (except for one time where a warmonger tried to create one, but it was solved after a few months). Do they still have conflicts? Yes. Do they have good motives to go to war? Not at all. Mages are quite busy with their stuff to bother about what vampires are doing. Werewolves have issues with two or three mages and don't care about the rest.<br /> <br /> I am not speaking from any theorethical possition about how the game plays, I do this every month. Of course, right now we are mostly using 1e rules (Except I have started adding obsessions into the mix, which seem to work fine so far). I am eager to see what 2e brings that I can start to use.<br /> <br /> So far, this experience has shown me that 6 arcana dots work perfectly with a cap at 3 dots for the start. I have done a few games where people start at 4 dots in an Arcana and they are fine too. I have even done a few Archmaster sessions. There are some players that do really hubristic things with their magic and abuse their powers. There are others that are really careful and avoid hubris. Each type of game has its highs and lows. As long as you and your players are on the same understanding of how to play the game, the kind of story you want and all that fine stuff, the actual amount of dots you have is not a problem.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T02:59:51-08:00","id":775348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. The comparison is unfair because the Vampire and Werewolf have serious &quot;genetic flaws&quot; (Silver/Lunacy/Fire/Sun/Beast/Rotschreck, need to drink blood, etc) when mages are normal people that can do some magic. If mages dont have the same number of advantages is because they dont have a relevant number of disadvantages like the &quot;monster of night&quot;.<br /> Paradox is a mage flaw, but it dont hurt much. C'mon, it works more like a setting device to explain why mages dont abuse of obvious magic in crowd and why they hide magic from normal people/sleepers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must note that I'm aware of the in-built drawbacks of the splats and was about to mention it in my post, but it seemed big enough as it was.<br /> <br /> That said, if you analize it you will see that it follows the same logic. Both Werewolves and Vampires have in-built abilities that are not dependant on any purchase or investment of xp on part of the player, so they also get weaknesses that are in-built and independent of those powers. Mages get most if not all of their oomph from purchased powers and so their primary weakness is also tied to those purchased powers.<br /> <br /> Also, some of the &quot;disadvantages&quot; of Vampires and Werewolves are more like double-edged swords. Both Frenzy and Death Rage provide significant advantages in the shape of increased resistance to mental manipulation (for both of them) and powerful boost to physical pools (for vampires) or free use and automatic activation of several powers (for werewolves).<br /> <br /> Silver (for werewolves) and Fire and Sunlight (for vampires) being extra-damaging is balanced against the fact that most other forms of damage are quite ineficient. Add on top of that the quick healing makes recovery easier. On the other hand mages are just as vulnerable as any regular human, and heals as slow as one without asist of magic or a great investment of their fuel trait.<br /> <br /> Note also, that Blood Sorcery is almost as flexible as mage Arcana at less investment, having only 5 discrete powers versus the 10 a mage have to spread on, and that you could get 3 dots of them on top of 2 dots of regular Disciplines at character creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":".  adding more thorough explanations about weaknesses of the splats 11-27-2015, 06:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T04:05:53-08:00","id":775371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775163#post775163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair, but not everyone need to have the same opinion. The developers need to build the game for everyone that whant to use the creatures of night in their games. This is one of the selling points from nWod, dont expect a 100% balanced crossover system, but giving more dots of &quot;power&quot; to the overpower Arcanum dont make sense to a World that live creatures of night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im not saying is the right move but neither the dev and most of the fanbase want balance. The idea that in order for mage to do the &quot;consequence of power&quot; tired trope mages need to be the most OP thing in the setting is crutch that the game happily uses. I even read arguments along the lines of &quot;mage is not a game about surpassing obstacles because they should be able to remove them without problem&quot; while i think that make the game more &quot;God: The awakening&quot; more than mage, is clear that is not gonna change.<br /> <br /> Mages (at least in 1st) can play in everyones sandboxes and do it better. They can do spirit better than werewolves, dreams better than changeling, and i dont care about requiem enough to check if they do social manipulation better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775348#post775348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver (for werewolves) and Fire and Sunlight (for vampires) being extra-damaging is balanced against the fact that most other forms of damage are quite ineficient. Add on top of that the quick healing makes recovery easier. On the other hand mages are just as vulnerable as any regular human, and heals as slow as one without asist of magic or a great investment of their fuel trait.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that mage have spells running on them 24/7. So they are as vulnerable as any human......with a effects running 24/7. Do mages exist that dont put on their shield on their morning rituals? Sure.......like vampires who walk the street juggling molotovs, they might exist but they arent the norm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775187#post775187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox doesn't hurt? Get serious and know what you're talking about. You do know that mages have a choice concerning paradox? Either contain it as unhealable bashing damage while grounding it into your pattern, which takes time to fully expel with conditions beyond the bashing damage you take Or you can release it which guarantees everyone else gets screwed, while your spell goes off fine and then gets twisted for the worst against you but after the fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dm 2 year long campaigns and play in another and paradox was never a threat. An inconvenience at best and i played &quot;thunder every problem away&quot; mage and ate all the paradox as bashing which was at most 3. I have had some obvious players (fuck the veil mages) and subtle ones. In first at least it never had any teeth.<br /> <br /> Going back to the OP of what one likes/dislikes. I dont quite like adamant hand as it is now, i preffer when it was set up as an martial art with different level and abilities.<br /> <br /> On the other hand i love the &quot;Fast Spells&quot; merit<br /> <br /> I love the idea of merit that allow different mages and that is not a merit exclusive of the adamantine arrow. I would like to see more of those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-27-2015, 07:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T05:10:35-08:00","id":775394,"title":"","content":"In order for mage to have &quot;Consequences of Power&quot; and &quot;Temptation of Power&quot; as tropes, you actually need to be short on power so you are tempted to...Reach. Which is why I think that my preferred model of play will be low (3 and less) Arcanas while utilizing tons of Reach options. Which is great, because in case of some Arcanas (looking at you, Death and Spirit) you needed like 3 to get anything useful, and then at 4 you suddenly became super powerful, outstripping other Arcanas in power due to flexibility of these high powered options. <br /> I love the fact that in 2nd Ed, Forces 2 mage will be really powerful as long as he is willing to utilize Reach on his spells and use stuff like...I don't know...lighter and taser.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T05:21:35-08:00","id":775398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775371#post775371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that mage have spells running on them 24/7. So they are as vulnerable as any human......with a effects running 24/7. Do mages exist that dont put on their shield on their morning rituals? Sure.......like vampires who walk the street juggling molotovs, they might exist but they arent the norm.</div> </div> </div> </div>eeeeeeeeexcept 2e Mage Armour isn't a spell any more, but is instead activated for a scene for a point of mana; you <i>can't</i> run it 24/7. Yeah, that was a bit of a flaw with the &quot;mages are pretty much baseline mortals if they don't have time to prepare&quot; theme, so 2e is fixing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T05:38:00-08:00","id":775408,"title":"","content":"People like to load up their characters with spells up to their limit, but I personally prefer to emphasize the fact that if you do so, you look like a Christmas Tree to anyone looking for paranormal...things, which in turn may actually jeopardize your safety (by making you easy to spot, find and target). Still, it's a style preference, and I certainly don't like the logical result of 1E system where you should ritual cast your defensive spells (not only Armor Spells, but stuff like &quot;I cast prolonged Control Water on this water and give it 10 extra durability, and then make it cover my body to form water armor with durability of 10&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T07:12:26-08:00","id":775438,"title":"","content":"Mages are incapable of defending against everything at once, so who cares if they waste resources on specific defenses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T07:26:13-08:00","id":775447,"title":"","content":"Mages are also limited on the number of active effects they can have running at the same time unless they want to take the risk of them going out of control or make a significant investment. A Gnosis 1 starting mage can have a whooping 1 spell runing at the same time, while a Blood Potency 1 vampire or Primal Urge 1 Werewolf can, virtually, have an indefinite number of efects on them at a given time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T07:26:26-08:00","id":775448,"title":"","content":"About werewolves, don't forget that 2 dots they spend for Shadow facets, which is, approximately, 3-dot Abilities (or abilities with big potential, like Element gift). Anyway, while w won't see the new Arcanas, we don't know, which benefits 2.0 mages actually have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T07:32:11-08:00","id":775453,"title":"","content":"To be fair, currently or in 1st edition, paradox doesn't really matter. I've run a couple year-long mage campaigns and... it only really came up when players went waaaaay overboard, as in casting 5+ vulgar spells in the same scene overboard. It's only at that point that the number of successes on paradox rolls become non-trivial to just take as bashing damage. So saying paradox is a real limitation is incorrect IMO, in 1st edition. It sounds like Paradox gets more teeth in 2nd, so I am looking forward to that.<br /> <br /> As for balance between splats... I can't really see how to do it without fundementally altering the way arcana works. Werewolf, vampire, etc powers are specific, mage powers are broad. Once a mage hits 3 or maybe 4 in an arcana, they just outstrip everyone else. It doesn't matter if you have Celerity 6, when I can use Spirit 2 to get spirits to spy on you, find your name and a piece of cloth, then use Space 4 to teleport you to the moon using a sliver of rock from the moon landing. All from the comfort of my home. <br /> <br /> If I ever had some guy wanting to play a vampire in a mage game, I'd throw something like 20 exp at him for starters (2nd ed rules). I mean, c'mon, this is white wolf games we are talking about, it wouldn't be white wolf if the authors actually understood how their rules worked. 2nd edition seems to be changing that, but still, don't expect miracles.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2206-suicide-king","name":"Suicide King","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T07:37:06-08:00","id":775459,"title":"","content":"I'd like to add that I, too, have run very long Mage campaigns (one is in its... Third year at this point?) and played in another in its second, and can honestly say that Paradox never had any real bite. In fact, in the game I ran, my players only had one Paradox in the entire playtime.<br /> <br /> With 2e, Paradox is much more of a choice and has much more bite, adding dice as quickly as it does. I've been kind of muddling with 1.5e rules and even in that limited form - using spells far more powerful than they likely are in the book - it's had a noticeable effect on decision-making already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T08:30:44-08:00","id":775484,"title":"","content":"My fix for Paradox in 1e was basically make it lethal. Problem solved.<br /> <br /> That said, I really really like Paradox more from what we have seen in 2e.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I didn't do it when I was starting as a ST, but later I started including drawbacks of lugging around active defenses all the time. The biggest and most interesting one is that other mages can detect you automatically when approaching from a 200 yard distance. A pretty significant drawback. On some scenes this meant that enemies know they were coming and where able to escape in time, prepare a quick ambush or put defenses up themselves. Other times this was used to track their routes and find their Sanctum (who they had hidden at the time).<br /> <br /> Thus, players had to be more discerning on when it was a good time to have defenses up and when not to.<br /> <br /> I am also glad that 2e fixed this anyways, I like the 2e method better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T08:34:19-08:00","id":775487,"title":"","content":"That's not even a house rule Arthexis, active supernatural abilities (Including spells) automatically ping Unseen Senses unless they're designed to foil that particular Mage ability. It wasn't clearly stated, but it was implied, glad to see someone's doing it right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T09:09:34-08:00","id":775502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775394#post775394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In order for mage to have &quot;Consequences of Power&quot; and &quot;Temptation of Power&quot; as tropes, you actually need to be short on power so you are tempted to...Reach. Which is why I think that my preferred model of play will be low (3 and less) Arcanas while utilizing tons of Reach options. Which is great, because in case of some Arcanas (looking at you, Death and Spirit) you needed like 3 to get anything useful, and then at 4 you suddenly became super powerful, outstripping other Arcanas in power due to flexibility of these high powered options.<br /> I love the fact that in 2nd Ed, Forces 2 mage will be really powerful as long as he is willing to utilize Reach on his spells and use stuff like...I don't know...lighter and taser.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.....so much this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775398#post775398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">eeeeeeeeexcept 2e Mage Armour isn't a spell any more, but is instead activated for a scene for a point of mana; you <i>can't</i> run it 24/7. Yeah, that was a bit of a flaw with the &quot;mages are pretty much baseline mortals if they don't have time to prepare&quot; theme, so 2e is fixing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did we got a preview on how mage armor is gonna be yet? I remember the dev saying thats was one of the option on the table but they were still working on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775438#post775438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages are incapable of defending against everything at once, so who cares if they waste resources on specific defenses?</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that against other supernaturals mostly the ones you need are shield against physical threats and agaisnt mental threats. The rest are mostly shields against other mages.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775447#post775447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages are also limited on the number of active effects they can have running at the same time unless they want to take the risk of them going out of control or make a significant investment. A Gnosis 1 starting mage can have a whooping 1 spell runing at the same time, while a Blood Potency 1 vampire or Primal Urge 1 Werewolf can, virtually, have an indefinite number of efects on them at a given time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which preview is that one? Because in 1st edition the limit was 3+gnosis so a gnosis 1 character could have 4 spells running. I houserule it to only gnosis but i didnt knew that was rule coming in 2nd, neat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775484#post775484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly, I didn't do it when I was starting as a ST, but later I started including drawbacks of lugging around active defenses all the time. The biggest and most interesting one is that other mages can detect you automatically when approaching from a 200 yard distance. A pretty significant drawback. On some scenes this meant that enemies know they were coming and where able to escape in time, prepare a quick ambush or put defenses up themselves. Other times this was used to track their routes and find their Sanctum (who they had hidden at the time).<br /> <br /> Thus, players had to be more discerning on when it was a good time to have defenses up and when not to.<br /> <br /> I am also glad that 2e fixed this anyways, I like the 2e method better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Curiously enough in another disconnect between fluff and mechanics in 1st there was a fluff piece in, i think, tome of mysteries about a mage doing the daily perma-shield and how stressful it was for him to do so, how going around the street with a magic shield was distracting and not something he do everyday.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T09:30:00-08:00","id":775515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775502#post775502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This.....so much this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Did we got a preview on how mage armor is gonna be yet? I remember the dev saying thats was one of the option on the table but they were still working on it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Except that against other supernaturals mostly the ones you need are shield against physical threats and agaisnt mental threats. The rest are mostly shields against other mages.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Which preview is that one? Because in 1st edition the limit was 3+gnosis so a gnosis 1 character could have 4 spells running. I houserule it to only gnosis but i didnt knew that was rule coming in 2nd, neat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Curiously enough in another disconnect between fluff and mechanics in 1st there was a fluff piece in, i think, tome of mysteries about a mage doing the daily perma-shield and how stressful it was for him to do so, how going around the street with a magic shield was distracting and not something he do everyday.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've been told they'll vary depending on which arcana you're using. I recall the examples we've been given being Time and Death. Time modified your (actually, I think it was your opponents) initiative in some way, while death gave you damage type downgrades like the undead.<br /> <br /> And yes, Spell limit is now equal to Gnosis, and anything cast above that costs an additoinal Reach.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T10:35:58-08:00","id":775540,"title":"","content":"I'm excited for new Mage Armors because they started as differently flavored armor effects, but now look like they are about making you harder to kill and making you little more monstrous and inhuman. Death Armor sounds fantastic, for example.<br /> Other thing I want to read is how unleashing spells (so you don't have to sustain them anymore), especially permanent ones, works now. I hated how prohibitive it was in1st ED, due to Willpower costs. But now, as recovering Willpower costs always one flat Experience, it almost seems too easy; it's kinda like buying a one dot merit. I wonder how it's balanced, because I kinda love idea of your mage slowly adding ongoing effects on themselves and becoming less and less normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T14:53:55-08:00","id":775638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775502#post775502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which preview is that one? Because in 1st edition the limit was 3+gnosis so a gnosis 1 character could have 4 spells running. I houserule it to only gnosis but i didnt knew that was rule coming in 2nd, neat.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the post (from Paradox preview), I think:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200b<img src=\"http://1.gravatar.com/avatar/a8a797c590bb3e7d5435dd21faedad7a?s=60&amp;d=identicon&amp;r=pg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Eolirin<br /> August 23, 2014 at 5:11 am<br /> <br /> I *think* he means active spell slots. You start increasing paradox when you go over them, right? Just straight Gnosis now, too? </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <img src=\"http://0.gravatar.com/avatar/6ee2a8748016f9b2902256eb8e571f5d?s=60&amp;d=identicon&amp;r=pg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Dave Brookshaw<br /> August 23, 2014 at 7:34 am<br /> <br /> Yeah \u2013 <u><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">it\u2019s just straight Gnosis, and every spell over it requires a Reach</span></b></u>. So, if you\u2019re gnosis 2 your third spell needs a Reach, your fourth spell needs two Reach and so on. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","user":"Sp4rt01","date":". 11-27-2015, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T15:40:42-08:00","id":775667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775540#post775540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm excited for new Mage Armors because they started as differently flavored armor effects, but now look like they are about making you harder to kill and making you little more monstrous and inhuman. Death Armor sounds fantastic, for example.<br /> Other thing I want to read is how unleashing spells (so you don't have to sustain them anymore), especially permanent ones, works now. I hated how prohibitive it was in1st ED, due to Willpower costs. But now, as recovering Willpower costs always one flat Experience, it almost seems too easy; it's kinda like buying a one dot merit. I wonder how it's balanced, because I kinda love idea of your mage slowly adding ongoing effects on themselves and becoming less and less normal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are a few methods for relinquishing a spell that we know of in 2e. 1) Spend a WP point, but if there's a lot of duration left then the spell will eventually go haywire. 2) Spend a WP dot, the duration doesn't matter it will continue to function. I bet it can be dispelled though. 3) Relinquish the spell to a Sleepwalker. Technically in this case the spell isn't relinquished at all, the Mage just offloads his personal control of it. <br /> <br /> Speculating, but you could probably get a supernatural entity to pay the WP dot cost for relinquishing a spell as part of a Pact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T17:06:18-08:00","id":775697,"title":"","content":"Spending a Willpower Dot to get permanent, let's say, Attribute Boosting spell relinquished still seems like a really, really good choice. BTW, I hated how powerful Attribute and Skill boosting spells of Mind were; I hope they got somehow nerfed (and skill increasing spell flat out removed from the game). <br /> Still, it's interesting to see that after you become capable of making some of your spell permanent, you can experiment with becoming posthuman mage shedding away his imperfections. <br /> These effects being dispellable is fine. Due to how Clash of Wills works against super-long effects, you probably won't lose them &quot;accidentally&quot; to a random Dispel. And Dispelling some Quality-of-Life spells (both minor and major - &quot;Animated Shadows are making up for my shattered spine, so I can walk normally&quot; and &quot;I can browse internet in my head&quot; fit here) can lead into interesting scenes where character is violently reminded how normal life looks like and how far she became removed from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T17:33:52-08:00","id":775704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775447#post775447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages are also limited on the number of active effects they can have running at the same time <u><b>unless they want to take the risk of them going out of control or make a significant investment.</b></u> A Gnosis 1 starting mage can have a whooping 1 spell runing at the same time, while a Blood Potency 1 vampire or Primal Urge 1 Werewolf can, virtually, have an indefinite number of efects on them at a given time.</div> </div> </div> </div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>A <b>starting Char can begin with 3 dots of Gnosis</b> (extremely recommended because magic dicepool);</li> <li>You can also<b> use mana to remove dice of paradox</b> and is absurdly easy to get mana even without Prime. C'mon, a char with a legacy can get a number of Mana per day equal to the Primary Arcanum of the legacy with only Oblations and withtout the use of a Hollow or Prime Arcanum (dont forget pattern scourging too)<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. It's so easy to get mana, this can be a problem because Paradox can become irrelevant again. Plus, a starting char can begin with a legacy with 2 dot of Gnosis now (but he need to pay some XP for the attainments, I think).</li> <li>We're talking about character creation, with that in mind I really cannot see how a 3 dot discipline/gift character can have this &quot;indefinite number of effects&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. <b>That <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">HYPERBOLE </span>is a flamebait, right </b>?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T17:47:04-08:00","id":775706,"title":"","content":"We don't know if Mana replenishment is as easy in 2nd Edition as it was in 1st ED (for example, I don't think that Artifacts are still going to be mana batteries), and there is probably a ton of things to spend mana on now, instead of &quot;pretty much nothing&quot; from before. Attainments, spells, Paradox, Mage Sight...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T18:52:36-08:00","id":775728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775704#post775704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>A <b>starting Char can begin with 3 dots of Gnosis</b> (extremely recommended because magic dicepool);</li> <li>You can also<b> use mana to remove dice of paradox</b> and is absurdly easy to get mana even without Prime. C'mon, a char with a legacy can get a number of Mana per day equal to the Primary Arcanum of the legacy with only Oblations and withtout the use of a Hollow or Prime Arcanum (dont forget pattern scourging too)<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. It's so easy to get mana, this can be a problem because Paradox can become irrelevant again. Plus, a starting char can begin with a legacy with 2 dot of Gnosis now (but he need to pay some XP for the attainments, I think).</li> <li>We're talking about character creation, with that in mind I really cannot see how a 3 dot discipline/gift character can have this &quot;indefinite number of effects&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. <b>That <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">HYPERBOLE </span>is a flamebait, right </b>?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>1. At the cost of <i>all</i> of their merit points. Raising your power stat in 2e costs 5 merit points per increase. That is a significant investment.<br /> <br /> 2. So a few points of mana per day, whoo, you're rolling in mana now. It also now costs mana per additional non-ruling arcana application to your Mage Sight, and Mage Armor costs a point of mana for every additional scene you have it active past the first. That isn't even including spell costs, be it for specific spell requirements or use of non-rote, non-ruling magic.<br /> <br /> 3. Infinite possibilities isn't what Vampires and Werewolves are about, so who cares if they're applicable magic is more focused or not? Working as intended. The additional 3 dots (assuming the unknown factors work like in 1e) will only net you 1 or 2 dots in your common arcana. That gives you access to Compelling, Knowing, Unveiling, Ruling, Shielding, and Veiling effects. Most of those are devoted purely to gathering and concealing information, which is literally a mages bread and butter. It is exactly what they are supposed to excel at over all others (supernaturals of not).<br /> <br /> The others give rudimentary control over the things that fall into the arcanums purview, including the ability to shield yourself from some of it's effects. This is important because in 2e mages aren't inherently immune to the effects of their own spells. If you create a fireball without first giving yourself protection from fire you're going to incinerate your own hand.<br /> <br /> So long story short, all the additional 3 dots give is a wider breath of possibilities in doing the very thing mages are <i>designed</i> to do. It really feels like you aren't really caught up on the spoilers given about mage 2e and that you're working with less information than everybody else. I recall someone making a thread compiling the spoilers given up to a certain point (I'm not sure how well maintained it is currently), you may want to go give it a read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 11-28-2015, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T19:02:06-08:00","id":775732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775704#post775704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>A <b>starting Char can begin with 3 dots of Gnosis</b> (extremely recommended because magic dicepool);</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>According to Dave, it's such a bad idea that he considered not allowing it in 2e.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/765599-i-m-reading-tome-of-watchtowers?p=770251#post770251\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...251#post770251</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/765599-i-m-reading-tome-of-watchtowers?p=770251#post770251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, like in VtR and WtF 2nd ed, five Merit dots per dot of Gnosis. I really would't recommend it in Mage, to the point that I nearly took the option out altogether.<br /> <br /> You'll be <i>crippled</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T20:57:26-08:00","id":775775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775704#post775704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>A <b>starting Char can begin with 3 dots of Gnosis</b> (extremely recommended because magic dicepool);</li> <li>You can also<b> use mana to remove dice of paradox</b> and is absurdly easy to get mana even without Prime. C'mon, a char with a legacy can get a number of Mana per day equal to the Primary Arcanum of the legacy with only Oblations and withtout the use of a Hollow or Prime Arcanum (dont forget pattern scourging too)<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. It's so easy to get mana, this can be a problem because Paradox can become irrelevant again. Plus, a starting char can begin with a legacy with 2 dot of Gnosis now (but he need to pay some XP for the attainments, I think).</li> <li>We're talking about character creation, with that in mind I really cannot see how a 3 dot discipline/gift character can have this &quot;indefinite number of effects&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. <b>That <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">HYPERBOLE </span>is a flamebait, right </b>?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>Completely, especially given we have no clue how oblation works now. <br /> <br /> By the way what's wrong with being able to get mana without some ridiculous crap you as as ST seem to love? Especially since your main reason to spend mana is to use attainments not spells now. It's quite enough that a mage can't really go full out like any other supernatural without serious planning and/or serious cost. <br /> <br /> So just do what I would do to end around your plan of making me a peon for your entertainment and just get Prime and make you work a bit by erasing the zero out of the hero from the start. You get into a legacy or create one for damn good reason you know.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 11-28-2015, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T06:44:51-08:00","id":775949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775704#post775704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>A <b>starting Char can begin with 3 dots of Gnosis</b> (extremely recommended because magic dicepool);</li> <li>You can also<b> use mana to remove dice of paradox</b> and is absurdly easy to get mana even without Prime. C'mon, a char with a legacy can get a number of Mana per day equal to the Primary Arcanum of the legacy with only Oblations and withtout the use of a Hollow or Prime Arcanum (dont forget pattern scourging too)<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. It's so easy to get mana, this can be a problem because Paradox can become irrelevant again. Plus, a starting char can begin with a legacy with 2 dot of Gnosis now (but he need to pay some XP for the attainments, I think).</li> <li>We're talking about character creation, with that in mind I really cannot see how a 3 dot discipline/gift character can have this &quot;indefinite number of effects&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. <b>That <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">HYPERBOLE </span>is a flamebait, right </b>?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>1) No Merits whatsoever as others pointed out. Is a trade off, as everything else, you will also have Paradox pile up faster wich ties in with...<br /> <br /> 2)... this. Not that absurdly easy to do as you think as odds are you won't have a Legacy as a starting character, but let's asume you do. Mana has a lot of uses now, so will have to decide where you want to spend it. If you boost your Gnosis you won't have a Hallow and also your Paradox pool will be 2 dice per Reach above your limit. Yeah, you could have 3 spells running without problem at the same time,but each aditional one are another two dice on your pool, for every spell you cast. It will quickly pile up. Do you really think you will have such amount of Mana to spare to be paying 2+ points everytime you want to do the simplest of magics?<br /> <br /> 3) Simply pointing out there's no actual cap. Also, at least in werewolf there's a lot of Facets that boost your packmates, so you can have some from each on top of yours. Also those red caps are only slightly aleviated by the joking smiley. I don't do flamebait, nor like being implied to. Don't be that guy, ok? We are all friends here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T07:39:16-08:00","id":775988,"title":"","content":"The reason in don't like improving Gnosis using starting merit points is that it makes for a &quot;blank&quot; character, someone who feels like a &quot;statistical human being&quot;, it just feels unnatural. Merits let you customize your character and make him feel unique, striping that off feels like ruining the players experience to achieve some goal (optimization comes to mind) that's not rly important in a storytelling game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T07:43:31-08:00","id":775994,"title":"","content":"So play that angle up, make it part of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T08:09:15-08:00","id":776019,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying you can't but I just don't like it and feels somewhat boring to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T19:30:09-08:00","id":776372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775949#post775949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that absurdly easy to do as you think as odds are you won't have a Legacy as a starting character, but let's asume you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember correctly, Legacy Attainments (and the other mechanical benefits of Legacy membership) will cost Experiences in 2ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T19:56:21-08:00","id":776382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775988#post775988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason in don't like improving Gnosis using starting merit points is that it makes for a &amp;quot;blank&amp;quot; character, someone who feels like a &amp;quot;statistical human being&amp;quot;, it just feels unnatural. Merits let you customize your character and make him feel unique, striping that off feels like ruining the players experience to achieve some goal (optimization comes to mind) that's not rly important in a storytelling game.</div> </div> </div> </div>At 5 merit per gnosis? No thanks, I'd rather just start at the bottom like some dumb ass virgin if my ST insisted on 0 experience characters. Merits are too awesome to give up for something easy as pie to raise in actual play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T02:29:29-08:00","id":776493,"title":"","content":"Talking about Merits - I used Arcane Experience before 2nd Edition became a thing, and limited my players purchases to &quot;magical stuff only with AExp, Gnosis rises up automatically at critical points of the story, normal Experience can be used to purchase merits skills and attributes as usual&quot;. I really like that Arcane Experience is given more spotlight in this edition, and while I don't think it's going to be as restrictive as my personal rules on Exp, I still like the direction they go for. <br /> As for merits vs gnosis - due to how it seems that Merits apparently can provide you with reliable and powerful yantras (even +3 ones), it isn't actually inferior to Gnosis now, as long as you cover your bases. Gnosis 3 will give you better ritual casting times (which, due to ability to instant cast anything as long as your Reach, isn't that game changing anymore; your Gnosis 1 mage in 1ED had to waste whole day casting his max Arcana spells, now he doesn't have to wait for Arcana 4 to reliably cast his Arc 3 spells!), 2 extra mana per turn, one extra yantra and +2 to general casting (plus other benefits that remain to be seen). Ritual Casting also doesn't seem to be that much of a deal anymore, because I *think* it's now flat Ritual Casting Time, not Ritual Casting Time * Number of Rolls, which is imho a godsend. <br /> So, your Gnosis 3 starting mage will have +2 dice and +1 yantra edge on your Merits one. However, if you grab some good yantra (let's say you managed to get one of the +3 yantras) with your Merit points, actual casting difference will vanish. Why?<br /> Gnosis 3 person has natural +2 edge; as long as you can get a yantra that is at least equal to +2, you are fine. In instant casting, you usually want to frontload your spell with big, reflexive yantra in order to not waste your rounds adding extra yantras; which also, accidentaly, makes that extra 3rd yantra less relevant. Getting yantra stronger than +1 seems kinda hard - +2 yantras usually demand some kind of sacrifice, be it resources or opportunity, and &quot;free to be taken&quot; +3 yantras seem to be rare and &quot;quest objective&quot; kind of thing. In non combat situation, your Merit Wizard can utilize her 2 yantras with &quot;My Personal +3 Yantra&quot; and High Speech for nice, +5 bonus. Gnosis 3 Wizard can probably manage +2, +1, +1, or +2 +2 +1. Which gives him a slight edge, but not that much actually. <br /> Of course, a lot of this depends on exact rules on pricing yantras. Still, abililty to get that buff to your casting with merits means that you don't *need* that extra gnosis desperately, as it's effect on gameplay seem to be less warping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T07:55:50-08:00","id":776584,"title":"","content":"I like how the orders are getting more of the spotlight than the consilium. 1es consilium had too much politics involved, whereas 2e is more about magic itself. I also really like that Space is getting fixed.<br /> <br /> One thing I greatly dislike is the dumbing down of metamagic. In 1e, you could count on a spell to likely be scene long, cast instantly ( not reflexively), and that it could reach your target presuming you could see/hear/smell him. On top of that, so long as you had one more dot in the arcanum than the spell, by at least one interpretation you could increase all the spell's aspects (but not each aspect to its maximum). That was a HUGE selling point of Mage for me. Now you get neither since there's only one natural reach per dot (for lower dots) and all spells are naturally &quot;ritual cast&quot; (absolute worst part of 2e since the point of ritual casting was that it was for your most powerful spells; normal magic is for here and now. BOOM! Done. Just like that.), touch range, and lasts just per turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T09:22:39-08:00","id":776626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775394#post775394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In order for mage to have <b>&quot;Consequences of Power&quot; and &quot;Temptation of Power&quot; as tropes, you actually need to be short on power so you are tempted to...Reach</b>. Which is why I think that my preferred model of play will be <b>low (3 and less) Arcanas while utilizing tons of Reach options</b>. Which is great, because in case of some Arcanas (looking at you, <b>Death and Spirit) you needed like 3 to get anything useful, and then at 4 you suddenly became super powerful</b>, outstripping other Arcanas in power due to <b>flexibility of these high powered options</b>.<br /> I love the fact that in 2nd Ed, Forces 2 mage will be <b>really powerful as long as he is willing to utilize Reach</b> on his spells and use stuff like...I don't know...lighter and taser.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same opinion here.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> &quot;More Power, more Paradox&quot;, but we need change the damage of paradox to lethal.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> About Death/Spirit ArcanaI I think that DaveB will put some Reach to limit the abuse of &quot;summon ephemera&quot;, but dont know how it will work. The real problem is that some ST dont give the consequence of summoning a Alien being to summoners that deal with spirits as &quot;machines that sell magic&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T09:56:05-08:00","id":776647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=776584#post776584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like how the orders are getting more of the spotlight than the consilium. 1es consilium had too much politics involved, whereas 2e is more about magic itself. I also really like that Space is getting fixed.<br /> <br /> One thing I greatly dislike is the dumbing down of metamagic. In 1e, you could count on a spell to likely be scene long, cast instantly ( not reflexively), and that it could reach your target presuming you could see/hear/smell him. On top of that, so long as you had one more dot in the arcanum than the spell, by at least one interpretation you could increase all the spell's aspects (but not each aspect to its maximum). That was a HUGE selling point of Mage for me. Now you get neither since there's only one natural reach per dot (for lower dots) and all spells are naturally &quot;ritual cast&quot; (absolute worst part of 2e since the point of ritual casting was that it was for your most powerful spells; normal magic is for here and now. BOOM! Done. Just like that.), touch range, and lasts just per turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know where you're getting dumbing down from; it's been massively expanded <i>and</i> clarified. 1e's creative thaumaturgy was an absolute mess, with spells seeming to almost arbitrarily use different guidelines on what could use what when; some spells staggered their duration (Scrying, for example) and others didn't; some automatically started with Advanced Duration; some started ranged automatically and others at touched. It was a tangled mess.<br /> <br /> What 2e does is streamline it; all spells start at the same baseline, with the same basic conditions, and you can raise it from there with Reach. In most instances, a Mage is actually going to be <i>better off</i> than they were in 1e. For example, a Thyrsus with Life 3 casting a spell to improve their Strength in 1e faced automatic Paradox for doing so, and a random result. In 2e, that same Mage can cast the spell for a concentration duration (the one turn thing is one turn <i>after</i> you stop concentrating, if you use concentration duration, unless I missed my mark) to allow them to do some basic heavy lifting and risks no Paradox. If they wish to make it scene length, they can risk Paradox for it. In either case, they know exactly what they're getting for the risk, whereas the 1e Thyrsus did not. Likewise, if they wished to, the 2e Thyrsus can cast it at range immediately from Life 3, provided they're willing to allocate the Reach.<br /> <br /> At Life 4, the 2e Thyrsus can now cast a Strength-enhancing spell on themselves for a scene-length duration for no Paradox risk. The 1e Thyrsus can now cast it at range, but still risks Paradox no matter what.<br /> <br /> I would say, based on this, that the 2e Thyrsus has the much better time of it, since the new system allows for a far greater diversity in focusing of casting purpose, a deliberate management of risk instead of making it random, and an allowance for players to be clever instead of every spell being just the same.<br /> <br /> Ritual casting in 2e allows you a bit more Reach <i>and</i> has some Paradox-blunting aspect that Dave hasn't actually elaborated on - we'll find out when the book comes out, I imagine - meaning that it's <i>still</i> more powerful than regular casting. When you're casting your biggest, most powerful spells, you'll still want to be casting ritually.<br /> <br /> Remember, <i>paradox-free Reach</i> is not the same thing as Reach itself; you can ostensibly take as much of the latter as you want for the spell. It's just that any over your limit risks Paradox. This means that Mages in 2e actually are less likely to inflict Paradox but are also far more versatile in their ability to cast; being able to choose what form the spell takes with far more acuity and, hence, understand and mange (and be responsible for) the risks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T10:37:31-08:00","id":776675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=776647#post776647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know where you're getting dumbing down from; it's been massively expanded <i>and</i> clarified. 1e's creative thaumaturgy was an absolute mess, with spells seeming to almost arbitrarily use different guidelines on what could use what when; some spells staggered their duration (Scrying, for example) and others didn't; some automatically started with Advanced Duration; some started ranged automatically and others at touched. It was a tangled mess.<br /> <br /> What 2e does is streamline it; all spells start at the same baseline, with the same basic conditions, and you can raise it from there with Reach. In most instances, a Mage is actually going to be <i>better off</i> than they were in 1e. For example, a Thyrsus with Life 3 casting a spell to improve their Strength in 1e faced automatic Paradox for doing so, and a random result. In 2e, that same Mage can cast the spell for a concentration duration (the one turn thing is one turn <i>after</i> you stop concentrating, if you use concentration duration, unless I missed my mark) to allow them to do some basic heavy lifting and risks no Paradox. If they wish to make it scene length, they can risk Paradox for it. In either case, they know exactly what they're getting for the risk, whereas the 1e Thyrsus did not. Likewise, if they wished to, the 2e Thyrsus can cast it at range immediately from Life 3, provided they're willing to allocate the Reach.<br /> <br /> At Life 4, the 2e Thyrsus can now cast a Strength-enhancing spell on themselves for a scene-length duration for no Paradox risk. The 1e Thyrsus can now cast it at range, but still risks Paradox no matter what.<br /> <br /> I would say, based on this, that the 2e Thyrsus has the much better time of it, since the new system allows for a far greater diversity in focusing of casting purpose, a deliberate management of risk instead of making it random, and an allowance for players to be clever instead of every spell being just the same.<br /> <br /> Ritual casting in 2e allows you a bit more Reach <i>and</i> has some Paradox-blunting aspect that Dave hasn't actually elaborated on - we'll find out when the book comes out, I imagine - meaning that it's <i>still</i> more powerful than regular casting. When you're casting your biggest, most powerful spells, you'll still want to be casting ritually.<br /> <br /> Remember, <i>paradox-free Reach</i> is not the same thing as Reach itself; you can ostensibly take as much of the latter as you want for the spell. It's just that any over your limit risks Paradox. This means that Mages in 2e actually are less likely to inflict Paradox but are also far more versatile in their ability to cast; being able to choose what form the spell takes with far more acuity and, hence, understand and mange (and be responsible for) the risks.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, by at least one interpretation (and implied by several spell descriptions) you could improve ALL aspects of a spell by having one more dot in an arcanum. In 2e, having one more dot gives you one extra reach, not three+ (range, duration, casting time, number of targets/area size). <br /> <br /> Paradox free reach is nice, but not when you could reliably expect your previous spells to be cast instantly, reach your target without having to grapple or touch them/it, amd last a whole scene. Now you have to either risk paradox or cast spells 2 dots lower than your max to do that. <br /> <br /> Of course paradox and the abyss was the part of the game I hated second most (yes hate, not dislike), right after the existence of the exarchs, so I guess I'm slightly biased. \ud83d\ude09 (Yeah, I was one of those weirdos that would find a way to remove paradox and the abyss from my chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T12:31:16-08:00","id":776739,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, beyond taking reach, a player can take dice penalties like 1e for access to even more spell factors and given you only need a single success. I'd imagine a mage would find ways to load up on yantras, and use rotes for the extra reach, and have 5-10 praxis for the easier exceptional success possibility. Beyond the fact that a dicepool of 3 shouldn't put you at too much risk versus success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T12:43:54-08:00","id":776746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=776675#post776675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1e, by at least one interpretation (and implied by several spell descriptions) you could improve ALL aspects of a spell by having one more dot in an arcanum. In 2e, having one more dot gives you one extra reach, not three+ (range, duration, casting time, number of targets/area size).<br /> <br /> Paradox free reach is nice, but not when you could reliably expect your previous spells to be cast instantly, reach your target without having to grapple or touch them/it, amd last a whole scene. Now you have to either risk paradox or cast spells 2 dots lower than your max to do that.<br /> <br /> Of course paradox and the abyss was the part of the game I hated second most (yes hate, not dislike), right after the existence of the exarchs, so I guess I'm slightly biased. \ud83d\ude09 (Yeah, I was one of those weirdos that would find a way to remove paradox and the abyss from my chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, 1e was a mess. Attack spells, for example, could only be cast at touch range with the dot allowed for it, then you could cast ranged with one higher, then sympathetic with one higher. Others, you could cast range from the first dot you had.<br /> <br /> That said, though, with 2e, you can access advanced factors from the very first point that spell of yours is able to be cast. It might risk Paradox, but that happened anyway in 1e, since any spells of 3 dots or more were usually vulgar, and it's far easier to mitigate with a dedicated tool in 2e than it was in 1e (not to mention how Praxes and Yantras also make it easier, when combined, for Mana use as well). In other words, you get access to versatility <i>sooner</i> in 2e than 1e. Yeah, the number of Paradox-free Reach is relatively small, but it's still exceptionally larger than in 1e, where that number was zero.<br /> <br /> You're actually complaining about a feature that lets you do what you wanted more.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T13:04:11-08:00","id":776760,"title":"","content":"Don't get me wrong, there are benefits to reach that are cool. But when spell aspects all get set back, that free reach just gets you back something you already had. I suppose some spells get more benefit by putting more reach into the same aspect, but if you want your baseline aspects returned to &quot;normal&quot; on your highest dot, then you have to risk paradox twice. Pros and cons. I suppose sometimes I'm a glass half empty guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T13:26:22-08:00","id":776768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=776739#post776739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, beyond taking reach, a player can take dice penalties like 1e for access to even more spell factors and given you only need a single success. I'd imagine a mage would find ways to load up on yantras, and use rotes for the extra reach, and have 5-10 praxis for the easier exceptional success possibility. Beyond the fact that a dicepool of 3 shouldn't put you at too much risk versus success.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Loading-up on Yantras is not so easy since the number of Yantras used is limited by Gnosis, and most only provide a +1 or +2 dice bonus..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/a-lever-and-a-firm-place-to-stand/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/a-lever-and-a-firm-place-to-stand/\" target=\"_blank\"> A lever and a firm place to stand &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/a-lever-and-a-firm-place-to-stand/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/a-lever-and-a-firm-place-to-stand/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (DAVE\u2019S NOTE \u2013 Breaking into the section for a moment, the number of Yantras you can use are:<br /> Gnosis Yantras<br /> 1 or 2 2<br /> 3 or 4 3<br /> 5 or 6 4<br /> 7 or 8 5<br /> 9 or 10 6) </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T15:01:32-08:00","id":776828,"title":"","content":"So far the only thing I can think of that I dislike in 2e is the fact that the new Reach system only determines whether or not a spell risks Paradox if there aren't Sleeper witnesses. When Sleepers are around, you risk Paradox for casting something &quot;obviously magical&quot;, which sounds like there's going to be a lot of arguing with the ST in 2e over whether or not your spell effect was coincidental. Hopefully there are guidelines in the book somewhere about what the game considers &quot;obviously magical&quot;?<br /> <br /> I also have serious trepidations about how difficult and punishing it apparently is to raise Wisdom in 2e. I don't like the idea of PCs having to hamstring their own development in order to redeem themselves Wisdom-wise, and ending up worse off than people who never dropped Wisdom in the first place, and people who dropped Wisdom and just didn't care. It's hard enough to justify spending XP on buying back a resource you can lose through gameplay as it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=775704#post775704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>A <b>starting Char can begin with 3 dots of Gnosis</b> (extremely recommended because magic dicepool)</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>Dave has stated (I don't remember where at this point, it might have even been this forum) that trading in starting merit dots for Gnosis in 2e is going to be so crippling to your character that he seriously considered not including the option to do so at all.<br /> <br /> I guess Mage 2e is going to have a lot of good Mage merits, which is something I look forward to. I like encouraging players to spend their XP on Merits and the like, while reserving Arcana and Gnosis increases for Arcane XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","user":"Juhn","date":". 11-29-2015, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T16:22:20-08:00","id":776869,"title":"","content":"Ah, mage merits. I'm glad they are taking a closer look at that because there was huge potential there that they missed in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T17:07:32-08:00","id":776891,"title":"","content":"I hope the &quot;obviously magical&quot; aspect works like this: if something you did using Magic causes a sleeper to roll for a breaking point, the spell has a very large abyssal sympathy generated from the invocation of the Curse required to apply the Quiescence on the Sleeper. If that happens, you always roll +1 Paradox (tier?) and apply a dice trick. Imagine it more like an Quiescence tax of sorts that a Mage must pay whenever it needs to be enforced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T17:31:38-08:00","id":776903,"title":"","content":"It's far simpler than that. Obvious is like doing the gun kata thing like Equilibrium or Ultraviolet. While the Bic Lighter of Doom isn't. <br /> <br /> Then your numbers come in, 1-2 sleepers? Likely just a paradox die. More then that or a crowd? Here come the dice tricks on top.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T18:18:24-08:00","id":776913,"title":"","content":"BTW, was there a rule change about accumulating Paradox? As in - I cast two spells. First one potentially provoked Paradox, and second one is also Paradox provoking. Is that second spell at +1 Paradox dice for each &quot;vulgar&quot; (Paradox-provoking) spell cast in this scene?<br /> Because I GMed a short 2 session game with whatever spoilers were available and included this rule, and boy Paradox looks innocent at first but it can escalate <i>fast</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T18:41:39-08:00","id":776924,"title":"","content":"+1 die per vulgar spell you cast in the same scene was a rule in 1e, yes. +1 die per vulgar spell that <i>anyone</i> casts in the same scene was a suggested rules hack in at least one book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T18:44:08-08:00","id":776925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=776913#post776913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, was there a rule change about accumulating Paradox? As in - I cast two spells. First one potentially provoked Paradox, and second one is also Paradox provoking. Is that second spell at +1 Paradox dice for each &amp;quot;vulgar&amp;quot; (Paradox-provoking) spell cast in this scene?<br /> Because I GMed a short 2 session game with whatever spoilers were available and included this rule, and boy Paradox looks innocent at first but it can escalate <i>fast</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you ran it correctly. Each vulgar spell you cast during a scene adds a die to your existing base paradox pool.<br /> <br /> For example say a mage has gnosis 3 and she cast 2 vulgar spells in the same scene previously and now is doing her third. ...her base pool would start at 5 dice without any sleepers around to add dice tricks on top. <br /> <br /> Unless she's in a demense, verge, or in the Astral or Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T19:52:05-08:00","id":776955,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but I'm asking if is there anything to suggest that this rule will be still in play in 2nd Edition or not <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> mostly because while in 1st Ed my players were were careful about Paradox and pretty much never invoked it, now there is at least one or two spells with paradox pool on it. This turns mage fights *very* hectic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T20:19:00-08:00","id":776965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=776955#post776955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but I'm asking if is there anything to suggest that this rule will be still in play in 2nd Edition or not <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> mostly because while in 1st Ed my players were were careful about Paradox and pretty much never invoked it, now there is at least one or two spells with paradox pool on it. This turns mage fights *very* hectic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is confirmed in the spoiled example of complete spellcasting at <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?591295-Mage-the-Awakening-The-Man-Comes-Around&amp;p=19183548#post19183548\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...8#post19183548</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daveb</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Now the downsides. This is going to </span></span><i>hurt</i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">, Paradox-wise. One Reach for instant casting, one for sensory range, one for Advanced Duration, three to activate </span></span><i>both</i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> of the spell's Reach clauses... That's a whopping eight Paradox dice (2 each for 4 Reach over the limit). <b>Plus one for this being Cowl's second Paradox roll of the scene.</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:blue\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Dave underlines the &quot;it isn't obvious *when cast*&quot; note in his playtest file</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">. Reduce that by 2 for using the coin again, and it's still seven dice. That could knock Cowl unconcious or leave him with a nasty Paradox Condition (or, if he chooses to not contain it, potentially summon a Gulmoth. Yeah, he doesn't even think about that).</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T01:30:55-08:00","id":777052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=776955#post776955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but I'm asking if is there anything to suggest that this rule will be still in play in 2nd Edition or not <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> mostly because while in 1st Ed my players were were careful about Paradox and pretty much never invoked it, now there is at least one or two spells with paradox pool on it. This turns mage fights *very* hectic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure in 2e when you add Paradox dice you always do so by the amount that your Gnosis generates (Except in the case of Sleeper witnesses which adds 1 die and then dice tricks), so if you have Gnosis 3 and you risked Paradox on a spell before and your next spell also risks Paradox because you're one over your safe Reach then you add +2 Paradox dice to the pool for both those instances for a total of 4 Paradox dice. Paradox dice add up really quickly, but it's also been mentioned that the curve will be flatter as a result, Gnosis 10 probably won't generate 5 Paradox dice at a time the way it does in 1e. It also provides a high demand for mana on top of being used to activate attainments and charge up Mage Sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T13:01:43-08:00","id":777873,"title":"","content":"The only thing that I really didn't like is the way that Supernal magic affects Integrity. I have no problem with the insta-kill spells that Masters of certain Arcana can use in 2ED. My problem is how Hunters would (at least theoretically) have little recourse against an enemy whose abilities constantly wear down their souls and can't even be remembered. You can houserule that taking up the Vigil also makes you a Sleepwalker, of course, but Hunters would still have to deal with constant Breaking Points. I normally don't say this because far too many people use the term willy-nilly, but all of this makes mages sound a bit Mary Sue-ish. Sure, there's the Abyssal Shard, and hubris goes hand in hand with great power and the following sensation of invincibility. I don't want to nerf mages, no way. I just think the playing field could be less uneven. Hopelly this will be taken into account during the development of Hunter 2ED.<br /> <br /> On a more positive note, it's nice to have a thread like this with people giving their feedback civilly. Mage 2ED may be in the final stages of development, but it's still good to see constructive criticism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-01-2015, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T13:27:13-08:00","id":777889,"title":"","content":"There isn't any concern about balance between game lines. If you're playing Hunter use its built in witches. If you're playing Mage expect Hunters who aren't Banishers to be screwed. There's nothing to complain about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T13:46:35-08:00","id":777901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=777873#post777873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that I really didn't like is the way that Supernal magic affects Integrity. I have no problem with the insta-kill spells that Masters of certain Arcana can use in 2ED. My problem is how Hunters would (at least theoretically) have little recourse against an enemy whose abilities constantly wear down their souls and can't even be remembered. You can houserule that taking up the Vigil also makes you a Sleepwalker, of course, but Hunters would still have to deal with constant Breaking Points. I normally don't say this because far too many people use the term willy-nilly, but all of this makes mages sound a bit Mary Sue-ish. Sure, there's the Abyssal Shard, and hubris goes hand in hand with great power and the following sensation of invincibility. I don't want to nerf mages, no way. I just think the playing field could be less uneven. Hopelly this will be taken into account during the development of Hunter 2ED.<br /> <br /> On a more positive note, it's nice to have a thread like this with people giving their feedback civilly. Mage 2ED may be in the final stages of development, but it's still good to see constructive criticism.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be noted that hunter 2ed isnt out yet, if it ever goes out so we dont know yet how they will be their take on intergrity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=777889#post777889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't any concern about balance between game lines. If you're playing Hunter use its built in witches. If you're playing Mage expect Hunters who aren't Banishers to be screwed. There's nothing to complain about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes there is things to complain about. That mages are the only things that threaten mages (as far a hunters go) doesnt sound mary sue-ish, it IS mary sue-ish. And the witch hunter (non-banisher) is a valid antagonist in both the core and some order books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 12-01-2015, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T13:56:29-08:00","id":777904,"title":"","content":"The Hunter vs. Mage argument has been thoroughly discussed, including ample comments by Dave about the Quiescence issue.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...nters-vs-mages</a><br /> <br /> Hunter are also certainly quite capable of hunting mages, it's just extremely difficult (as are all major splats), and helps explain why Hunter includes three distinct power tiers (at least in 1e), the highest of which are generally immune to the Quiescence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 12-01-2015, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T15:21:06-08:00","id":777936,"title":"","content":"LRS: Life is unfair, get used to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T15:37:11-08:00","id":777944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=777936#post777936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">LRS: Life is unfair, get used to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dont be the guy who ruins this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=777873#post777873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On a more positive note, it's nice to have a thread like this with people giving their feedback civilly. Mage 2ED may be in the final stages of development, but it's still good to see constructive criticism.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T17:26:49-08:00","id":777983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=777944#post777944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dont be the guy who ruins this</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, then when you use a term, use the proper definition. Mary Sue: <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">a young or low-rank person who saves the day through extraordinary abilities. Often but not necessarily this character is recognized as an </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Self-insertion\" target=\"_blank\">author insert</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> and/or wish-fulfillment.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T18:30:27-08:00","id":778017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=777983#post777983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, then when you use a term, use the proper definition. Mary Sue: <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">a young or low-rank person who saves the day through extraordinary abilities. Often but not necessarily this character is recognized as an </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Self-insertion\" target=\"_blank\">author insert</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> and/or wish-fulfillment.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> except i was using the term with the intent of the person i quoted<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=777873#post777873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. I normally don't say this because far too many people use the term willy-nilly, but all of this makes mages sound a bit <b><u>Mary Sue-ish</u></b>. Sure, there's the Abyssal Shard, and hubris goes hand in hand with great power and the following sensation of invincibility. I don't want to nerf mages, no way. I just think the playing field could be less uneven. Hopelly this will be taken into account during the development of Hunter 2ED.</div> </div> </div> </div>but applied to mage, author insertion aside the term also conveys a character that is good at everything with no disserning flaws. And to an extend that is mages, they do spirits better than werewolf, pledges and dreams better than changeling and maybe mental powers better than vampires (i dont care much for requiem, to buy the book and check).<br /> <br /> While the fluff and other splats talks the worry about hunters and most say things along the lines of &quot;while mortal are inferior on one on one be aware of their organization/ingenuity&quot; mage kinda shrugs and says &quot;Not mages! they get their special hunters because only mages can kill mages&quot; the core puts the hunters as antagonist same with some of the orders book but in plays most people would tell you to just use the banishers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T19:07:20-08:00","id":778032,"title":"","content":"You only need one Sleepwalker to make a Hunter cell a viable threat to a Mage.<br /> <br /> Dave has said that there are spirit things that werewolves do better than Mage, things that in fact Mages cannot do. I don't know what those things might be, but I'm willing to take his word for it.<br /> <br /> Mages obviously have flaws or there wouldn't be an interesting game. Part of their flaws is that they screw up Sleepers who witness their magic. It's not the goal of the game to be mean to Hunters, but to be true to its own premise. If that steps on the toes of Hunter, a separate game line, so be it, they don't need to cater to each other. So much so that Hunter goes out of its way to give you tools to build new monsters instead of forcing you to dig through the other major game lines. That's Hunter saying screw Mage right there, and vampires and werewolves and whatever, and that is absolutely fine.<br /> <br /> It's a stupid complaint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-01-2015, 10:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T19:22:04-08:00","id":778037,"title":"","content":"It gets even stupider when you realize that the Orders regularly employ Sleepers who could turn into very well informed Hunters at any moment. They may not remember the magic, but they sure as hell will remember who to whack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T19:31:03-08:00","id":778040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778032#post778032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You only need one Sleepwalker to make a Hunter cell a viable threat to a Mage.<br /> <br /> Dave has said that there are spirit things that werewolves do better than Mage, things that in fact Mages cannot do. I don't know what those things might be, but I'm willing to take his word for it.<br /> <br /> Mages obviously have flaws or there wouldn't be an interesting game. Part of their flaws is that they screw up Sleepers who witness their magic. It's not the goal of the game to be mean to Hunters, but to be true to its own premise. If that steps on the toes of Hunter, a separate game line, so be it, they don't need to cater to each other. So much so that Hunter goes out of its way to give you tools to build new monsters instead of forcing you to dig through the other major game lines. That's Hunter saying screw Mage right there, and vampires and werewolves and whatever, and that is absolutely fine.<br /> <br /> It's a stupid complaint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, that im not saying on using mage in hunter but to use hunter in mage. While i highly doubt that NWoD 1.0 wasnt meant for crossover initially with its whole unifying designs (axis of 5 for everyone, moralities for everyone, etc) im not arguing about using mages in hunter but how hunters cannot be a proper antagonist only by stretching probabilities.<br /> <br /> And as the OP is asking what we dont like about 2ed, im gonna add i dont like they are keeping Quiescence. I think it exist for 2 things, one is for justifying to the more detail oriented fans as to how the &quot;veil&quot; is maintain and secondly as a whole &quot;sleepers and mages live in different worlds&quot;. While i understand the reasoning i feel its heavy handed in its implementation. The veil thing should be more of an optional rules of sorts for those who need less details on the veil and as for the whole humanity separated etc i think magic is enough for that and the whole forgetfulness is a way to kill stories and possible antagonists. Its not needed.<br /> <br /> As for what mages cannot do than werewolf can, i guess we should wait to see what 2ed mage has to offer because as to right now 1st mage can do spirits better than werewolves but honestly as the power creep of the other lines goes i dont think they will nerf mages but i could be wrong.<br /> <br /> And honestly, its not a stupid complain to want fluff to match the mechanics, if you feel the opinion of other somehow diminish your own when in disagreement to the point that you feel that dismissive remarks are the answer then the problem is yours.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778037#post778037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It gets even stupider when you realize that the Orders regularly employ Sleepers who could turn into very well informed Hunters at any moment. They may not remember the magic, but they sure as hell will remember who to whack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming for a moment that those people whom the order has sympathetic connection can leave the order......a very big IF. Without knowledge of the magic how can you prepare for whacking said mage? See for hunters their danger lays in preparations and planning which are things cannot be done if the hunter cannot remember what he needs to prepare for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 12-01-2015, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T20:55:00-08:00","id":778091,"title":"","content":"With respect to all the major splats, not just mages, recall that the various books state that <i>humanity</i> collectively is a threat, but individual humans, not so much.<br /> <br /> Moreover, as has already been noted, many Hunters can effectively hunt mages without suffering from the Quiescence, and most are Tier 3. Your complaint is essentially that normal humans without any inherent powers aren't a serious threat to people who control reality with their will alone. I don't know why this would be surprising, and that's before the Quiescence and the primary themes of alienation from humanity and effects of the unwise use of power factors into the Mage setting.<br /> <br /> Mage without Quiescence or the equivalent wouldn't be a tweak to the setting, it would be a totally different game. As long as certain Hunters are actually mortal humans, they will be affected just like everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T21:05:38-08:00","id":778094,"title":"","content":"Hence they don't hunt mages unless they happen to be a sleepwalker usually. Which isn't a ridiculous assumption.<br /> <br /> What's to say Hunters can't employ a sleepwalker in similar functions that mages do by the way? You could have a sleepwalker being your eyes for your Hunter cell. It is awkward but doable. Think Criminal Minds or NCIS. <br /> <br /> That's why Banishers take that spot. To fight fire it's pretty useful to actually see said fire correct? Or we get Hunter the Imbued again. I hate that game and obviously I wasn't the only one that wasn't buying it without actually thinking the premise was ridiculous.<br /> <br /> For your information only mages with major dots in Spirit come close to what any Uratha does concerning spirits (they have gifts/facets beyond any mage that hasn't achieved archmastery) while actually knowing the rules to make it worse, unlike most mages beyond Dreamspeakers and associated legacies at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 12-02-2015, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T23:49:27-08:00","id":778142,"title":"","content":"I am sustained by the tears of Hunter fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":26}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T00:19:50-08:00","id":778155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778142#post778142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am sustained by the tears of Hunter fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do the tears of Hunter fans taste any differently than than tears of other people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T00:32:00-08:00","id":778162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778155#post778155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the tears of Hunter fans taste any differently than than tears of other people?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe they are particularly salty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T03:33:12-08:00","id":778225,"title":"","content":"If somebody can deduce or recall that a person is an actual mage, even if they never properly remember the magic, to be a member of one of the damn Orders, I'd say they can do it well enough to attempt randomly unloading a gun into the mage going about their business in the street, or better yet sniping them from a relatively long distance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T03:36:51-08:00","id":778227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778091#post778091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With respect to all the major splats, not just mages, recall that the various books state that <i>humanity</i> collectively is a threat, but individual humans, not so much.<br /> <br /> Moreover, as has already been noted, many Hunters can effectively hunt mages without suffering from the Quiescence, and most are Tier 3. Your complaint is essentially that normal humans without any inherent powers aren't a serious threat to people who control reality with their will alone. I don't know why this would be surprising, and that's before the Quiescence and the primary themes of alienation from humanity and effects of the unwise use of power factors into the Mage setting.<br /> <br /> Mage without Quiescence or the equivalent wouldn't be a tweak to the setting, it would be a totally different game. As long as certain Hunters are actually mortal humans, they will be affected just like everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, quiescence wouldn't change the setting as much. The alienation angle can be made perfectly without it. A good example would be for example a mastigo, if any close relative or significant person would learn that said character can control minds then that reframe their entire life. How does human cope with the doubt that what they feel is artificial or not? That seems a more toolbox approach to it than the heavy handed quiessence because it also allows for <br /> <br /> As for hunters, in first edition i would complain that the resistance rolls for everything on humans are 1 sided. There are 3 stats vs 1 (attribute + skill + arcanum vs resolve) instead or a more even if still favoring the supernatural contested roll off (attribute + skill + arcanum vs willpower). However, as the new magic roll is 2 stat with a bunch of modifiers (yantras) vs something we dont know yet, im hopeful. And if not it can be houserule away.<br /> <br /> As for quiessence, problem isn't that bob the clerk cannot go toe to toe with a mage but that while fluff talks about hunter as a threat they arent. <br /> <br /> Its the same problem with lunacy when things like this are rules then the options are either to DM fiat or stretch veliability. So any human who remember is either WP 7+, so the story of mortal or the DM has to say &quot;yeah i know the rules says WP 7 can only remember.....but he does&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T03:40:55-08:00","id":778230,"title":"","content":"Normal Human Hunters are a danger to Mages anyway, because they don't ping first and most basic defence of mages - their spider sense Magical Sight. Dude with a sniper rifle looking at you when you go back home from magical adventures? Unless you have very specific magic active, you won't see the bullet coming. You may activate your Mage Armor reflexively, sure, but without specific Arcana, what can you really do other than running away? Same thing with getting your food poisoned, home bombed, etc - not every mage has every single Arcana at their desposal, and while sure, most of them probably can solve any problem you throw at them, not all of them can <i>detect</i> these problems easily. And often, all you need is to delay the &quot;oh uh&quot; moment.<br /> Mages are so obsessed with supernatural that they are often blind to non magical threats. Spirit trying to put your house on fire using it's powers will ping your mage sight. Arsonist won't. Magical explosion spell will ping your sight. Bomb won't. Sabotaged car won't. Sure, if you attack mage directly and don't alpha strike them, they will unmake you. But that's pretty much your fault, isn't it? It's like inviting a Vigor spamming, Celerity glowing Vampire to a fair duel in the middle of night, or trying to grapple Werewolf to death. Aren't hunters all about tactics? Not all tactics are viable. Use ones that are. This is the whole point of being a tactician.<br /> Munduane things are blind spot of mages. Use it. Stay out of sight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I disagree, quiescence wouldn't change the setting as much. The alienation angle can be made perfectly without it. A good example would be for example a mastigo, if any close relative or significant person would learn that said character can control minds then that reframe their entire life. How does human cope with the doubt that what they feel is artificial or not? That seems a more toolbox approach to it than the heavy handed quiessence because it also allows for </div> </div> </div>You are missing the most basic, traumatizing realization of being mage with family - that your husband, your daughter, and your mother NEVER will be able to see all the wonderful things you are seeing, never will be able to see your magic, and being your new yourself [casting magic] will actually soulhurt them. It's like obtaining most wonderful thing in the world, but never being able to share it with people you care about. Your lives and worlds grow apart. It's terrible experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 12-02-2015, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T06:10:14-08:00","id":778280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778230#post778230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are missing the most basic, traumatizing realization of being mage with family - that your husband, your daughter, and your mother NEVER will be able to see all the wonderful things you are seeing, never will be able to see your magic, and being your new yourself [casting magic] will actually soulhurt them. It's like obtaining most wonderful thing in the world, but never being able to share it with people you care about. Your lives and worlds grow apart. It's terrible experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you also missing the other side of the coin. I once had a talk with a close friend whom she told me how she was scared of her father because everytime they had a discussion he would take his gun and put it on the table, this was in the 70s and in a country where this was legal. He never used, he never threaten noone with it he didnt even raise it but every single discussion with him was tainted with that gun. Bringing magic to ones family is that gun, times 10. There is, imo, no need to some methaphysical mechanic to souls and what not about why is alienating to be a mage.<br /> <br /> Still the game is done, and even this thread is more about what we like/dislike about the game. My only hope is that quiessence is like in 1st edition, easy to remove without to much complication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T06:10:29-08:00","id":778281,"title":"","content":"Plus, Sleepers can learn about the abilities of Mages even if they never remember actually seeing it. Again, Sleepersvwork for the Orders, they're not doing it for free. They know -something- about what Mages can do despite the fact they've never seen it first hand. It's perfectly possible to prepare for a fight against a Mage even if you don't know everything they can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T06:22:33-08:00","id":778287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778281#post778281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, Sleepers can learn about the abilities of Mages even if they never remember actually seeing it. Again, Sleepersvwork for the Orders, they're not doing it for free. They know -something- about what Mages can do despite the fact they've never seen it first hand. It's perfectly possible to prepare for a fight against a Mage even if you don't know everything they can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. You don't have to be able to see something for yourself to know about it. You don't need to see a guy shoot fire out of his hands to be able to figure out he was responsible for the recent series of strange house fires that have claimed half a dozen lives within the last 2 months. While being able to see these things surely makes it <i>easier,</i> this isn't about making it easy for Hunters. It simply isn't the point. But while it isn't easy, it is more than possible, and as long as you're aware that said person is the target, that person is just as easy to hunt as any other target. Hell, probably easier assuming you don't show your hand too early.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T06:36:20-08:00","id":778293,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that it <i>might </i>be possible to show sleepers magic without getting hit with paradox or dissonance. <br /> <br /> Ok, so out of sight you conjure some sort of object with magic. Maybe by making a bit of tass, doesn't really matter. Then you show the sleeper the object, and then cancel the spell. The object vanishes. Ta da!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T07:29:15-08:00","id":778309,"title":"","content":"Get Apocalypse as an Attainment - one Mana for free, so you would activate Sight for three Arcana at no price + one Mana for ALL the remaining Sights. Attainment is a normal part of reality, so Abyss can't do shit and there is nothing to forget. Any spell detected would register only as a change in what you already see - spells are manipulations of reality against it's normal state, but world *is* ultimately made of magic, of Mana, so if seeing that world with Apocalypse doesn't provoke Abyss, nothing happening during watching it will.<br /> <br /> <br /> ... You hear that? That's <i>every</i> Ministry sending Ochemata after you. Good luck! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> This would incidentally make a good Hieromagus. Isn't he/she supposed to destroy Quiescence with their very presence?<br /> <br /> But enough of that, this Legacy would be quite powerful. It needs some setbacks - how about getting it's first Attainment requires you to never have caused or risked Paradox and you won't be able to overreach, with every Sleeper witnessing your casting while not under Apocalypse making your spell to not go off at all...?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> P.S.: I've actually created a Hieromagus Legacy, the initiation, how you get Attainments, attitude to the world, everything. I'm just waiting for 2e to come out to finish off some uncertainities.<br /> <br /> It's funny how this would show, that the biggest reason for Mages complaining about everything bad with the world, would be that none of them had the spine to be consistent enough in their beliefs and not dip into the metaphysical well of all contradiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 12-02-2015, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T07:48:24-08:00","id":778314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778309#post778309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Get Apocalypse as an Attainment - one Mana for free, so you would activate Sight for three Arcana at no price + one Mana for ALL the remaining Sights. Attainment is a normal part of reality, so Abyss can't do shit and there is nothing to forget. Any spell detected would register only as a change in what you already see - spells are manipulations of reality against it's normal state, but world *is* ultimately made of magic, of Mana, so if seeing that world with Apocalypse doesn't provoke Abyss, nothing happening during watching it will.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think apocalypse would cause Integrity checks for most sleepers, even as an Attainment. Not because of the Abyss, but because sleepers cannot process the new sensory information. The spell is not called apocalypse for nothing. But still, the sleeper would not necessarily forget.<br /> <br /> We should not forget that contact with the supernatural is often a breaking point in and off itself, even when the Abyss or Supernal is not involved, and that mortals in the World of Darkness tend to rationalize suppernatural occurances away, even without Quiessence.<br /> <br /> By the way, I am not trying to trivialize the impact of Quiessence or trying to defend it. I just wanted to make clear that Quiessence is very close to a phenomenon that at least in second edition, affects all mortal-supernatural interactions. Although I guess that most people who don't like Quiessence also could do without this effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T07:54:43-08:00","id":778320,"title":"","content":"Yeah, a True Hieromagus would understand the responsibility and not just activate Apocalypse in the middle of Times Square. The Sleeper would have to be in the know and a part (however small) of an Order, and be of high Integrity. Wisdom break is luckily out of window in 2e as well, where Attainments are concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T11:36:44-08:00","id":778488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778293#post778293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurs to me that it <i>might </i>be possible to show sleepers magic without getting hit with paradox or dissonance.<br /> <br /> Ok, so out of sight you conjure some sort of object with magic. Maybe by making a bit of tass, doesn't really matter. Then you show the sleeper the object, and then cancel the spell. The object vanishes. Ta da!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Quiescence is different from paradox and dissonance.<br /> <br /> Quiescence always causes a breaking point in normal humans (anyone without a supernatural or Sleepwalker merit) whenever they witness magic AND forces them to totally forget about it or rationalize the event as non-magical (no roll to resist). Dissonance is a related effect where the presence of sleepers breaks down spells over time.<br /> <br /> The importance of Quiescence is that a mage can <i>never </i>really share his magic with friends or loved ones because it injures them on a soul deep level and they will not even remember.<br /> <br /> Note that the Veil is not a choice by mages to protect them from humanity, but a means for mages to protect sleepers. Mages' alienation from humanity is set by an absolute rule, the Quiescence, and its elimination would indeed significantly change the setting. Creating some &quot;exception&quot; for the sole crossover reason of sleeper Hunters having an easier chance of hunting mages is contrary to one of the most important aspects of the mage setting. It's also completely unnecessary as not only can sleeper Hunters still hunt mages, albeit with a great deal of difficulty, virtually every Tier 3 Hunter is already immune to the Quiescence because they have an inherent supernatural ability and the Sleepwalker Merit is a measly one dot choice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778227#post778227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for quiessence, problem isn't that bob the clerk cannot go toe to toe with a mage but that while fluff talks about hunter as a threat they arent.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The fluff of all the major splat books discuss <i>humanity collectively</i> as a threat to supernaturals, not individual humans. <br /> <br /> There's a reason why Tier 3 Hunters exist, and why the monsters in the Hunter books are decidedly less dangerous and powerful than the other actual gameline splats, mages and otherwise.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T11:41:32-08:00","id":778492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778142#post778142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am sustained by the tears of Hunter fans.</div> </div> </div> </div> cartman pls leave<br /> <br /> Seriously, though. I have some ideas of my own for making Hunters vs Mages confrontations less uneven. I felt I should do something if the official rules don't support what I want, instead of just complaining. I ain't gonna foam at the mouth because someone on the Internet disagrees with me. To each his own. I actually agree that a non-Hunter Sleeper stands virtually no chance against any decently skilled and prepared Mage. I have this homebrewed Merit tied to the Conviction Powerstat from Mirrors that gives you a fairly high chance at surviving an Unmaking spell. I might add a drawback for repeated use within a short time span on top of the willpower cost. I won't make every Hunter a Sleepwalker just for taking up the Vigil, but I will try to come up with more ways to acquire Supernatural Merits. I like the sound of trying to piece together the evidence from conflicting memories after a fight with a Mage. But even with Sleepwalker status, high Resistance Attributes, multiple Merits for improving said Attributes and tons of willpower points, Mages can still use Unraveling spells with 1 Reach + 1 Mana to deal aggravated damage without the target Withstanding. And that's without going into Scrying, Mage Armor, mind reading, teleportation, divination, regeneration, and so on. I am ok with limiting Mage antagonists to Tier 3 Hunters for the most part, especially in 2ED. In my games, Mages will usually have the upper hand, but they will still have plenty of reasons to fear Hunters. Neither side will curb stomp the other all the time, which will force both of them to stay on their toes and keep their eyes open. The themes of each game will remain intact, to boot. That sounds fair to me.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to say this isn't the end of the world, even if Hunter 2ED pretty much agrees with DaveB.<br /> <br /> Peace, everyone. Best of luck to all the STs who want to change what doesn't work for their game group. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-02-2015, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T11:56:55-08:00","id":778500,"title":"","content":"It's nice that even your own game agrees with DaveB. As others have said including myself not all sleepwalkers have to work for the Pentacle/Seers or even mages. And tier 3 Hunters exist for damn good reason. This isn't Witchcraft and the quiescence is there to make it so.<br /> <br /> What's stopping a regular Hunter cell from running into a tier 3 Hunter? My guess would be nothing but the ST as usual. <br /> <br /> But instead most ST's have an irresistible itch to fix what works just fine without houserules for a problem that doesn't exist outside their own mind. Because they are fixated on mythical game balance and can't accept life isn't fair. Like real life some supernaturals are better then others at things and some antagonist groups aren't equipped to deal with certain supernatural groups. End of story, full stop.<br /> <br /> Hence you employ people that can actually see what said group does and devise some tactics. Aren't Hunters all about tactics? Don't tactics encompass everything including the kitchen sink? Remember life isn't fair and it works both ways between antagonist/protagonist. Just remember that the antagonist can be just as tactical as any Hunter in many cases especially if they're mages because like Hunters they are fully human also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 12-02-2015, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T12:11:21-08:00","id":778507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778488#post778488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fluff of all the major splat books discuss <i>humanity collectively</i> as a threat to supernaturals, not individual humans.<br /> <br /> There's a reason why Tier 3 Hunters exist, and why the monsters in the Hunter books are decidedly less dangerous and powerful than the other actual gameline splats, mages and otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really many fluff pieces both talk about example of a group of hunter doing this or that agaisnt mages which is kinda sad because all that read is that the people who writes the fluff resides in another plane of existence from the people who writes the rules. I really wish i could use hunters as antagonist per raw.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778230#post778230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Normal Human Hunters are a danger to Mages anyway, because they don't ping first and most basic defence of mages - their spider sense Magical Sight. Dude with a sniper rifle looking at you when you go back home from magical adventures? Unless you have very specific magic active, you won't see the bullet coming. You may activate your Mage Armor reflexively, sure, but without specific Arcana, what can you really do other than running away? Same thing with getting your food poisoned, home bombed, etc - not every mage has every single Arcana at their desposal, and while sure, most of them probably can solve any problem you throw at them, not all of them can <i>detect</i> these problems easily. And often, all you need is to delay the &quot;oh uh&quot; moment.<br /> Mages are so obsessed with supernatural that they are often blind to non magical threats. Spirit trying to put your house on fire using it's powers will ping your mage sight. Arsonist won't. Magical explosion spell will ping your sight. Bomb won't. Sabotaged car won't. Sure, if you attack mage directly and don't alpha strike them, they will unmake you. But that's pretty much your fault, isn't it? It's like inviting a Vigor spamming, Celerity glowing Vampire to a fair duel in the middle of night, or trying to grapple Werewolf to death. Aren't hunters all about tactics? Not all tactics are viable. Use ones that are. This is the whole point of being a tactician.<br /> Munduane things are blind spot of mages. Use it. Stay out of sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem with this is how does the hunter knows that he has to attack the mage with a sniper? Or poison his food? I think you guys are putting way too little importance in seeing. The example of the sleeper guy who work for the order but somehow is allowed to let go, didnt witness magic but knows mage A set fire to lots of places. What possible way has he of knowing he must use a sniper/car bomb to attack him? If the mortal could remember then it becomes easier to justify this. He follow the mage around got a feel for what he does with magic and then says &quot;yeah im gonna be better off sniping this guy&quot;<br /> <br /> Otherwise is contrive. &quot;Oh, he just use this weird methods of killing you that you dont have an arcana to counter&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778230#post778230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that the Veil is not a choice by mages to protect them from humanity, but a means for mages to protect sleepers. Mages' alienation from humanity is set by an absolute rule, the Quiescence, and its elimination would indeed significantly change the setting. Creating some &quot;exception&quot; for the sole crossover reason of sleeper Hunters having an easier chance of hunting mages is contrary to one of the most important aspects of the mage setting. It's also completely unnecessary as not only can sleeper Hunters still hunt mages, albeit with a great deal of difficulty, virtually every Tier 3 Hunter is already immune to the Quiescence because they have an inherent supernatural ability and the Sleepwalker Merit is a measly one dot choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all not everyone wants to use Taskforce valkyrie/cherion. If a theme of mage that its fans likes to clutch as it safety blanket against many criticism about unecesary power high level is the abuse of power then the story of a mortal abused by a mage and that biting him in the ass with mundane means is proper with the theme.<br /> <br /> Secondly Quiescence is not as vital to the setting, Ascension ran a &quot;similar&quot; feel and it didn't had some methapysical thing that erase people's memories. Without Quiescence one can run the same story that one runs with it + more types. With Quiescence one is limited to 1 story, the same old brooding &quot;oh woe me, i must be forever apart from humanity *play angel theme son* &quot;.<br /> <br /> So if without Quiescence one can run the whole &quot;separation of humanity&quot; theme or do more stories. And with Quiescence you can run only that one, then it isnt better really. Instead of just letting the option open they put this big NO sign in the form of rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":".  Missing a piece 12-02-2015, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T12:15:10-08:00","id":778509,"title":"","content":"(psst. Valkyrie's magical armamts don't count as an internal power - they're Sleepers, not Sleepwalkers!)<br /> <br /> And &quot;safety blanket?&quot; Real nice backhandedly calling the game childsh. My days of not taking these complaints seriously are certainly coming to a middle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T12:22:48-08:00","id":778514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778507#post778507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really many fluff pieces both talk about example of a group of hunter doing this or that agaisnt mages which is kinda sad because all that read is that the people who writes the fluff resides in another plane of existence from the people who writes the rules. I really wish i could use hunters as antagonist per raw.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Problem with this is how does the hunter knows that he has to attack the mage with a sniper? Or poison his food? I think you guys are putting way too little importance in seeing. The example of the sleeper guy who work for the order but somehow is allowed to let go, didnt witness magic but knows mage A set fire to lots of places. What possible way has he of knowing he must use a sniper/car bomb to attack him? If the mortal could remember then it becomes easier to justify this. He follow the mage around got a feel for what he does with magic and then says &quot;yeah im gonna be better off sniping this guy&quot;<br /> <br /> Otherwise is contrive. &quot;Oh, he just use this weird methods of killing you that you dont have an arcana to counter&quot;. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> First of all not everyone wants to use Taskforce valkyrie/cherion. If a theme of mage that it likes to clutch as it safety blanket against many criticism about unecesary power high level is the abuse of power then the story of a mortal abused by a mage and that biting him in the ass with mundane means is proper with the theme.<br /> <br /> Secondly Quiescence is not as vital to the setting, Ascension ran a &quot;similar&quot; feel and it didn't had some methapysical thing that erase people's memories. Without Quiescence one can run the same story that one runs with it + more types. With Quiescence one is limited to 1 story, the same old brooding &quot;oh woe me, i must be forever apart from humanity *play angel theme son* &quot;. <br /> <br /> So if without Quiescence one can run the whole &quot;separation of humanity&quot; theme or do more stories. And with Quiescence you can run only that one, then it isnt better really. Instead of just letting the option open they put this big NO sign in the form of rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, MtAs ran that so well.....it can't even decide how to run magic well or give one good reason to actually do coincidental magic in the first place, let alone answer the question why sleepers are so offensively clueless. Between paradox/dissonance/quiescence it's clear and logical why sleepers are in the dark. And why it benefits both sides. <br /> <br /> But hey run the game how you prefer just don't think you are running HtV as envisioned or intended. Or to me doing nothing more then running Witchcraft with a different game engine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 12-02-2015, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T12:26:10-08:00","id":778515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778500#post778500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's nice that even your own game agrees with DaveB. As others have said including myself not all sleepwalkers have to work for the Pentacle/Seers or even mages. And tier 3 Hunters exist for damn good reason. This isn't Witchcraft and the quiescence is there to make it so.<br /> <br /> What's stopping a regular Hunter cell from running into a tier 3 Hunter? My guess would be nothing but the ST as usual.<br /> <br /> Hence you employ people that can actually see what said group does a devise some tactics. Aren't Hunters all about tactics? Don't tactics encompass everything including the kitchen sink? Remember life isn't fair and it works both ways between antagonist/protagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes because every hunter antagonist needs magic hunters or other endowments.....werent you the one who complain that hunters shouldnt be Reckoning?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778500#post778500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But instead most ST's have an irresistible itch to fix what works just fine without houserules for a problem that doesn't exist outside their own mind. Because they are fixated on mythical game balance and can't accept life is fair and like real life some supernaturals are better then others at things and some antagonist groups aren't equipped to deal with certain supernatural groups. End of story, full stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>While other other ST get angry when they disagree with their gods and put on the white shining armor to rabbidly defend them agaisnt any criticism because in the end said games werent made by people but by GODS! And the posibility that they do something wrong is heresy!!!! March brave soldier, for the honor of mage has being stained! It and Dave brookshaw are in need of white knights!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 12-02-2015, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T12:27:11-08:00","id":778517,"title":"","content":"Quiescence is essential to the setting of Mage. Not as a means of disarming hunters, but to reinforce the 'prisoners of the lie' aspect of the world. If that irks you, just you could always, you know, not use Quiescence in your games. Not a whole lot breaks if you take it out, and there are still ample reasons for Mages to avoid casting around sleepers (Paradox, Integrity damage, the risk of getting people with sniper rifles after them).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T12:28:49-08:00","id":778519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778509#post778509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And &quot;safety blanket?&quot; Real nice backhandedly calling the game childsh. My days of not taking these complaints seriously are certainly coming to a middle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry that got missing a piece. I was writting on the phone, the complete sentence was &quot;If a theme of mage that its fans likes to clutch as it safety blanket against many criticism about unecesary power high level is the abuse of power then the story of a mortal abused by a mage and that biting him in the ass with mundane means is proper with the theme.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T12:30:52-08:00","id":778521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778517#post778517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quiescence is essential to the setting of Mage. Not as a means of disarming hunters, but to reinforce the 'prisoners of the lie' aspect of the world. If that irks you, just you could always, you know, not use Quiescence in your games. Not a whole lot breaks if you take it out, and there are still ample reasons for Mages to avoid casting around sleepers (Paradox, Integrity damage, the risk of getting people with sniper rifles after them).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ummm that why i said, this <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778280#post778280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still the game is done, and even this thread is more about what we like/dislike about the game. My only hope is that quiessence is like in 1st edition, easy to remove without to much complication.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T12:56:50-08:00","id":778536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778507#post778507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really many fluff pieces both talk about example of a group of hunter doing this or that agaisnt mages which is kinda sad because all that read is that the people who writes the fluff resides in another plane of existence from the people who writes the rules. I really wish i could use hunters as antagonist per raw.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you actually read the fluff pieces in <i>Witchfinders</i> (the HtV book about hunting witches) you'll find that even T3 Hunters (the Malleus Mallificarum, specifically) are laughably ineffective at hunting awakened mages: the only people in the fiction in the book that actually manage to accomplish anything against an Awakened Mage is another Awakened Mage.<br /> <br /> I don't know of any other book where a Hunter group confronts an Awakened rather than some sort of generic sorcerer.<br /> <br /> So the fiction is consistent with the rules - Hunters are not well equipped to deal with the Awakened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T12:57:44-08:00","id":778537,"title":"","content":"Quiescence doesn't make you blank totally on what happened. Mage beating you with shadows and breaking your legs will not be forgotten. You will rationalize how he exactly conducted his violence, but you will remember the violence. Mage mind charming you will be remembered as drugging you, and so on. There still can be &quot;pistol on the table&quot;. Anyway, in direct confrontation, Hunter has *more* chance of beating a Mage than beating a Vampire or Werewolf. Why is not that a problem exactly, other than &quot;I can use fire to do aggravated damage!&quot;, which won't help you with &quot;1 Blood on Celerity to auto-win initiative, 3 Blood on Physical Potency, HOMERUN BABY HOMERUN!&quot; ?<br /> War in which hunter fight is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asymmetric_warfare\" target=\"_blank\">assymetric warfare</a>. You *can* win it. Making you equal to your opponents makes it symmetrical, which makes it kind of self defeating. Why would a Hunter shoot me with Sniper Rifle or bomb me? Because it's the thing people who are outclassed to equalize the playing field. And yes, even a hunter who fights people with knives (because...it's cool, I guess?) can get a drop on Mage, because stabbing wizards with pointy knives is dangerous as hell, especially if you win Surprise Check and get two rounds to stab them, because unlike all other things, they just go &quot;whooosh&quot; at full bash health meter.<br /> Hunter has no chances at fair, arena type fights. Be it versus Mages, be it versus Vampires, be it versus Werewolves. Of the three, first one is easiest to smack down, because both Vampire and Werewolf can tear you up even without being built up as combat machines. Starting Mage can probably cast spells that can disable you in two or three turns (not sure if it's that easy to instant disable in one single roll), as their direct damage potential is &quot;bashing damage equal to potency&quot;. Mages, like hunter, have to prep too; Forces 2 mage without a lighter or handy power socket won't be much of a threat to murderhobo Hunter, for example.<br /> BTW, all dear Hunters - get Stealth as your Proffession Skill. Rote Ambush with Risk Willpower is your greatest strength in direct combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T13:12:51-08:00","id":778547,"title":"","content":"LRS: It's not about white knighting for Dave, it's about trying to get you to see how you're misinterpreting the game...badly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T13:20:34-08:00","id":778554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778536#post778536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you actually read the fluff pieces in <i>Witchfinders</i> (the HtV book about hunting witches) you'll find that even T3 Hunters (the Malleus Mallificarum, specifically) are laughably ineffective at hunting awakened mages: the only people in the fiction in the book that actually manage to accomplish anything against an Awakened Mage is another Awakened Mage.<br /> <br /> I don't know of any other book where a Hunter group confronts an Awakened rather than some sort of generic sorcerer.<br /> <br /> So the fiction is consistent with the rules - Hunters are not well equipped to deal with the Awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, i should have clarified, i meant mage books. There are plenty of comments about X mage killed by hunters, X atheneum destroyed by them. Even the seers of the throne book mentions says to treat them with care because they can be dangerous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778537#post778537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quiescence doesn't make you blank totally on what happened. Mage beating you with shadows and breaking your legs will not be forgotten. You will rationalize how he exactly conducted his violence, but you will remember the violence. Mage mind charming you will be remembered as drugging you, and so on. There still can be &quot;pistol on the table&quot;. Anyway, in direct confrontation, Hunter has *more* chance of beating a Mage than beating a Vampire or Werewolf. Why is not that a problem exactly, other than &quot;I can use fire to do aggravated damage!&quot;, which won't help you with &quot;1 Blood on Celerity to auto-win initiative, 3 Blood on Physical Potency, HOMERUN BABY HOMERUN!&quot; ?<br /> War in which hunter fight is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asymmetric_warfare\" target=\"_blank\">assymetric warfare</a>. You *can* win it. Making you equal to your opponents makes it symmetrical, which makes it kind of self defeating. Why would a Hunter shoot me with Sniper Rifle or bomb me? <b><u>Because it's the thing people who are outclassed to equalize the playing field.*1</u></b> And yes, even a hunter who fights people with knives (because...it's cool, I guess?) can get a drop on Mage, because stabbing wizards with pointy knives is dangerous as hell, especially if you win Surprise Check and get two rounds to stab them, because unlike all other things, they just go &quot;whooosh&quot; at full bash health meter.<br /> Hunter has no chances at fair, arena type fights. Be it versus Mages, be it versus Vampires, be it versus Werewolves. Of the three, first one is easiest to smack down, because both Vampire and Werewolf can tear you up even without being built up as combat machines. Starting Mage can probably cast spells that can disable you in two or three turns (not sure if it's that easy to instant disable in one single roll), as their direct damage potential is &quot;bashing damage equal to potency&quot;. Mages, like hunter, have to prep too; Forces 2 mage without a lighter or handy power socket won't be much of a threat to murderhobo Hunter, for example.<br /> BTW, all dear Hunters - get Stealth as your Proffession Skill. Rote Ambush with Risk Willpower is your greatest strength in direct combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this is getting anoying because i have explained before. Im not arguing that a hunter should beat a mage in fair 1-1 fight in a white room. im not saying that, im not arguing for that. Im not saying that in said white room the mage and hunter must be on equal footing.<br /> <br /> Hunters can only win when they get a propper plan and propper planning, which quienssence completely strips. *1 How would he knows he is outclassed if he cant remember what the mage did? If he rationalizes that its a drug or whatever then how he knows he is outclassed?<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;gun on the table&quot;, if you meant as the example said above then it doesnt applied. That was an example about how quiessence isnt needed to enforce the separation of humanity from the mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778514#post778514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, MtAs ran that so well.....it can't even decide how to run magic well or give one good reason to actually do coincidental magic in the first place, let alone answer the question why sleepers are so offensively clueless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, they handle it the best possible way. It was good for those anal retentive st who needs an explanation for the &quot;masquerade&quot; to function and for those who went the dresden route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T13:28:44-08:00","id":778562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778547#post778547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">LRS: It's not about white knighting for Dave, it's about trying to get you to see how you're misinterpreting the game...badly.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a reason that i say that you and kumiko seem to treat Dave like flawless god and this sentence perfectly encompass it.<br /> <br /> You cannot conceive the idea that someone understand the whys and still disagree with him? Im not misinterpreting anything, i understand he thinks quiessence is vital for a theme of separating humanity from the sleepers and maintain the veil. And i know this will blow your mind but, i don't agree with him. Nothing against the guy honestly, just dont agree with him on that. I think is heavy handed, i think is forces mechanics on things that shouldn't have mechanics and let for ST interpretation. I think is dissonant with a chunk of the fluff and worse of all i think it takes stories away without giving anything in return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T13:35:58-08:00","id":778566,"title":"","content":"Okay. So you prefer stupid mortals, even more stupid mages and hunters so insane that they are virtually useless? Hint, MtAs never explained why typical humans couldn't see magic straight up and if so why they didn't organize into Hunter cells not run by Angels of all things, being so insane they couldn't actually function if you thought about it for a second. Cool beans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 12-02-2015, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T13:39:24-08:00","id":778569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778554#post778554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Exactly, they handle it the best possible way. It was good for those anal retentive st who needs an explanation for the &quot;masquerade&quot; to function and for those who went the dresden route.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ascension's &quot;consensual reality&quot; and coincidental/vulgar distinctions were a red hot mess, and even the tremendous M20 tome has failed to mitigate the debates that have raged for decades. <br /> <br /> As a fan of WW books since they first appeared in the early 1990, I found the nWOD's setting and mechanical streamlining, particularly in Awakening, to be monumental improvements, and the spoilers for Mage 2e look to be yet further excellent refinements and updates. <br /> <br /> What you appear to like about Ascension is precisely what the clear majority of Awakening (and a large number of Ascencion) fans view as a cautionary tale for PRG development.<br /> <br /> In any event, Mage 2e is written and done, the Quiescence is part of the canon setting, and the vast majority of Mage fans appear quite satisfied. If you don't like the Quiescence or anything else, feel free to eliminate it from your games. Neither Dave nor jackbooted WW stormtroopers will break down your door and arrest you for having badwrongfun.<br /> <br /> Finally, if you believe Hunter may now have a &quot;Awakened Mage problem,&quot; you concerns probably should be best addressed to Monica Valentinelli, the new Hunter 2e developer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T13:45:45-08:00","id":778572,"title":"","content":"You know, I'll agree with Loki here. It's definitely possible to remove Quiescence and still maintain the tone and feel of Awakening. As long as magic still hurts sleepers and their presence invokes the Abyss that's plenty of reason right there for Mage's to feel separated and alone. There's some revamping to do with the Orders, The Diamond would likely have to be more active in hunting down and suppressing sleepers who insist on trying to out magic (which, IMO, puts Hunters at an even greater disadvantage, because now Mage society is deliberately targeting them. For their own safety no less). But overall its entirely doable.<br /> <br /> <b>However,</b> and this is a big however, Quiescence is a big part of the Mage setting, and has been since the formative moments of 1e. Removing it would be a humongous change to the world Mage presents. For that reason alone it should remain. Don't like it? The books account for that. The very first rule in all the nWoD books is the Golden Rule: discard what you dislike.<br /> <br /> In that regard it's very similar to Ascension (which people knock for being unclear, but I laud for recognizing the advantage table top games have over all other genres: Storyteller moderation).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 12-02-2015, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T13:53:25-08:00","id":778576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778562#post778562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a reason that i say that you and kumiko seem to treat Dave like flawless god and this sentence perfectly encompass it.</div> </div> </div> </div>People hardly treat Dave as a &quot;flawless god,&quot; and if you've read many of the comments following release of many of the 2e spoilers, criticisms were ample and sometimes quite severe by people who were otherwise generally satisfied with the game (check out the comments for the Mysterium spoilers!). <br /> <br /> In fact, Dave's embrace of Open Development has often been quite thankless. To his credit, Dave has made changes and clarifications when thought they were required. However, and thank God, Mage 2e is not a game designed by committee, and there ultimately needs to be single, consistent, and firm vision. Dave has, IMHO correctly, decided to maintain internal thematic and mechanical consistency in Mage over limited crossover objections and concerns.<br /> <br /> The debates about Hunter vs Mages have been extensively discussed, Dave has offered his perspective, people have responded, and final decisions made. Simply, most seem very happy, but it's impossible to please everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T13:56:57-08:00","id":778578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778569#post778569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ascension's &quot;consensual reality&quot; and coincidental/vulgar distinctions were a red hot mess, and even the tremendous M20 tome has failed to mitigate the debates that have raged for decades.<br /> <br /> As a fan of WW books since they first appeared in the early 1990, I found the nWOD's setting and mechanical streamlining, particularly in Awakening, to be monumental improvements, and the spoilers for Mage 2e look to be yet further excellent refinements and updates.<br /> <br /> What you appear to like about Ascension is precisely what the clear majority of Awakening (and a large number of Ascencion) fans view as a cautionary tale for PRG development.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just defended Ascension take on the masquerade, i made not reference on the consensual reality, magick system and how that worked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778566#post778566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. So you prefer stupid mortals, even more stupid mages and hunters so insane that they are virtually useless? Hint, MtAs never explained why typical humans couldn't see magic straight up and if so why they didn't organize into Hunter cells not run by Angels of all things, being so insane they couldn't actually function if you thought about it for a second. Cool beans.</div> </div> </div> </div>They did explain it. They saw magic and didnt foget about it. And i talked about how the handle the masquerade not hunters, <u><b>you</b></u> however, are the one that said hunters all should have supernatural stuff ala hunter the reckoning (all tier 3 or get out). The masquerade was maintained because if a mage broke it either hunter or the technocracy would rain on said mage. Not to mention the other supernaturals who would take issue.<br /> <br /> The maintanance of the masquerade was left up in the air as it should, the anal retentive ST could latch on one of the multiple explanation. The dresden masquerade one, could just move one and not worry much about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778572#post778572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I'll agree with Loki here. It's definitely possible to remove Quiescence and still maintain the tone and feel of Awakening. As long as magic still hurts sleepers and their presence invokes the Abyss that's plenty of reason right there for Mage's to feel separated and alone. There's some revamping to do with the Orders, The Diamond would likely have to be more active in hunting down and suppressing sleepers who insist on trying to out magic (which, IMO, puts Hunters at an even greater disadvantage, because now Mage society is deliberately targeting them. For their own safety no less). But overall its entirely doable.</div> </div> </div> </div>This<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T13:59:56-08:00","id":778579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778578#post778578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This</div> </div> </div> </div>Please note the &quot;However&quot; portion of my original post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T14:10:01-08:00","id":778586,"title":"","content":"I said THEY SHOULD NOT. Is three times enough to get the message across? If not, I am willing to tell you exactly what I think about your opinion. Just to prepare you from future misunderstandings it's pretty much diametrically opposed to your assessment of the situation on multiple levels and has exactly nothing to do with DaveB given it's likely I was playing and running the WoD before him. It's crappy to hit 50 very soon but happens if you're lucky.<br /> <br /> There is good reason for disonance/paradox/quiescence/wisdom they work together to make MtAw a horror game not urban fantasy or culture wars like Mtas. Remove one leg and the whole table collapses or becomes something else entirely.<br /> <br /> That's fine but it isn't horror to me. It's more like Dresden Files or Witchcraft which are fine games in their own right but not what I want out of MtAw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 12-02-2015, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T14:19:16-08:00","id":778593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778572#post778572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>However,</b> and this is a big however, Quiescence is a big part of the Mage setting, and has been since the formative moments of 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of 1e, in 1e a Sleeper's Willpower score determined how severely they were affected by Quiescence, with the rare Sleeper with a maxed-out Willpower score being completely unaffected and remembering everything. I wonder if that's still the case? I find myself hoping that it is. I like the idea of the rare high-Willpower Sleeper being the only one who's seeing all this crazy stuff (and probably thinking he's crazy himself, considering nobody else around him remembers things the way he does).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T14:27:06-08:00","id":778600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Juhn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778593#post778593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of 1e, in 1e a Sleeper's Willpower score determined how severely they were affected by Quiescence, with the rare Sleeper with a maxed-out Willpower score being completely unaffected and remembering everything. I wonder if that's still the case? I find myself hoping that it is. I like the idea of the rare high-Willpower Sleeper being the only one who's seeing all this crazy stuff (and probably thinking he's crazy himself, considering nobody else around him remembers things the way he does).</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on Dave's spoilers and numerous comments, I believe Quiescence is an absolute and now unconnected to Willpower (although a high Integrity will help with those Breaking Point rolls).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ill-lie-to-you/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ill-lie-to-you/\" target=\"_blank\"> I&rsquo;ll Lie To You &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ill-lie-to-you/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/ill-lie-to-you/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sleepers<br /> Mechanically, every human character in the World of Darkness that isn\u2019t Awakened or a Sleepwalker is a Sleeper. In the Fallen World Chronicle, the Sleeper rules extend the Integrity rules found in the God-Machine Chronicle, Strix Chronicle, and Idigam Chronicle, centered around that most Magely of Breaking Point questions:<br /> What Have You Forgotten?<br /> The basics of being a Sleeper are as follows;<ul><li>If a Sleeper character perceives an obviously magical effect caused by Supernal magic (whether it\u2019s the powers of a Supernal entity or a mage\u2019s spell) they immediately suffer a Breaking Point against Integrity.</li> <li>If a Sleeper is present when a mage tries to cast a spell with an obviously magical effect, they add a die of Paradox Risk. Multiple Sleepers don\u2019t add more dice, but apply a dice trick to the Paradox roll: 9-again for a couple of people, 8-again for a dispersed group like urban foot traffic, and rote factor for a large crowd.</li> <li>Sleepers who come into contact with obvious spells after they\u2019ve been cast slowly dispel them, in an effect mages call \u201cDissonance\u201d</li> <li>Quiescence: The scene after a Sleeper witnesses a spell \u2013 whether they caused it to crumble under Dissonance or not \u2013 they forget about it. Their memory warps, and they rationalize the event away or substitute a non-magical equivalent. Convincingly reminding them (including using magic to do so) causes them to suffer another Breaking Point, and then forget again.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T14:46:13-08:00","id":778606,"title":"","content":"Sure, but Quiescence having graduated effects wouldn't actually contradict the general rules there - the book itself might get more specific.<br /> <br /> And even if it doesn't, I imagine it wouldn't break the game to houserule it.<br /> <br /> Also, having just looked it up again, it appears that the &quot;Sleepers forget magic&quot; was part of &quot;Disbelief&quot; in 1e, which explains why it's actually called Disbelief - it's less about the unravelling spells and more the part where Sleepers disbelieve what they see and substitute it either with nothing (if their willpower score is low), or remember it as a dream or substitute a rational explanation (if their willpower score is middling). Based on 1e core, the Quiescence is just &quot;the general tendency for people not to Awaken to the truth&quot;, which I believe has been folded into the definition of The Lie in 2e.<br /> <br /> I like 2e's terminology better, if only for separating the terms for &quot;Sleepers forget magic&quot; and &quot;Sleepers unravel spell effects&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T15:32:27-08:00","id":778636,"title":"","content":"Have I expressed how much I like new purview of Death and Prime, Secrets and Truth respectively? I find these much more interesting than &quot;Ghosts&quot; or &quot;Primal Fire&quot;; I can't wait to make a character with both of them, and go into a legacy all about exploring these two in tandem. Would make a great Obrimos detective who isn't cheating and using Time and Mind :P. (I loved 11th Question fluff, but I never liked playing a detective type character with Time and Mind [Mind was pretty important for Questions]; their abilities always felt like defeating <i>the purpose of playing a detective</i>])<br /> Also, I really like idea of mixing and reinforcing shadows with platonic phantasms, and vice versa...looks like interesting way to do &quot;stuff of pure power&quot; temporal creations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T15:40:50-08:00","id":778642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Juhn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778606#post778606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but Quiescence having graduated effects wouldn't actually contradict the general rules there - the book itself might get more specific.<br /> <br /> And even if it doesn't, I imagine it wouldn't break the game to houserule it.<br /> <br /> Also, having just looked it up again, it appears that the &quot;Sleepers forget magic&quot; was part of &quot;Disbelief&quot; in 1e, which explains why it's actually called Disbelief - it's less about the unravelling spells and more the part where Sleepers disbelieve what they see and substitute it either with nothing (if their willpower score is low), or remember it as a dream or substitute a rational explanation (if their willpower score is middling). Based on 1e core, the Quiescence is just &quot;the general tendency for people not to Awaken to the truth&quot;, which I believe has been folded into the definition of The Lie in 2e.<br /> <br /> I like 2e's terminology better, if only for separating the terms for &quot;Sleepers forget magic&quot; and &quot;Sleepers unravel spell effects&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>They changed it to clarify it actually has nothing to do with belief or disbelief of magic or a person's strength of mind (willpower). It is a curse and there is no way around it beyond either being some level of supernatural or being a sleepwalker.<br /> <br /> To me that makes far more sense then &quot;I disbelieve!!!!&quot; &quot;Or if I try really hard because I have a really strong mind I won't forget&quot;. Because it just is, Now it makes total sense that there can be a globally networked society completely hidden from everybody without the CWoD solution of having everything run by some supernatural group while everybody else is painted as being willfully ignorant or that mundane law enforcement wouldn't have clue one about what is actually going on at some level. Especially with things like cell phones, computers, tablets, intranet, apps for social media that keep us all networked up as a matter of daily life.<br /> <br /> Dissonance is completely seperate and is the term for &quot;unraveling&quot; spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 12-02-2015, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T15:53:26-08:00","id":778653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778642#post778642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They changed it to clarify it actually has nothing to do with belief or disbelief of magic or a person's strength of mind (willpower). It is a curse and there is no way around it beyond either being some level of supernatural or being a sleepwalker.<br /> <br /> To me that makes far more sense then &quot;I disbelieve!!!!&quot; &quot;Or if I try really hard because I have a really strong mind I won't forget&quot;. Because it just is, Now it makes total sense that there can be a globally networked society completely hidden from everybody without the CWoD solution of having everything run by some supernatural group while everybody else is painted as being willfully ignorant or that mundane law enforcement wouldn't have clue one about what is actually going on at some level. Especially with things like cell phones, computers, tablets, intranet, apps for social media that keep us all networked up as a matter of daily life.<br /> <br /> Dissonance is completely seperate and is the term for &quot;unraveling&quot; spells.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I now get a certain sense of schadenfreude that groups like Network Zero who try to meticulously document and record supernatural events as proof of their existence probably suffer the worst when it comes to supernal magic.<br /> <br /> They get a breaking point and forget every time they watch a video or read an account of supernal magic, a vicious cycle that's sure to leave them insane or suicidal. If they happen to be a Sleepwalker, all they'll accomplish is inflicting this curse on everyone they try to convince, and they'll still never remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T15:58:22-08:00","id":778657,"title":"","content":"BTW, for Hunters vs Mages thing - I think Hurt Locker will make you people happy. It seems that it will contain a lot of power house, mortals-only merits. Punch Drunk, for example; another one, relevant to this, is a merit that allows you to ignore tilts for a number of rounds. It scales with your stats, and starts with a minimum of 3 tilts for 3 rounds, I think. Why is this relevant?<br /> Because most of mage abilities to disable you in one move are translated to &quot;inflict really nasty tilt&quot;. Want to fight mages? Get that merit. Blindness? Ignore it! Shadowy tentacles trying to immobilize you? Punch them and go for the mages throat! Sure, it's only 3 rounds and only 3 tilts, but mage is going to inflict one tilt per round at best; and if you can't kill them in 3 rounds, then you are fucked either way.<br /> Another thing to remember is that mages need to use yantras in their spells. Yantras take time. Spells with only one Yantra are not that strong, especially if they are contested or resisted; another way of beating a mage is superior numbers, because adding people to the mix means that mage can't put as much power into potency, and needs to spread the dice around. And if mage is arrogant enough to try casting spells longer than instant casts, then well, smash them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T16:11:53-08:00","id":778667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778657#post778657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, for Hunters vs Mages thing - I think Hurt Locker will make you people happy. It seems that it will contain a lot of power house, mortals-only merits. Punch Drunk, for example; another one, relevant to this, is a merit that allows you to ignore tilts for a number of rounds. It scales with your stats, and starts with a minimum of 3 tilts for 3 rounds, I think. Why is this relevant?<br /> Because most of mage abilities to disable you in one move are translated to &quot;inflict really nasty tilt&quot;. Want to fight mages? Get that merit. Blindness? Ignore it! Shadowy tentacles trying to immobilize you? Punch them and go for the mages throat! Sure, it's only 3 rounds and only 3 tilts, but mage is going to inflict one tilt per round at best; and if you can't kill them in 3 rounds, then you are fucked either way.<br /> Another thing to remember is that mages need to use yantras in their spells. Yantras take time. Spells with only one Yantra are not that strong, especially if they are contested or resisted; another way of beating a mage is superior numbers, because adding people to the mix means that mage can't put as much power into potency, and needs to spread the dice around. And if mage is arrogant enough to try casting spells longer than instant casts, then well, smash them.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the strongest advantages of the Arcana is that most provide one or more means of providing a quick and fairly easy escape from a violent encounter, whether it's teleportation, flight and super-speed, or simply vanishing into Twilight or the past.future, etc. Mages who cannot expeditiously kill or disable their adversaries can usually get the hell out of Dodge real quick.<br /> <br /> This creates a <i>very</i> bad situation for any Hunters. The mage is now angry and possibly obsessed, and knows he's definitely being hunted and likely by whom (the attack may have even provided him a sympathetic Yantra to be used later!). He can thoroughly prepare to defend himself and seek allies and other protection. At this point, any prudent Hunters should update the wills, say their goodbyes to family and friends, and prepare to painfully shuffle off their mortal coil. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T16:13:25-08:00","id":778668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems that it will contain a lot of power house, mortals-only merits. </div> </div> </div>Are they mortal only? I was under the impression they were open to anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T16:31:18-08:00","id":778675,"title":"","content":"In the comments thread, author specified that he intends to certain power hourse merits be only mortal-only. Which may or may not suck, depends on your perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T19:42:13-08:00","id":778768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778636#post778636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have I expressed how much I like new purview of Death and Prime, Secrets and Truth respectively? I find these much more interesting than &quot;Ghosts&quot; or &quot;Primal Fire&quot;; I can't wait to make a character with both of them, and go into a legacy all about exploring these two in tandem. Would make a great Obrimos detective who isn't cheating and using Time and Mind :P. (I loved 11th Question fluff, but I never liked playing a detective type character with Time and Mind [Mind was pretty important for Questions]; their abilities always felt like defeating <i>the purpose of playing a detective</i>])<br /> Also, I really like idea of mixing and reinforcing shadows with platonic phantasms, and vice versa...looks like interesting way to do &quot;stuff of pure power&quot; temporal creations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, if you keep up with League of Legends lore, I'm trying to design a Legacy based on <a href=\"http://leagueoflegends.wikia.com/wiki/Illaoi\" target=\"_blank\">Illaoi</a>. I'm about 70% certain it should be Prime Ruling, Death Optional, but I'm still toying with it and won't be able to commit confidently to my ideas until I see the write-ups for the individual Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T19:52:15-08:00","id":778774,"title":"","content":"What's with all this Hunter vs Mage stuff? I'm not even sure I understand the point of it. I mean, Hunters are if anything <i>helped</i> by these things. Sure, it's a Breaking Point, but you also dissolve your mage opponent's magic and make it Paradoxed. The only issue is Quiescence, but even then Hunters are the type to not trust their memory and go &quot;dey took're memories!&quot;<br /> <br /> Even then, Sleepwalker is a 1 dot merit, and is easy to justify for a Hunter. &quot;Oh, why are you so willing to believe in the Supernatural and not try to reason it away?&quot; &quot;I'm actually partly awakened to the Lie of the world&quot; &quot;Makes sense to me&quot;. Nevermind the ease of making an Endowment for each Hunter group that would help. Advanced Armoury? An eyedrive like they use with the Silents in Doctor Who. Thaumatechnology? Hell, the Banality Worm seems to imply it's an Abyssal Entity that eats even non-Supernal supernatural effects, maybe it grants clarity. Relic? Glass eye that needs to be used as a replacement for a real eye. You see fine, even if it's creepy, and it prevents Lunacy and Quiescence and maybe lets you Clash of Wills against effects like Auspex. Don't Ascending Ones already have some Balm of True Sight or whatever? Lucifuge aren't human. Do Benedictions count as internal? Either way, I'm sure in <b>Spirit Slayers</b> they have some anti-Lunacy ability. What else is there... Mysteres? They're Claimed. Knights of Saint Adrian? Eye tattoos are gaudy, but whatever works.<br /> <br /> This stuff ain't hard, people... You've got half a dozen ways to &quot;fix&quot; this thing that ain't broken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T20:13:06-08:00","id":778778,"title":"","content":"This thread is the supernal symbol of jumping the gun.<br /> <br /> We've gotten a lot spoiled, but there's plenty of key things we haven't seen, not to mention some of the spoilers lack the greater context of the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T20:40:53-08:00","id":778785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778774#post778774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's with all this Hunter vs Mage stuff? I'm not even sure I understand the point of it. I mean, Hunters are if anything <i>helped</i> by these things. Sure, it's a Breaking Point, but you also dissolve your mage opponent's magic and make it Paradoxed. The only issue is Quiescence, but even then Hunters are the type to not trust their memory and go &quot;dey took're memories!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Dissonance only applies to long-last magical effects, and is useless in combat. Sleepers also only add one Paradox die spellcasting dice pools, and is hardly crippling. Sleeper Paradox and Dissonance are certainly inconvenient and sometimes problematic, but hardly equalize sleepers and mages.<br /> <br /> Quiescence is primarily a perceived problem because it prevents sleeper Hunters from ever realizing an Awakened mage or Awakened magic might be the cause of a problem and properly preparing for an encounter with a A-list supernatural. Fighting your average Obrimos or Mastigos is certainly <i>far</i> more dangerous than your run of the mill occultist, psychic or gangbanger.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778778#post778778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread is the supernal symbol of jumping the gun.<br /> <br /> We've gotten a lot spoiled, but there's plenty of key things we haven't seen, not to mention some of the spoilers lack the greater context of the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>While true, Dave's been pretty clear about the Quiescence and sleeper Hunter vs. Mage issue, and has offered his thoughts on multiple occasions.<br /> <br /> I believe his comment, &quot;I am sustained by the tears of Hunter fans,&quot; really speaks for itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T21:02:12-08:00","id":778789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778785#post778785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dissonance only applies to long-last magical effects, and is useless in combat. Sleepers also only add one Paradox die spellcasting dice pools, and is hardly crippling. Sleeper Paradox and Dissonance are certainly inconvenient and sometimes problematic, but hardly equalize sleepers and mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can also add 9 or 8-again and even Rote quality (though I doubt that many Hunters will be in a group).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Quiescence is primarily a perceived problem because it prevents sleeper Hunters from ever realizing an Awakened mage or Awakened magic might be the cause of a problem and properly preparing for an encounter with a A-list supernatural. </div> </div> </div>But that's wrong and dumb. Remembering the event rationally doesn't mean they can't doubt their own memories, and it doesn't mean they can't research a mage. A proper Hunter cell should be able to deal with Purple Man going &quot;forget about me&quot; simply by understanding they have gaps in their memory and stories that don't add up. How did the man get across the room so fast? You remember him running, but there's no way he could have. It must be wizardry. Time to hit the library. (Turns out the solution is to hit it with a car)<br /> Why does no one have this problem with Lunacy? That prevents Hunters from remembering things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I believe his comment, &quot;I am sustained by the tears of Hunter fans,&quot; really speaks for itself. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it speaks to the fact that he finds the entire debate silly :V<br /> If you're playing Hunter, use Hunter rules. It's much easier, causes much less headache, and is more internally consistent. Or just give the Hunters the Sleepwalker Merit. Or one of a number of other things. Hell, give all your Hunters Sleepwalker and suddenly they have to deal with the fact that they remember but no one else does. You don't have to fundamentally change Mage to &quot;deal&quot; with anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T21:11:10-08:00","id":778793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778789#post778789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can also add 9 or 8-again and even Rote quality (though I doubt that many Hunters will be in a group).<br /> <br /> But that's wrong and dumb. Remembering the event rationally doesn't mean they can't doubt their own memories, and it doesn't mean they can't research a mage. A proper Hunter cell should be able to deal with Purple Man going &quot;forget about me&quot; simply by understanding they have gaps in their memory and stories that don't add up. How did the man get across the room so fast? You remember him running, but there's no way he could have. It must be wizardry. Time to hit the library. (Turns out the solution is to hit it with a car)<br /> Why does no one have this problem with Lunacy? That prevents Hunters from remembering things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quiescence either causes total amnesia, or if that is impractical, forces you to rationalize the supernal event as entirely non-supernatural. <br /> <br /> A Hunter wouldn't have odd memory gaps or unexplained stories. They would either have nothing, and thus no need or interest in an explanation, or would have already provided themselves with a convenient non-supernatural explanation for the supernal event.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T21:21:47-08:00","id":778796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778793#post778793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quiescence either causes total amnesia, or if that is impractical, forces you to rationalize the supernal event as entirely non-supernatural.<br /> <br /> A Hunter wouldn't have odd memory gaps or unexplained stories. They would either have nothing, and thus no need or interest in an explanation, or would have already provided themselves with a convenient non-supernatural explanation for the supernal event.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Their memory warps, and they rationalize the event away or substitute a non-magical equivalent. Convincingly reminding them (including using magic to do so) causes them to suffer another Breaking Point, and then forget again.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You and I seem to have quite a different opinion on what the word &quot;warp&quot; means. Just because they remember it one way doesn't mean that's the way it happened. And it doesn't require them to &quot;remember&quot; it how it went down to feel that their memory is wrong. I mean, that's already how memory works to begin with, and Hunters are the kind of people who will doubt their memories by nature (or they won't live long after the first Ventrue encounter).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T21:27:43-08:00","id":778797,"title":"","content":"It is my understanding that anything that causes recall of a witnessed supernal event, regardless of later rationalization or non-supernatural explanation, will cause the subject to again suffer Quiescence.<br /> <br /> As we appear to have far different interpretations of the pertinent spoilers, hopefully Dave will offer a ruling or clarification. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T22:17:12-08:00","id":778811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778789#post778789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can also add 9 or 8-again and even Rote quality (though I doubt that many Hunters will be in a group).<br /> <br /> But that's wrong and dumb. Remembering the event rationally doesn't mean they can't doubt their own memories, and it doesn't mean they can't research a mage. A proper Hunter cell should be able to deal with Purple Man going &quot;forget about me&quot; simply by understanding they have gaps in their memory and stories that don't add up. How did the man get across the room so fast? You remember him running, but there's no way he could have. It must be wizardry. Time to hit the library. (Turns out the solution is to hit it with a car)<br /> Why does no one have this problem with Lunacy? That prevents Hunters from remembering things.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, it speaks to the fact that he finds the entire debate silly :V<br /> If you're playing Hunter, use Hunter rules. It's much easier, causes much less headache, and is more internally consistent. Or just give the Hunters the Sleepwalker Merit. Or one of a number of other things. Hell, give all your Hunters Sleepwalker and suddenly they have to deal with the fact that they remember but no one else does. You don't have to fundamentally change Mage to &quot;deal&quot; with anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give the man a cigar. In fact it is just fine from a mage perspective if you do so. Because now their target can fight back full force. But if I were a mage (Obrimos for example) that saw my best shot didn't work I'd use Forces 2 and go full invisible and get the hell out of Dodge. Then afterwards my new obsession would be &quot;Hunt the Hunters&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 12-03-2015, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T22:25:25-08:00","id":778813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778796#post778796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You and I seem to have quite a different opinion on what the word &quot;warp&quot; means. Just because they remember it one way doesn't mean that's the way it happened. And it doesn't require them to &quot;remember&quot; it how it went down to feel that their memory is wrong. I mean, that's already how memory works to begin with, and Hunters are the kind of people who will doubt their memories by nature (or they won't live long after the first Ventrue encounter).</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the Masquerade is just that, a contrivance. Quiensense is a soul deep curse on EVERY human that isn't either a sleepwalker or supernatural in some form themselves. Lunacy is kind of a little sister to quiescence it isn't a socio-political treaty like the Masquerade, it's something that just is at the primal level that humanity has no say in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 12-03-2015, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T22:37:51-08:00","id":778815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778813#post778813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunacy is kind of a little sister to quiescence it isn't a socio-political treaty like the Masquerade, it's something that just is at the primal and soul level that humanity has no say in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunacy is the deep down, ancestral fear of the wolf at the door.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T22:49:55-08:00","id":778818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778815#post778815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunacy is the deep down, ancestral fear of the wolf at the door.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, it's a primal fear of the dark and the monsters beyond the campfire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T23:25:00-08:00","id":778828,"title":"","content":"All I want to say is that the idea that a Hunter would think sniping someone from a block or two away would be a weird approach to offing someone... kinda funny.<br /> <br /> I'm <i>reasonably</i> certain that the proper mindset to survive the Vigil is to employ as much overkill as you can - after, of course, determining which overkill will work.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/357795-hunters-and-the-theory-of-everything\">I mean, hunters run on bullshit <i>anyway</i></a> - if solving your problems by hitting them with a truck is wrong, I don't want to be right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T02:53:26-08:00","id":778881,"title":"","content":"The Sleeping Curse is one of the reasons I feel that any mortal seriously attempting to Hunt mages needs a dedicated scribe/information keeper. I'm talking about someones whose dedicated role is to stay back at base, have constant contact with the agents in the field, and have the active hunters call in what they're seeing so that they can record it. If I recall correctly, I'm fairly sure that Quiescence only affects those who actually <i>perceive </i>Supernal magic in some way and only takes hold <i>after</i> the scene is over with. So I'd assume that someone who only hears a secondhand account of, but is never actually exposed to, the magic itself would be relatively fine.<br /> <br /> So you have a guy sitting back at base with some sort of radio or other communications device, or hell, maybe with some sort of machine with speech to text so he couldn't even get any actual audio, receiving constant reports of what the people in the field are seeing at the moment. So this guy, who wouldn't be affected by the information he's handling, would keep track of all records and suspect data, only telling the guys who were exposed to magic who they needed to take down, what tactics to use, and what equipment to bring. Never hinting that magic was a factor so as to not cause a breaking point recursion, but supplying the Hunters with everything they might need to be able to react appropriately to what they're dealing with.<br /> <br /> Now there are still problems with even this, and the people doing the actual visual investigation are going to need therapists to deal with the landslide of breaking points that this sort of job is going to put them through, but it's pretty much the best they're going to get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 12-03-2015, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T04:21:24-08:00","id":778909,"title":"","content":"That's a great idea Ashenrogue. Compartmentalizing information to prevent dissonance from preventing the hunters fighting back at full strength / preparedness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T07:58:19-08:00","id":779011,"title":"","content":"On 4chan, Dave has offered some additional clarification about the Quiescence and Hunters' use of notes, recording, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#117743\"><b>DaveB</b></span> <span style=\"color:#117743\">!!kn3vuELOelB</span> 12/03/15(Thu)05:50:08 </span></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> In the scene directly following exposure to the Supernal or Abyssal, a Sleeper forgets what she saw, or else changes how she remembers it toward the mundane. Any serious attempt to prod at those false memories, bring them into question, or correct them with magic trigger a breaking point as if she were witnessing the traumatic event again for the first time, followed by the memory being removed again. It is as harrowing in memory is it is in reality. Quiescence, like Dissonance, is not limited to the spells of mages; Sleepers\u2019 memories are clouded by the interior of ruins of the Time Before, the presence of the Mad, Emanation Realms, and sighting Supernal or Abyssal entities.<br /> <br /> <b>Pretty much any Hunter tactic to take notes, record what's happening, or prod at Quiescence because you think a mage is nearby will put you on a one-way train to Crazytown, Paranoia. population: you.</b><br /> <br /> Unless I can interest you in this shiny one-dot Merit called &quot;Sleepwalker&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T08:24:53-08:00","id":779021,"title":"","content":"I think Ashenrogue's idea would still work, but it means you could never debrief Hunters in the field after going up against a Mage. They would basically only get to know that they did good, or bad while the guy who stayed behind arranges tactics accordingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T08:40:12-08:00","id":779028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779021#post779021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Ashenrogue's idea would still work, but it means you could never debrief Hunters in the field after going up against a Mage. They would basically only get to know that they did good, or bad while the guy who stayed behind arranges tactics accordingly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree that it would protect the &quot;coordinator&quot; and might provide a small measure of tactical assistance. However, as you and Ashenrogue acknowledge, the people actually doing the fighting will still suffer greatly and potentially repeatedly.<br /> <br /> I would also note that there's really no reason for average mortal Hunters to believe they need to employ such unusual measures. Given the very nature of the Quiescence, how do they even know about it, no less understand effective means to try to avoid it. Further, given the already poor odds faced by Hunters fighting A-list supernaturals, and the various supernatural and mundane means to jam communications and completely obviate the suggested tactic, leaving someone behind can mean the difference between life and death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T08:50:22-08:00","id":779034,"title":"","content":"From what DaveB just mentioned a couple of posts up the coordinator would still have to be a sleepwalker to make it even remotely workable and that would bring it's own set of problems <br /> <br /> Ie. even taping or whatever remote method employed is affected by the quiescence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T08:55:32-08:00","id":779038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779034#post779034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what DaveB just mentioned a couple of posts up the coordinator would still have to be a sleepwalker to make it even remotely workable and that would bring it's own set of problems<br /> <br /> Ie. even taping or whatever remote method employed is affected by the quiescence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally forgot that just <i>hearing</i> a supernal event will still trigger Quiescence, and thus a sleeper &quot;coordinator&quot; may still be affected using Ashenrogue's suggestion.<br /> <br /> Damn that Quiescence is nasty...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T09:56:33-08:00","id":779052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=778774#post778774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even then, Sleepwalker is a 1 dot merit, and is easy to justify for a Hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it? Where's the info from? I remember it being 3 dot in 1e.<br /> <br /> Re: Quiescence: It should <u><i><b>really</b></i></u> scale like Lunacy if it doesn't already. As in, exceptional success - remember with perfect clarity, dramatic failure: become Sleepwalker authomatically (and, depending not the reading, keep your Intergrity without any condition whatsover), no XP on condition and a Beat as ususal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":6508,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","user":"Tambov","date":". 12-03-2015, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T10:08:42-08:00","id":779054,"title":"","content":"Something that stood out to me from what DaveB was quoted as saying above is this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i> Quiescence, like Dissonance, is not limited to the spells of mages; Sleepers\u2019 memories are clouded by the interior of ruins of the Time Before, <b>the presence of the Mad</b>, Emanation Realms, and sighting Supernal or Abyssal entities.</i> </div> </div> </div><i><br /> <br /> So I've always liked the idea of one of the Mad who takes Solopsism to it's extreme but if sleepers are forced to forget their presence then that might be fairly common.</i><br /> <br /> &quot;Why are you protecting her? She's not even real. I visited her three times this week and she greeted me the same way each time. Real people don't respond like that. They remember! Not her though. Not any of the teeming masses. We're alone here. Two real human beings in a city full of walking lies. So no I'm not giving her &quot;soul&quot; back. I need whatever this thing is more than miss &quot;Hi, I'm Sally, what's your name?&quot; does.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1571-kamikazegerbil","name":"Kamikazegerbil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1571_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T10:08:53-08:00","id":779055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779052#post779052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it? Where's the info from? I remember it being 3 dot in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave has repeatedly mentioned the fact and several people have quoted various posts in which he's done so. Sleepwalker was four dots in 1e and served as a prerequisite for the one-dot Proximus Merit in the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T10:09:20-08:00","id":779056,"title":"","content":"It's 1 dot.<br /> <br /> Quiescence doesn't scale. It did in 1e, where willpower 9 and 10 people could remember, but we're getting rid of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T10:21:24-08:00","id":779063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779056#post779056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's 1 dot.<br /> <br /> Quiescence doesn't scale. It did in 1e, where willpower 9 and 10 people could remember, but we're getting rid of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why should it be stronger than Lunacy? The latter is basically an extention of the Raptor and can be overcome (or overcome you, on dramatic failure. same difference).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T10:25:15-08:00","id":779069,"title":"","content":"Why shouldn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T10:34:05-08:00","id":779074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779034#post779034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what DaveB just mentioned a couple of posts up the coordinator would still have to be a sleepwalker to make it even remotely workable and that would bring it's own set of problems <br /> <br /> Ie. even taping or whatever remote method employed is affected by the quiescence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking walky talkies, &quot;This guy just shot a fireball at me!&quot; It's not until after the scene that Quiescence kicks in, and being informed of events second hand like that would cut out the Quiescence for the coordinator. Still risky if he hears magic over the comm system, but if it's push to talk the odds go down a lot and the coordinator can build tactical profiles on targets. More information can be gained via less than direct contact with the enemy by finding and interrogating or flipping a Mage's mortal-ish allies.<br /> <br /> Incredibly dangerous but doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T10:47:08-08:00","id":779084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779074#post779074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking walky talkies, &amp;quot;This guy just shot a fireball at me!&amp;quot; It's not until after the scene that Quiescence kicks in, and being informed of events second hand like that would cut out the Quiescence for the coordinator. Still risky if he hears magic over the comm system, but if it's push to talk the odds go down a lot and the coordinator can build tactical profiles on targets. More information can be gained via less than direct contact with the enemy by finding and interrogating or flipping a Mage's mortal-ish allies.<br /> <br /> Incredibly dangerous but doable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem being nobody will believe him after the scene even if a non sleepwalker wouldn't be affected by hearing such madness. Then you have the problem of the hunted becoming the hunter that I mentioned earlier because even without mucking up your communication it's too slow and you start at ground zero every single time if they aren't sleepwalkers themselves. With the issue of having a mage hunting them if you manage to get in the way of her business. One pissed off, obsessed mage. Obsessed about you and yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T11:00:47-08:00","id":779091,"title":"","content":"I like the more clear division of the Free Council from the rest of the Orders, and improved playability for Seer characters. I also like the expansion of antagonists, and hope we get playable support in future books. For some, at least, as obviously some don't have concepts that really lend themselves to PCs. Incorporating Mage Sight into inherent abilities is a nice touch and fits with the overall theme of second edition, where they seem to want to give you a bunch of abilities out of the box naturally so your character feels more like what they're supposed to, rather than a mortal who can do some extra stuff if you buy it. Spell permanency is a big like.<br /> <br /> The increased emphasis on obsessing over mysteries seems a little lackluster considering the scope of power and ability available to Mages, but I haven't been keeping up with all of the open development and am mostly waiting for the book to see how that pans out before flat out deciding I like or dislike it. Also while many games really appeal to me by playing off the, 'What if they're right?' idea when it comes to antagonist factions I'm not sure if Mage is getting that across as well or at all, but like the mystery thing I'd have to wait for the book to really make a decision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-03-2015, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T11:21:39-08:00","id":779108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779084#post779084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem being nobody will believe him after the scene even if a non sleepwalker wouldn't be affected by hearing such madness. Then you have the problem of the hunted becoming the hunter that I mentioned earlier because even without mucking up your communication it's too slow and you start at ground zero every single time if they aren't sleepwalkers themselves. With the issue of having a mage hunting them if you manage to get in the way of her business. One pissed off, obsessed mage. Obsessed about you and yours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I did say it would be incredibly dangerous. Anyways, he doesn't have to get them to believe anything except, &quot;This went good/bad, this is what we'll do next time.&quot; Assuming they live long enough to get a next time. I'm not arguing that Hunters stand a snowball's chance in Hell against Mages, I just got excited by if they had to try here's a way they could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T11:22:03-08:00","id":779110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779074#post779074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking walky talkies, &quot;This guy just shot a fireball at me!&quot; It's not until after the scene that Quiescence kicks in, and being informed of events second hand like that would cut out the Quiescence for the coordinator. Still risky if he hears magic over the comm system, but if it's push to talk the odds go down a lot and the coordinator can build tactical profiles on targets. More information can be gained via less than direct contact with the enemy by finding and interrogating or flipping a Mage's mortal-ish allies.<br /> <br /> Incredibly dangerous but doable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the biggest problem besides the basic tactical and practical implementation, as suggested by Kumiko, is that the Hunter witnesses will not believe the &quot;coordinator&quot; if he later suggests the other Hunters encountered magic. Trying to convince them otherwise or help them remember will cause the Quiescence to affect them again, a cycle that could easily drive them insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T11:22:59-08:00","id":779112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779069#post779069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why shouldn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no reason for it to.<br /> <br /> Everything Quisecence does to Sleepers (if successful), every role Quisence play, Lunacy does just as well. Lunacy and Quisence are absolutely equivalent to each other in fluff in purpose. If succeeding on a Quiesence check prevents the Abyss from fucking you, succeeding on a Lunacy check prevent an aspect of the Raptor from fucking you. If the Abyssal shard is integral to being a Sleeper, so is the Lunacy flight response.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":6508,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","user":"Tambov","date":". 12-03-2015, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T11:24:41-08:00","id":779113,"title":"","content":"Why would he suggest they encountered magic? I'm assuming a Hunters that are pretty close-knit group that's earned each other's trust though. Definitely making some assumptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T11:28:20-08:00","id":779118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779063#post779063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why should it be stronger than Lunacy? The latter is basically an extention of the Raptor and can be overcome (or overcome you, on dramatic failure. same difference).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Quiescence is not &quot;stronger&quot; than Lunacy, it's just different. Quiescence enforces the setting themes in Mage that do not exist, at least not to the same extent, in Werewolf, mechanical similarities between Lunacy and Quiescence notwithstanding. <br /> <br /> It's comparable to noting the nuances between a vampire's Predatory Aura and werewolf's Hunter's Aspect (and presumably mage's Nimbus).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T11:32:11-08:00","id":779122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779118#post779118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quiescence enforces the setting themes in Mage that do not exist, at least not to the same extent, in Werewolf, mechanical similarities between Lunacy and Quiescence notwithstanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Name one theme, just one, and it will invariably apply to Werewolf as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T11:36:27-08:00","id":779126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779113#post779113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would he suggest they encountered magic? I'm assuming a Hunters that are pretty close-knit group that's earned each other's trust though. Definitely making some assumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Quiescence has nothing to do what what any Hunter believes or the trust among the group. As indicated in Dave's original spoilers for the Lie and the clarification today, a Hunter that encounters a supernal or abysmal event suffers Quiescence. Anything that might reasonably remind them of the supernal event will again trigger Quiescence.<br /> <br /> It's virtually impossible to cheat the Lie, and notes, recordings, memory aids, and even crafty discussions, potentially make the problem worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T11:42:29-08:00","id":779130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779112#post779112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no reason for it to.<br /> <br /> Everything Quisecence does to Sleepers (if successful), every role Quisence play, Lunacy does just as well. Lunacy and Quisence are absolutely equivalent to each other in fluff in purpose. If succeeding on a Quiesence check prevents the Abyss from fucking you, succeeding on a Lunacy check prevent an aspect of the Raptor from fucking you. If the Abyssal shard is integral to being a Sleeper, so is the Lunacy flight response.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want an in canon explanation as to why Quiescence shouldn't tie to Willpower, how's this: If Willpower 9 &amp; 10 are what it takes to remove the lie, then a Mage only needs Mind 3 or 4 to peel back the Lie from dozens or potentially hundreds of people at a time (by boosting their Resolve &amp; Composure). That runs absolutely counter to the setting of Mage, where the lie is a massive, neigh insurmountable force that separates Mages from their sleeping friends and family.<br /> <br /> If you want to actual explanation, it's because the Devs don't bother with cross-game balance. So they would never bother to compare it to Lunacy in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T11:52:09-08:00","id":779138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779112#post779112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no reason for it to.<br /> <br /> Everything Quisecence does to Sleepers (if successful), every role Quisence play, Lunacy does just as well. Lunacy and Quisence are absolutely equivalent to each other in fluff in purpose. If succeeding on a Quiesence check prevents the Abyss from fucking you, succeeding on a Lunacy check prevent an aspect of the Raptor from fucking you. If the Abyssal shard is integral to being a Sleeper, so is the Lunacy flight response.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are in no way equivalent or the same. Lunacy is basically just humanity's primal fear of the boogeyman, the dark beyond the fire light, the things in that dark. Hence the reason it can be overcome in rare cases. Because it's just fear albeit primal fear. But fear can bargained with, contained, fought through with willpower and skill <br /> <br /> The Quiescence is curse of the soul it's not external it's literally part of your soul and cannot be bargained with on any level. It's not fear it's what makes a Sleeper a sleeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 12-03-2015, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T11:53:13-08:00","id":779140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779122#post779122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? Name one theme, just one, and it will invariably apply to Werewolf as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First, I never said that the games might not have some similar themes, but the stresses and importance of different aspects are important.<br /> <br /> In Mage, a primary theme is mages' alienation from humanity; only mages recognize the prison of the Lie. Every sleeper has a shard of the abyss infecting their very soul. This not only causes increased risk of Paradox and Dissonance, but Quiescence, a injury to the actual souls of sleepers and the absolute inability to remember supernal or abysmal effects. The Quiescence has nothing to do with willpower or resolve. It's an extra-dimensional curse upon all of sleeping Humanity.<br /> <br /> &quot;Lunacy is the deep down, ancestral fear of the wolf at the door.&quot; (p.100). It reinforces the themes of werewolves as the ultimate hunters, Werewolf's primary focus. While similar in that it alienates werewolves from humanity, it's not nearly as fundamental to the game line as the Lie is to Mage. Notably, unlike Paradox, Dissonance and Quiescence, Lunacy and other inherent aspects of Humanity do not negatively affect werewolf abilities or powers.<br /> <br /> If you require some mechanical balancing for justification, while Lunacy offers humans some opportunity to resist, it similarly offers nothing even remotely analogous to the detrimental effects of Paradox or Dissonance, which automatically affect mages without a roll to resist.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 12-03-2015, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T12:06:07-08:00","id":779150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779130#post779130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want an in canon explanation as to why Quiescence shouldn't tie to Willpower, how's this: If Willpower 9 &amp; 10 are what it takes to remove the lie, then a Mage only needs Mind 3 or 4 to peel back the Lie from dozens or potentially hundreds of people at a time (by boosting their Resolve &amp; Composure). That runs absolutely counter to the setting of Mage, where the lie is a massive, neigh insurmountable force that separates Mages from their sleeping friends and family.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, there is a spoiled spell that temporarily removes Quiescence. It also grants mage sight, but you should be able to creative thaumaturgy a spell that just removes quiescence.<br /> <br /> <b>Apocalypse (Prime 4)</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Persuasion, Socialize<br /> <b>Cost:</b> One Mana per extra Arcanum (optional)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The subject of this spell has the scales of the Lie removed from their eyes. Anyone subject to the spell, mage, Sleeper, or other supernatural being, gains Mage Sight attuned to the Aether in the manner of an Obrimos. Along with this gift comes temporary immunity to Quiescence and an instinctive knowledge of how to use Mage Sight. It does not, however, prepare the subject for how to <i>interpret</i> the visions received under Mage Sight, and the uninitiated are likely to suffer Breaking Points from the trauma of the Sight.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>Add any other Arcanum *:</b> As with her own Attainments, the mage may add her other Arcana into the Mage Sight granted by the spell, which costs one Mana per Arcanum.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/drawn-to-the-flame/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/drawn-to-the-flame/\" target=\"_blank\"> Drawn to the Flame [Mage: The Awakening] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/drawn-to-the-flame/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/drawn-to-the-flame/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","user":"solidork","date":". 12-03-2015, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T12:26:05-08:00","id":779173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779150#post779150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, there is a spoiled spell that temporarily removes Quiescence. It also grants mage sight, but you should be able to creative thaumaturgy a spell that just removes quiescence.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, though note that it is inherently traumatizing, and an all around miserable experience for the poor sleeper/sleepwalker who is subject to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T12:27:22-08:00","id":779175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779150#post779150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, there is a spoiled spell that temporarily removes Quiescence. It also grants mage sight, but you should be able to creative thaumaturgy a spell that just removes quiescence.<br /> <br /> <b>Apocalypse (Prime 4)</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Persuasion, Socialize<br /> <b>Cost:</b> One Mana per extra Arcanum (optional)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The subject of this spell has the scales of the Lie removed from their eyes. Anyone subject to the spell, mage, Sleeper, or other supernatural being, gains Mage Sight attuned to the Aether in the manner of an Obrimos. Along with this gift comes temporary immunity to Quiescence and an instinctive knowledge of how to use Mage Sight. It does not, however, prepare the subject for how to <i>interpret</i> the visions received under Mage Sight, and the uninitiated are likely to suffer Breaking Points from the trauma of the Sight.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>Add any other Arcanum *:</b> As with her own Attainments, the mage may add her other Arcana into the Mage Sight granted by the spell, which costs one Mana per Arcanum.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/drawn-to-the-flame/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/drawn-to-the-flame/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>There is an archmage experimenting with doing pretty much just that but methinks the Exarchs and their lackeys (Seers) wouldn't just stand by and let that happen if it were either long-term or without multiple breaking points every way possible for a sleeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 12-03-2015, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T12:28:35-08:00","id":779178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779150#post779150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, there is a spoiled spell that temporarily removes Quiescence. It also grants mage sight, but you should be able to creative thaumaturgy a spell that just removes quiescence.<br /> <br /> <b>Apocalypse (Prime 4)</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/drawn-to-the-flame/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/drawn-to-the-flame/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>The spell is called &quot;Apocalypse&quot; for a reason. It<i> temporarily</i> suspends the Quiescence, and likely causes more and lasting problems for the subject.<br /> <br /> There's also nothing about the spell (which is Prime, not Mind) that would suggest a higher Willpower would offer any resistance or immunity to the Quiescence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T12:38:36-08:00","id":779186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779063#post779063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why should it be stronger than Lunacy? The latter is basically an extention of the Raptor and can be overcome (or overcome you, on dramatic failure. same difference).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just as likely that Lunacy comes from Luna, and that it's part of her defence for the Uratha.<br /> If anything, it piggybacks off of the Lie.<br /> <br /> If the Raptor was behind it, all animals would probably trigger Lunacy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T12:42:07-08:00","id":779189,"title":"","content":"Does Lunacy still seriously cripple your ability to fight back in the moment? I know it grants conditions now, but don't remember what they do except for the one that makes you go berserk and attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T12:47:05-08:00","id":779196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779189#post779189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Lunacy still seriously cripple your ability to fight back in the moment? I know it grants conditions now, but don't remember what they do except for the one that makes you go berserk and attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can. Two of the three standard Conditions are responses to fear, Fight or Flight. So it's possible everyone you expose yourself to could whip out their guns and start coming for you. Another causes you to run away or turn catatonic if flight isn't possible. The last, Receptive, leaves you sort of Open to the Hisil. There are several abilities werewolves have that take advantage of the infliction of Lunacy, at least one offers another Condition that leads to awestruck worship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T12:54:51-08:00","id":779202,"title":"","content":"Dave has provided yet another 4chan comment on Quiescence,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#117743\"><b>DaveB</b></span> <span style=\"color:#117743\">!!kn3vuELOelB</span> 12/03/15(Thu)13:02:40 </span></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Remembering the false memory Quiescence left you with doesn't retrigger you. Having the flaws in it pointed out doesn't necessarily do so (although see the standard &quot;what have you forgotten&quot; Breaking Point for Integrity).<br /> <br /> &quot;Any *serious* attempt:&quot; if you uncover the truth, the Abyss bites down again.<br /> <br /> And you're nearly right. The Breaking Point is the Abyss destroying magic. The memory effects afterwards are a defense mechanism. Otherwise you'd risk integrity every time you thought about it.<br /> <br /> Which would make for an interesting Mystery. Some poor bastard who's immune to Quiescence but isn't a Sleepwalker. They'd go screamingly insane in short order.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T13:00:20-08:00","id":779203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779112#post779112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Everything Quisecence does to Sleepers (if successful), every role Quisence play, Lunacy does just as well. Lunacy and Quisence are absolutely equivalent to each other in fluff in purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>The implications of &quot;the basic premise of our reality is a Lie&quot; and &quot;all people have a capacity to become capable of changing reality&quot; go a bit deeper than &quot;werewolves are really scary (unless you've got an iron will)&quot;.<br /> <br /> An iron will should not be sufficient to remove the scales from your eyes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> succeeding on a Lunacy check prevent an aspect of the Raptor from fucking you.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are literally making this up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T13:04:24-08:00","id":779206,"title":"","content":"Perhaps in the interests of getting back on topic, people who want to talk about Quiescence could make a different thread about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T13:45:09-08:00","id":779230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779206#post779206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps in the interests of getting back on topic, people who want to talk about Quiescence could make a different thread about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, do we know anything about goetic for 2ed?<br /> <br /> I always liked goetic though i have never had a player use it, which is sad. Does it work the same way? snap fingers, summon inner demon, break it kneecaps and gain 1 WP?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T13:47:55-08:00","id":779232,"title":"","content":"I like the apparent greater emphasis on the astral in 2e, and am looking forward to more information on astral familiars. I hope they constitute more than summoning your pain or envy as a sidekick, and contains a large variety of interesting and unique options similar to Spirit familiars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T14:12:13-08:00","id":779257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779230#post779230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Okay, do we know anything about goetic for 2ed?<br /> <br /> I always liked goetic though i have never had a player use it, which is sad. Does it work the same way? snap fingers, summon inner demon, break it kneecaps and gain 1 WP?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I remember, you no longer need anything other than Mind to properly summon a goetic entity (although you do need Death or Spirit if you want to give it an ephemeral &quot;body&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T15:08:44-08:00","id":779301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779063#post779063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The latter is basically an extention of the Raptor</div> </div> </div> </div> That's, uh, news to me. I feel fairly confident that 'extention of the Raptor' didn't appear anywhere in our design docs for WtF 2e (nor did the word Exarch at all).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T15:15:59-08:00","id":779310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779301#post779301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's, uh, news to me. I feel fairly confident that 'extention of the Raptor' didn't appear anywhere in our design docs for WtF 2e (nor did the word Exarch at all).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Stew obviously didn't give you the double super-secret Mage / Werewolf crossover outline... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T15:20:57-08:00","id":779315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779310#post779310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Stew obviously didn't give you the double super-secret Mage / Werewolf crossover outline... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Too bad, this Raptor thing sounds pretty cool. I mean isn't that a great idea/concept for a Beast somewhere in there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T15:31:13-08:00","id":779326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779315#post779315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Too bad, this Raptor thing sounds pretty cool. I mean isn't that a great idea/concept for a Beast somewhere in there?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Possibly, although it has nothing to do with Werewolf Lunacy or Mage Quiescence.<br /> <br /> I don't recall, does Beast even have a Quiescence or Lunacy equivalent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T15:43:08-08:00","id":779332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779326#post779326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Possibly, although it has nothing to do with Werewolf Lunacy or Mage Quiescence.<br /> <br /> I don't recall, does Beast even have a Quiescence or Lunacy equivalent?</div> </div> </div> </div>No idea. Beast isn't my thing I just thought Raptor would make a good concept for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T15:49:22-08:00","id":779336,"title":"","content":"Beasts powers are kind of invisible to non-supernaturals. Like, if one claws you a vampire will see huge claws overlayed on their hand, but a human will just see them swipe with a normal hand and then fall over with huge claw marks on them for no apparent reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T15:57:05-08:00","id":779341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779336#post779336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts powers are kind of invisible to non-supernaturals. Like, if one claws you a vampire will see huge claws overlayed on their hand, but a human will just see them swipe with a normal hand and then fall over with huge claw marks on them for no apparent reason.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Beasts have no scary, upsetting, or amnesia-causing aura?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T16:21:54-08:00","id":779346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779038#post779038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I totally forgot that just <i>hearing</i> a supernal event will still trigger Quiescence, and thus a sleeper &quot;coordinator&quot; may still be affected using Ashenrogue's suggestion.<br /> <br /> Damn that Quiescence is nasty...</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I mentioned if this became a problem, to have it setup that all incoming speech is instead converted to text. Thus, the coordinator wouldn't even receive audio. Also, this is more for reconnaissance than anything else. I'd assume that Hunters wouldn't want to just bust in at first sight with no real preparation for what they're going after. And as someone else mentioned, push to talk is what I was assuming going in, not transmitting everything automatically, just having the people in the field report back pretty much everything they see.<br /> <br /> So at this point, the coordinator sitting back at base would have had absolutely <i>zero</i> exposure to any sort of Supernal magic. No visuals, no audio, no touch, taste, or smell. All they'd be working with are sheets of mundane paper, written on by mundane ink. And even if the events described would be unbelievable to your average joe, the guy keeping track of these things is still a Hunter. He knows there's shit out there, and without ever feeling the touch of Quiescence there's nothing to really force him to think differently. So he'd take his in-scene reports seriously, and prepare countermeasures to the things depicted within.<br /> <br /> So at this point, when the field agents go in, even if they don't consciously know what they're going to be dealing with, they'll still have all they need to be able to appropriately react to any previously gained information. Now whether they could adapt to the situation quickly enough is simply going to be a measure of the Hunters skill. They don't know what they're going into, so even though they're equipped with everything (relatively) that they'd need, if they lack the appropriate training necessary to keep cool under pressure and adapt they're pretty much dead regardless. That said, that's pretty much always been the case, so I figure if they're any good at being a Hunter at all this shouldn't be that much of an issue against mages specifically as it's already a base job prerequisite.<br /> <br /> That and the people doing recon are still going to suffer a lot of breaking point checks regardless. Larger organizations have the benefit of being able to rotate out their recon specialist to give them time to get their shit together. Small cells will obviously struggle, but that's just the usual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 12-03-2015, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T16:24:31-08:00","id":779348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779341#post779341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Beasts have no scary, upsetting, or amnesia-causing aura?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it would be boring if all the creatures had &quot;masquerade enforcing&quot; powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T16:31:51-08:00","id":779353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779346#post779346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why I mentioned if this became a problem, to have it setup that all incoming speech is instead converted to text. Thus, the coordinator wouldn't even receive audio. Also, this is more for reconnaissance than anything else. I'd assume that Hunters wouldn't want to just bust in at first sight with no real preparation for what they're going after. And as someone else mentioned, push to talk is what I was assuming going in, not transmitting everything automatically, just having the people in the field report back pretty much everything they see.<br /> <br /> So at this point, the coordinator sitting back at base would have had absolutely <i>zero</i> exposure to any sort of Supernal magic. No visuals, no audio, no touch, taste, or smell. All they'd be working with are sheets of mundane paper, written in mundane ink. And even if the events described would be unbelievable to your average joe, the guy keeping track of these things is still a Hunter. He knows there's shit out there, and without ever feeling the touch of Quiescence there's nothing to really force him to think differently. So he'd take his in scene reports seriously, and prepare countermeasures to the things depicted within.<br /> <br /> So at this point, when the field agents go in, even if they don't consciously know what they're going to be dealing with, they'll still have all they need to be able to appropriately react to any previously gained information. Now whether they could adapt to the situation quickly enough is simply going to be a measure of the Hunters skill. They don't know what they're going into, so even though they're equipped with everything (relatively) that they'd need, if they lack the appropriate training necessary to keep cool under pressure and adapt they're pretty much dead regardless. That said, that's pretty much always been the case, so I figure if they're any good this shouldn't be that much of an issue against mages specifically as it's already a base job prerequisite.<br /> <br /> That and the people doing recon are still going to suffer a lot of breaking point checks regardless. Larger organizations have the benefit of being able to rotate out their recon specialist to give them time to get their shit together. Small cells will obviously struggle, but that's just the usual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your plan is complicated, time-consuming, subject to numerous potential operational pitfalls and technological hurdles, dangerous, and I'm still not quite sure how sleeper Hunters would even have the knowledge or wherewithal about Awakened mages or the Quiescence to even formulate such a plan. However, it may indeed work, although the I'm also unsure if the benefits are worth it.<br /> <br /> I just keep seeing any mage with at least Forces 2 and the slighest tactical sense cutting-off all communication with the coordinator (and among the attacking Hunters) with the barest of effort if and when the mana hits the fan. Plans usually fall apart upon first contact with the enemy (although if the Hunters survive, they'll likely have no memory of any plan).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T17:04:17-08:00","id":779367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779353#post779353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your plan is complicated, time-consuming, subject to numerous potential operational pitfalls and technological hurdles, dangerous, and I'm still not quite sure how sleeper Hunters would even have the knowledge or wherewithal about Awakened mages or the Quiescence to even formulate such a plan. However, it may indeed work, although the I'm also unsure if the benefits are worth it.<br /> <br /> I just keep seeing any mage with at least Forces 2 and the slighest tactical sense cutting-off all communication with the coordinator (and among the attacking Hunters) with the barest of effort if and when the mana hits the fan. Plans usually fall apart upon first contact with the enemy (although if the Hunters survive, they'll likely have no memory of any plan).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Complicated? Not really. Time consuming? Not really? These are things that Hunters should be doing regardless assuming they possess the manpower. Doing recon and having someone to coordinate everyone and keep track of details is a basic step to becoming organized, and taking notes is the first step to gathering information about anything. It should become pretty obvious pretty quickly that the minds/memories of those who witness the event directly become compromised and that notes and other reminders don't really work very well. And a hunter cell that hasn't learned the value of recon is a dead hunter cell. Regardless of whether they unknowingly bust into a vampires 'haven' unaware that that vampire is the Prince, and his 'haven' is Elysium or trying to chase down someone they believed to be a mage only to find themselves lost in the Hedge as the changeling they were gunning for jukes them in the thorns, not doing your research gets people killed. <br /> <br /> As for how they'd know to do so, that's easy. The next logical step of finding out memories are being messed with is to test these things, to see if the notes and other recordings affect those who were not directly exposed. This could fairly easily be tested even on non-hunters (and assuming you want a thorough test you'll probably have to test it on non-hunters at some point regardless). Results would show that perceiving the event itself would mess with memories, but as long as direct perception isn't involved you're good. And then the Hunters spread the information around to other cells, and then even hunters who haven't specifically done these tests will know.<br /> <br /> Honestly, with as ever present an effect it is, this should be as common knowledge as fire and vampires. How would hunters know to use fire against vampires? Testing. Sure, some fictional sources list fire as a weakness, but there are just as many that don't. Someone had to test all the myths at some point, be it fire, sunlight, garlic, wooden stakes, spilled rice, whatever. Same thing here. People will do testing, and once they're pretty sure of their findings, word will spread. Hell, it was probably one of the Tier 3 organizations that figured this crap out first, but information trickles down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T17:05:40-08:00","id":779368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> although if the Hunters survive, they'll likely have no memory of any plan </div> </div> </div>What? They shouldn't lose memory of anything but the spells themselves. Why/How would they forget the plan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T17:35:23-08:00","id":779382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779126#post779126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Quiescence has nothing to do what what any Hunter believes or the trust among the group. As indicated in Dave's original spoilers for the Lie and the clarification today, a Hunter that encounters a supernal or abysmal event suffers Quiescence. Anything that might reasonably remind them of the supernal event will again trigger Quiescence.<br /> <br /> It's virtually impossible to cheat the Lie, and notes, recordings, memory aids, and even crafty discussions, potentially make the problem worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say anything about it being affected by belief. By trust I meant that the Hunters in the field would just have to take the coordinator's word for it that things went well or badly and what tactics to employ, because obviously he wouldn't be able to tell them how it all actually went down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T17:48:41-08:00","id":779389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779368#post779368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? They shouldn't lose memory of anything but the spells themselves. Why/How would they forget the plan?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the plan isn't Supernal you see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T18:16:05-08:00","id":779403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779368#post779368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? They shouldn't lose memory of anything but the spells themselves. Why/How would they forget the plan?</div> </div> </div> </div>The plan to what exactly? What the &quot;coordinator&quot; is either jabbering about or won't say anything about? The three different but similar things your team is saying happened and can't explain why the plan for what was that again? Went wrong. <br /> <br /> Why did we just make some elaborate plan for some witch that is turning people into frogs when all she's doing is cataloging and saving a protected species. Because she is some kind of animal rights activist?<br /> <br /> To be crystal clear journals, tapes, video, any kind of record of the Supernal will be affected by the Quiescence whenever a sleeper sees it or hears it. Full Stop.<br /> <br /> Tier 3 Hunters are sleepwalkers for a reason and likely supernatural themselves to boot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 12-03-2015, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T18:26:55-08:00","id":779411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779389#post779389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the plan isn't Supernal you see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why there is no reason for you to forget it.... <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The plan to what exactly? What the &quot;coordinator&quot; is either jabbering about or won't say anything about? The three different but similar things your team is saying happened and can't explain why the plan for what was that again? Went wrong. </div> </div> </div>Why would you ignore the coordinator who's whole purpose is to deal with the fact that your memory is going to be incorrect in a minute? That's just stupid. Also you can know what the plan is for, sleepers can know about magic without losing their memories, they just cannot remember when they see a spellcast in front of them and their mind Later makes up a mundane excuse for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T18:28:25-08:00","id":779414,"title":"","content":"Honestly, if there are trust issues then we're really just talking about a fairly terrible Hunter cell that likely wouldn't do very well regardless of what they were facing. Lunacy? Vampire mind fuckery? If you have a guy whose job it is to keep track of the things that you and other operatives can't necessarily be expected to accurately judge and you refuse to take their word because reasons, then you're probably going to fail and die regardless of what you're trying to hunt.<br /> <br /> Even ignoring Supernal magic, there is a lot of mind crap that can be thrown around in direct confrontation situations. I'd pretty much recommend a guy constantly outside of the field acting as a coordinator regardless of what you're trying to hunt just as a matter of course. Again, this is harder for small tier 1 cells due to lack of manpower, but they were screwed from the start regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T18:38:53-08:00","id":779428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779414#post779414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even ignoring Supernal magic, there is a lot of mind crap that can be thrown around in direct confrontation situations. I'd pretty much recommend a guy constantly outside of the field acting as a coordinator regardless of what you're trying to hunt just as a matter of course. Again, this is harder for small tier 1 cells due to lack of manpower, but they were screwed from the start regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it's specifically called out as standard practice for either Task Force Valkyrie or Cheiron.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T18:43:22-08:00","id":779432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779414#post779414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, this is harder for small tier 1 cells due to lack of manpower, but they were screwed from the start regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div>And we have come full circle. Dave's initial point was that lower tier sleeper Hunters were simply ill equipped to deal with Awakened mages (or probably any major splat). Hunter indeed accounted for this with its own monster creation system and access to multiple tiers of power, and if some brave and foolish Hunters want to focus on Awakened mages, the Quiescence can be overcome with a cheap and easy one dot merit.<br /> <br /> Now, back to begging for some spoilers about goetic familiars... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T18:43:47-08:00","id":779433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779411#post779411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why there is no reason for you to forget it.... <br /> <br /> <br /> Why would you ignore the coordinator who's whole purpose is to deal with the fact that your memory is going to be incorrect in a minute? That's just stupid. Also you can know what the plan is for, sleepers can know about magic without losing their memories, they just cannot remember when they see a spellcast in front of them and their mind Later makes up a mundane excuse for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because he's a liar and crazy. Because nobody would ever trust on the level you're positing without at least a shred of proof. And he can NEVER even try to give you that. Basically for all intents and purposes you are on a wild goose chase likely to drive you or your coordinator 100% insane quick and fast. <br /> <br /> No, sleepers cannot know about magic after the fact because to be forced to means the Quiescence kicks in again and they suffer another breaking point just like new. So just be a sleepwalker and problem solved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 12-03-2015, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T18:53:36-08:00","id":779439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779428#post779428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe it's specifically called out as standard practice for either Task Force Valkyrie or Cheiron.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which are mostly if not all sleepwalkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T18:55:41-08:00","id":779441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779433#post779433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because he's a liar and crazy. Because nobody would ever trust on the level you're positing without at least a shred of proof. And he can NEVER even try to give you that. Basically for all intents and purposes you are on a wild goose chase likely to drive you or your coordinator 100% insane quick and fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except Hunters know there are mind effects that can mess with a persons memory. They know this for a fact. Hell, the conflicting reports of what happened in the initial confrontation by the people who were there (because I'm fairly sure that it has never been stated that everyone remembers events the exact same way) and memory blanks are enough to justify having an outside guy doing the information handling.<br /> <br /> This is why a hunter cell should recruit someone explicitly for this purpose. This isn't just some random guy who doesn't know anything. This is The Coordinator, the guy who keeps shit straight even when half the group thinks they were all trounced by a guy on steroids wearing a Barney the Dinosaur costume while the other half are arguing it was someone cosplaying Dr. Mundo. This is the guy you trust above all else, even your own memories, because you <i>know for a fact</i> that with the things you face your own mind isn't even safe from being tampered with.<br /> <br /> And I'm fairly certain that given a few missions without such a person having their back, they'll reconsider their choice not to listen, because people will <i>die.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 12-03-2015, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T19:01:06-08:00","id":779450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779439#post779439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which are mostly if not all sleepwalkers.</div> </div> </div> </div>In first edition that wasn't as much of a burden and it's too soon to say what they are in second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T19:10:46-08:00","id":779455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779450#post779450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In first edition that wasn't as much of a burden and it's too soon to say what they are in second.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a 1 dot merit in 2e. So this whole conversation is silly in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T19:19:08-08:00","id":779468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779433#post779433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because he's a liar and crazy. Because nobody would ever trust on the level you're positing without at least a shred of proof. And he can NEVER even try to give you that. Basically for all intents and purposes you are on a wild goose chase likely to drive you or your coordinator 100% insane quick and fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. If you don't trust your fellow cellmates to the extent your saying, then you should leave the cell, you are a liability.<br /> 2. The fact that everyone has different memories is proof.<br /> 3. The fact that you probably just acted on the mage casting a spell before you &quot;realized&quot; that the lightning bolt was actually a bullet, since the curse doesn't seem immediate, meaning the hunters would probably notice they're acting strange.<br /> 4. You probably already know a bit about the supernal if your hunting a mage, so you likely know that your memories are going to be weird (You know, the whole reason why their is a coordinator...)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, sleepers cannot know about magic after the fact because to be forced to means the Quiescence kicks in again and they suffer another breaking point just like new. So just be a sleepwalker and problem solved. </div> </div> </div>They can know about mages externally, they just cannot remember the specific instance of a spell. There are organizations in 2e for the Orders which have sleepwalkers in them that are aware of magic, but just ensure that they never witness it occurring because they have been told it will damage their mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T19:19:26-08:00","id":779469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779441#post779441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except Hunters know there are mind effects that can mess with a persons memory. They know this for a fact. Hell, the conflicting reports of what happened in the initial confrontation by the people who were there (because I'm fairly sure that it has never been stated that everyone remembers events the exact same way) and memory blanks are enough to justify having an outside guy doing the information handling.<br /> <br /> This is why a hunter cell should recruit someone explicitly for this purpose. This isn't just some random guy who doesn't know anything. This is The Coordinator, the guy who keeps shit straight even when half the group thinks they were all trounced by a guy on steroids wearing a Barney the Dinosaur costume while the other half are arguing it was someone cosplaying Dr. Mundo. This is the guy you trust above all else, even your own memories, because you <i>know for a fact</i> that with the things you face your own mind isn't even safe from being tampered with.<br /> <br /> And I'm fairly certain that given a few missions without such a person having their back, they'll reconsider their choice not to listen, because people will <i>die.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>It's not like memory gaps like vampires. It's basically they have their explanation and no reason to hunt beyond some guy talking gibberish with no physical proof that conflicts in any way with their memories that have NO gaps. .<br /> Unless they're sleepwalkers which means they're tier 3 Hunters or better be. Because just being a sleepwalker and a tier 1 hunter will do nothing but get you killed because they would know they don't have the resources in most cases. Plus the fact that if they are sleepwalkers the tier 3 Hunters will get them in the fold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 12-03-2015, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T19:25:29-08:00","id":779474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not like memory gaps like vampires. It's basically they have their explanation and no reason to hunt beyond some guy talking gibberish with no physical proof that conflicts in any way with their memories that have NO gaps. </div> </div> </div>I'm relatively sure guns don't normally leave burn marks rather than bullet holes. Things like that are the proof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T19:27:18-08:00","id":779477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779469#post779469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not like memory gaps like vampires. It's basically they have their explanation and no reason to hunt beyond some guy talking gibberish with no physical proof that conflicts in any way with their memories that have NO gaps. .<br /> Unless they're sleepwalkers which means they're tier 3 Hunters or better be. Because just being a sleepwalker and a tier 1 hunter will do nothing but get you killed because they would know they don't have the resources in most cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for when they can't find a way to fill in the gap with something mundane, in which case it is just blank. And you don't <i>need</i> to be a Sleepwalker to be an effective Hunter, it just makes things easier. Not being a Sleepwalker might restricts what you'd generally be doing a bit, sure, but even that restriction can be ignored, just with consequences. I really don't think Sleepwalkers are the majority when it comes to Hunters of any tier, though I do think the chances of there being a Sleepwalker in a given group of Hunters possibly increases the higher up you go in tiers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 12-03-2015, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T19:41:06-08:00","id":779485,"title":"","content":"Basically accept the fact a Hunter that isn't a sleepwalker are not equipped to hunt Awakened Mages. It's basically as simple as that. So stop bitching and trying to invent unrealistic workarounds and take a 1 dot merit available to all sleepers and move on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T19:51:37-08:00","id":779494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779477#post779477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except for when they can't find a way to fill in the gap with something mundane, in which case it is just blank. And you don't <i>need</i> to be a Sleepwalker to be an effective Hunter, it just makes things easier. Not being a Sleepwalker might restricts what you'd generally be doing a bit, sure, but even that restriction can be ignored, just with consequences. I really don't think Sleepwalkers are the majority when it comes to Hunters of any tier, though I do think the chances of there being a Sleepwalker in a given group of Hunters possibly increases the higher up you go in tiers.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it can't. It's nothing like the Masquerade which is entirely a socio-political agreement or Lunacy which is Primal Fear. Both of which can be fought against by willpower, talent, skill and information.<br /> <br /> It's curse that is soul deep that the people in charge of the prison do not want changed EVER. It literally erases all evidence of any form or any kind if you are a sleeper Because the Masters of reality want it so. DEAL WITH IT and become a sleepwalker. And yes if you're tier 3 and actually equipped to hunt Awakened Mages you are in fact a sleepwalker. That level Conspiracy requires it just to enter.<br /> <br /> Given Awakened Mages and MtAw operate on tier 3 at the least it makes total sense that if you want to hunt them you at least better be able to see magic and the world as it really is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 12-03-2015, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T20:00:29-08:00","id":779501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779494#post779494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's curse that is soul deep that the people in charge of the prison do not want changed EVER. It literally erases all evidence of any form or any kind if you are a sleeper Because the Masters of reality want it so. DEAL WITH IT and become a sleepwalker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it doesn't say that it erases all the evidence, it only been said that it erases the memory of the spell itself being cast. Also we know from leaks that there are sleepers who are aware of the supernal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yes if you're tier 3 and actually equipped to hunt Awakened Mages you are in fact a sleepwalker. That level Conspiracy requires it just to enter. </div> </div> </div>Where are you getting this impression at all? I haven't seen anything that suggests it. There are conspiracies like Luciferge that are sleepwalkers because they are physiologically supernatural, but there is nothing at all that suggests Aegis, valkyrie, etc. are sleepwalkers at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T20:11:34-08:00","id":779504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779501#post779501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except it doesn't say that it erases all the evidence, it only been said that it erases the memory of the spell itself being cast. Also we know from leaks that there are sleepers who are aware of the supernal.<br /> <br /> <br /> Where are you getting this impression at all? I haven't seen anything that suggests it. There are conspiracies like Luciferge that are sleepwalkers because they are physiologically supernatural, but there is nothing at all that suggests Aegis, valkyrie, etc. are sleepwalkers at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, sleepers are not aware of the Supernal. What don't you get from they will either go insane or rationalize any form of the Supernal away into something mundane or if dissonance doesn't just destroy anything meant to last? To interact or fight something you have to accept it at the very least and actually see it to actually effect it.<br /> <br /> Example, the Kindred know and accept that spirits and the Shadow exist but the vast majority don't have the tools to either interact, fight against or defend themselves against either.<br /> <br /> Much like sleeper Hunters vs Awakened Mages but worse in the case of those Hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 12-03-2015, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T20:17:18-08:00","id":779506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779504#post779504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, sleepers are not aware of the Supernal. What don't you get from they will either go insane or rationalize any form of the Supernal away into something mundane or if dissonance doesn't just destroy anything meant to last?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are sleepers aware of the supernal, the blog post thing said there are organizations with sleeper members in it who are aware.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T20:26:45-08:00","id":779508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779506#post779506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are sleepers aware of the supernal, the blog post thing said there are organizations with sleeper members in it who are aware.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right but they can't interact with it on any level without dissonance and quiescence kicking in whenever appropriate.<br /> <br /> Where Hunters are involved that means dead Hunters because even without screwing with their information their command and control is too slow for real time combat against an Awakened Mage. Unless they're sleepwalkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 12-03-2015, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T20:28:43-08:00","id":779511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779508#post779508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right but they can't interact with it on any level without dissonance and quiescence kicking in whenever appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fail to see how that's an issue with the coordinator idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T20:49:13-08:00","id":779516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779494#post779494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it can't. It's nothing like the Masquerade which is entirely a socio-political agreement or Lunacy which is Primal Fear. Both of which can be fought against by willpower, talent, skill and information.<br /> <br /> It's curse that is soul deep that the people in charge of the prison do not want changed EVER. It literally erases all evidence of any form or any kind if you are a sleeper Because the Masters of reality want it so. DEAL WITH IT and become a sleepwalker. And yes if you're tier 3 and actually equipped to hunt Awakened Mages you are in fact a sleepwalker. That level Conspiracy requires it just to enter.<br /> <br /> Given Awakened Mages and MtAw operate on tier 3 at the least it makes total sense that if you want to hunt them you at least better be able to see magic and the world as it really is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it doesn't need to be. I don't <i>need</i> to see you cast magic to shoot you dead in your face. I don't <i>need</i> to see you cast magic to know you <i>can</i> cast magic. I don't <i>need</i> to see you cast magic to track you down. I don't <i>need</i> to see you cast magic to <i>Hunt</i> you. <i>Period</i>. End of discussion. There is nothing you can say to counter this, it is all fact.<br /> <br /> I don't need to be a Sleepwalker to know you're a mage, track you down, and kill you. There is nothing about Quiescence that prevents me from doing any of those things. It does <i>not</i> change evidence, it does <i>not</i> change fact, it does not do <i>anything </i>except prevent a person from remembering magic as magic. But even if a person doesn't remember magic as magic, it doesn't mean they can't figure out from circumstantial evidence, because circumstantial evidence is not changed by Quiescence, that you are able to cast magic. They don't need to be able to remember what you did to know you did something.<br /> <br /> Another thing to keep in mind is that it only alters the memories of people who have memories of the magic itself to begin with. If, while you are perceiving magic, you tell someone else who can't perceive it what it is you are seeing, even after you've been made to forget it yourself the person you told will remember what you told them. What you tell people while witnessing magic is not magic itself and is thus not susceptible to Quiescence. So with this in mind, if you set up a system similar to what I proposed earlier, there is <i>nothing</i> about the Sleeping Curse as we know it that would interfere with that. Is it flawless? No. Is it foolproof? No, But nothing is flawless and foolproof, not even magic. Which seems to be something you need to learn.<br /> <br /> So as I've said, no, you do <i>not</i> need to be a Sleepwalker to hunt a mage. There are so many ways to off an unsuspecting mage it isn't even funny. Without knowing it's coming and time to prepare, mages are nothing but human, and just as easy to take out as any Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 12-03-2015, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T21:40:58-08:00","id":779533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779516#post779516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except it doesn't need to be. I don't <i>need</i> to see you cast magic to shoot you dead in your face. I don't <i>need</i> to see you cast magic to know you <i>can</i> cast magic. I don't <i>need</i> to see you cast magic to track you down. I don't <i>need</i> to see you cast magic to <i>Hunt</i> you. <i>Period</i>. End of discussion. There is nothing you can say to counter this, it is all fact.<br /> <br /> I don't need to be a Sleepwalker to know you're a mage, track you down, and kill you. There is nothing about Quiescence that prevents me from doing any of those things. It does <i>not</i> change evidence, it does <i>not</i> change fact, it does not do <i>anything </i>except prevent a person from remembering magic as magic. But even if a person doesn't remember magic as magic, it doesn't mean they can't figure out from circumstantial evidence, because circumstantial evidence is not changed by Quiescence, that you are able to cast magic. They don't need to be able to remember what you did to know you did something.<br /> <br /> Another thing to keep in mind is that it only alters the memories of people who have memories of the magic itself to begin with. If, while you are perceiving magic, you tell someone else who can't perceive it what it is you are seeing, even after you've been made to forget it yourself the person you told will remember what you told them. What you tell people while witnessing magic is not magic itself and is thus not susceptible to Quiescence. So with this in mind, if you set up a system similar to what I proposed earlier, there is <i>nothing</i> about the Sleeping Curse as we know it that would interfere with that. Is it flawless? No. Is it foolproof? No, But nothing is flawless and foolproof, not even magic. Which seems to be something you need to learn.<br /> <br /> So as I've said, no, you do <i>not</i> need to be a Sleepwalker to hunt a mage. There are so many ways to off an unsuspecting mage it isn't even funny. Without knowing it's coming and time to prepare, mages are nothing but human, and just as easy to take out as any Hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure you can if you actually have a damn reason beyond murder? <br /> <br /> Say I'm a mage and you are a sleeper hunter. Tell me why or how you have a clue about me? <br /> <br /> I'm waiting...remember I'm not fire balling sleepers, or mind controlling city officials. I'm just telling people their true fate and healing stray animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 12-04-2015, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T21:56:27-08:00","id":779540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779511#post779511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fail to see how that's an issue with the coordinator idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has everything to do with said mythical coordinator and you and I know it. Don't be mad just accept it's silly and any mage worth a damn would make your ignorant cell pay and recruit your coordinator for herself while killing you if she didn't actually care about you. <br /> <br /> Your whole plan is child's play to fuck over to any mage's desire that has Forces 2. All covert no less. Sleeper Hunters just aren't equipped for any mage that isn't stupid and soft. And since mages aren't usually either I guess you better have a Plan B.<br /> <br /> Because any mage worth the name has a Plan A/B/C at the least. It's what they are and do. They hunt out, find and hopefully solve mysteries. In any and all permutations.<br /> <br /> Say I'm that mage those poor bastards targeted...I'd mess their communications up while using said communications to find their over watch, turn invisible, leave the scene, and introduce myself to your coordinator without you knowing anything. No obvious magic beyond the first volley. No paradox. Forces is no joke in a world built on technology and science. Fate is just awesome when hacking and Prime is truth. A truth that the coordinator can and will accept unlike any sleeper Hunter unless said mage wanted to harm said Hunters.<br /> <br /> Pretty much all that I mentioned is totally doable by a newbie Obrimos. God help you if you're hunting an experienced mage. An adept with Forces would be able to kill a typical Hunter cell with one spell. Literally hit you before you had a chance to strike given sniping isn't a great idea against a mage with Forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 12-04-2015, 01:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T22:46:09-08:00","id":779562,"title":"","content":"I love this. It never ends","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T23:15:08-08:00","id":779571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779562#post779562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love this. It never ends</div> </div> </div> </div>Just grab the popcorn and enjoy reading Kumiko`s crusade in white knighting mages.....not mage the game, or even the author....it has descended into &quot;ZOMG MAGE SPLAT MUST RULZ!!!!!&quot;. The level of chauvinism that those answers have degraded by now, are utterly fascinating.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779562#post779562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm waiting...remember I'm not fire balling sleepers, or mind controlling city officials. I'm just telling people their true fate and healing stray animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the botton of the barrel by now. If you all remember, i whom argue most against the Quiessence for, beside it status as unecesary heavy handed measure, the fact that a classic theme of mage is the abuse of power, then the classic story of:<br /> <br /> Mage abuse human with magic because he think he is superior, human take it but of all who do one plan and execute a plan that make said mage eat his teeth. Classic story of abuse of power and hubris that quiessence completely negated unless one resorts to supernatural merit or supernatural hunters.<br /> <br /> So that mage kumiko examples is not the point of said plot. Does it really diminish that much that a mage can lose a fight? I honestly feel bad for you that the idea of a mage losing against any other thing that is not a mage hurts your enjoyment of the game. You can house rule that mages win always and everything can be fine <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T23:20:38-08:00","id":779572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779562#post779562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love this. It never ends</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I tagged-out awhile ago.<br /> <br /> Everyone offered their opinion, nothing at this point is going to change, and Dave provided some clarifications. It's time to move on before it get nasty.<br /> <br /> Besides, contentious debates are not conducive to beseeching Dave for more spoilers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T00:02:17-08:00","id":779585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779341#post779341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Beasts have no scary, upsetting, or amnesia-causing aura?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, they have to do it the hard way. That's how they feed after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T00:27:58-08:00","id":779599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779585#post779585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, they have to do it the hard way. That's how they feed after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>How uncivilized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T00:36:26-08:00","id":779602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779533#post779533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure you can if you actually have a damn reason beyond murder?<br /> <br /> Say I'm a mage and you are a sleeper hunter. Tell me why or how you have a clue about me?<br /> <br /> I'm waiting...remember I'm not fire balling sleepers, or mind controlling city officials. I'm just telling people their true fate and healing stray animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've had reports of weird things going on in your neighborhood, some sort of alleged prophet and healer. We'd heard that it was all through some nutty chinese herbalism bullshit but we sen't someone down to investigate anyways, just in case. Odd thing is, when we surveyed people we'd seen come and go, we couldn't seem to get any sort of consensus on what was being done, just that it worked. So, just to be sure we set up a few small recording devices around where you lived, and areas in which you frequented. The evidence we gained is fairly damnable.<br /> <br /> We'd raided witches before and have a bit of a database of terms and jargon you all love to use collected from various books and notes the dead monsters left behind, and lady, we've caught you with quite a few of em. Now, this alone isn't <i>quite</i> enough to send you to the gallows, well, for our cell specifically, some would have killed you over this alone. No, the real nail in the coffin is the company you keep. A sister cell a bit further up state has been dealing with a man known as Laurence McCallister. You know Laurence, don't you? Turns out Laurence has been starting all kinds of trouble. Obvious trouble. Obvious trouble that leaves a trail so wide a two year old could follow it, assuming the two year old wasn't scared away by the bodies.<br /> <br /> You and Laurence had a few choice words the other day, yes, yes, we were listening in even then. We heard everything. And we know you and him don't get along very well, and honestly, you've not done anything to really warrant what you're going to get, but we have to make sure. There have been a <i>lot</i> of witches who seemed to be fairly nice, upstanding people until you dug a little deeper and found the skeletons. I wonder what we'll find out about you once this is all over with.<br /> <br /> Also, those connected to you are also being put under investigation under suspicion of being witches. For their sake, lets hope they come up clean.<br /> <br /> This would be to argument you would have been provided if the Hunters hadn't just gunned you down out of nowhere, putting enough lead in your body that, assuming you had lived, would have allowed you to walk around unharmed while juggling 6 lbs. of uranium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T01:42:17-08:00","id":779621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779599#post779599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How uncivilized.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the word you're looking for is &quot;beastly&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T01:53:45-08:00","id":779624,"title":"","content":"The strange thing for hunting witches - you locate one by <b>having problem with remembering</b> what bad it done to you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> But <i>surely</i> you will know it done it - by making your Integrity lower you are more than sure, even if evidence are murky... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T02:47:27-08:00","id":779643,"title":"","content":"Hunters can't actually see their own character sheet, y'know. In game &quot;I lost integrity&quot; isn't quite so obvious a thing to see. Especially when you don't remember the event that caused it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T03:07:07-08:00","id":779649,"title":"","content":"Well, the Integrity loss itself maybe not ready aparent, but the asociated Conditions are. You know you expererienced something that you cannot remeber clearly that shoock you to the core.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I still can wrap my mind around what the problem is with taking the Sleepwalker Merit. I mean, that only represents that you are a regular human as humans were suposed to be, being a Sleepwalker doesn't make your character supernatural. I cannot but see it as a natural progression of the Vigil, first you refuse to make-beliebe that everything was alright with the world because it was ovbious there where monsters out there and at some point the scales fall completly and you ditch the Curse of Quiescence and the enforced ignorance that goes with it. Free your mind and the soul will follow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 12-04-2015, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T03:50:58-08:00","id":779673,"title":"","content":"I doubt Quiescence leaves enough of a gap in memory to leave a hole to question. It would suck if it did since prodding at it would cause it to scrub your soul with sandpaper again and again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T05:45:15-08:00","id":779733,"title":"","content":"I think just the disparity between various witnesses memory is enough to varant suspicion.<br /> <br /> - &quot;We nearly got him but he jumped though the open window&quot;<br /> - &quot;Wait i thought the window was closed&quot;<br /> &lt;beat&gt;<br /> - &quot;Vile witch screwed with our memories! Time for blood&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T06:22:16-08:00","id":779748,"title":"","content":"To just point out what Dave has already said and others have already posted in this forum (once more):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> DaveB !!kn3vuELOelB 12/03/15(Thu)05:50:08<br /> <br /> In the scene directly following exposure to the Supernal or Abyssal, a Sleeper forgets what she saw, or else changes how she remembers it toward the mundane. Any serious attempt to prod at those false memories, bring them into question, or correct them with magic trigger a breaking point as if she were witnessing the traumatic event again for the first time, followed by the memory being removed again. It is as harrowing in memory is it is in reality. Quiescence, like Dissonance, is not limited to the spells of mages; Sleepers\u2019 memories are clouded by the interior of ruins of the Time Before, the presence of the Mad, Emanation Realms, and sighting Supernal or Abyssal entities.<br /> <br /> Pretty much any Hunter tactic to take notes, record what's happening, or prod at Quiescence because you think a mage is nearby will put you on a one-way train to Crazytown, Paranoia. population: you.<br /> <br /> Unless I can interest you in this shiny one-dot Merit called &quot;Sleepwalker&quot;... </div> </div> </div>So:<ul><li>Memory's can be <u>wiped clean (i.e. a gap in your memory</u> or they can <u>become re-written to explain away the magic a of a scene to be mundane</u>.</li> <li> it is the trauma of seeing magic that causes the integrity loss, and the memory warping or repression is a means to protect the sleepers mind from further harm.</li> <li> Mentioning offhand won't trigger any issues, but forcing a confrontation between the warped memory/lack of it and reality so as to make someone aware of what happened causes the trauma to re-occur and the defenses to kick back in (i.e. integrity loss and memory alteration). This includes reviewing notes, having someone tell you, watching a video, etc.</li> <li>it is not just obvious magic, but essentially anything of the abyss or supernal, that causes this damage and forces the memory changes in the sleeper to allow them to stay sane(-ish).</li> <li> Dave state a Hunter who wants to investigate and see supernal magic needs the sleepwalker merit, or will face this memory loss, or insanity if they try to overcome it.</li> </ul><br /> There is also specific mention in another Dave post that the trauma is due to the Abyss response to the act of experiencing the Supernal (or being forced to re-experience it) and if someone didn't forget but still had the abyssal shard, they would quickly go insane from seeing an act and then reliving it (and sufferingthe corresponding trauma) again and again. <br /> <br /> Here is what I get from this:<ul><li> It sucks to be a mage. Sure, you have this nice added hammer to the fireball you throw at those annoying sleepers (if you are willing to take a Wisdom hit, at least), but it means you can't use obvious magic around anyone with out mind raping them and warping their memory. So all your friends and family? Unless you lucked out to be born into a bunch of sleepwalker/Proximi, expect to never be able to reveal anything unless you want to traumatize dear old mom and dad (and then have them forget anyway). Save that school bus if kids by blasting the rampaging demon back into the Shadow? Great, you just ripped up their souls a bit and no one will remember your heroics (beyond maybe being the weirdo who ran into a bus and shot a wierd bear with a rocket launcher, or something). Heck, it means Mages trying to investigate such an attack cannot ask witnesses of it info and get anything accurate without traumatizing the sleepers again. Mages are walking Cthullus who reveal themselves anytime they reveal their power, and even the memory of what <br /> <br /> Essentially, the weirdness censor around mages hurts everyone, not just hunters, including sometimes the mage themselves (for the Wisdom risk). If Dresden followed Mage rules, half of Chicago likely would have gone insane by now with warped recollections of days worth of memories.</li> <li> That said, we know sleepers can help and participate in the Orders, and even know someone is a mage/can do magic. They don't forget that or go into shock from it. This points to the fact that while obvious magic, along with everything abyssal and supernal, is shielded by the curse, knowledge about such things can be learned. A sleeper could know their master needs a virgin sacrifice for a spell and deliver her/him to the mage, and later clean up the mess. Their master could explain that said sacrifice will let them cast a spell assuring their enemies lie in ruin, and then the sleeper hears about the mysterious death across town of a powerful gangster. But if they saw the spell itself being cast, or witnessed the effects, it likely would be scrubbed from their mind.</li> <li>Dave has given us the answer to what you can do if you want Hunters to have means to remember: take the merit. And considering its cost versus all the damage you could take from not buying it, it seems like a no brainer, especially since the first encounter with obvious magic would likely earn a good number of beats in my game, especially with the trauma component).</li> </ul><br /> So, can sleeper Hunters hunt an Awakened? Sure. It just means that Mages are not going to be tracked by sleepers for the big, showy acts, but by patterns that form around them: the guy who is way to lucky, the person who seems to always know what people want, the guy who walked away from a car crash for the 4th time in as many years. Their going to note the circles they associate with, the tools and oddities. They will track manifests and disappearances. They can investigate the outcomes of scenes and put together potential magical explanations for the outcomes. While they may be pretty damn certain, they will never be able to have concrete certainty as any obvious magic they witness will be scrubbed from memory, any evidence drying their brain again and again.<br /> <br /> What this means is that Hunters who are not sleepwalker will have to hunt mages on circumstantial evidence, rather than concrete proof (as such proof causes insanity and memory issues). So that guy you shot from across the street could be a Mage, or just a mortal occultist who happened to get lucky.<br /> <br /> TL;DNR: Awakened Mages won't be obviously magical, as subtle magic is... subtle, and obvious magic causes memory re-writes and mind rape. It doesn't mean they don't leave mundane evidence and can't be tracked, it just means a Hunter will never be certain except in a scene where they are directly exposed to any obvious magic, and hunting mages without the sleepwalker merit is not good for one's sanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T06:30:54-08:00","id":779752,"title":"","content":"Of course, hunters going insane is the leading source of what is planned to be the focus antagonist for them in 2e, so clearly a fair few non-sleepwalker hunters do try the recording method, to mixed results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T07:45:44-08:00","id":779803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779733#post779733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think just the disparity between various witnesses memory is enough to varant suspicion.<br /> <br /> - &amp;quot;We nearly got him but he jumped though the open window&amp;quot;<br /> - &amp;quot;Wait i thought the window was closed&amp;quot;<br /> &lt;beat&gt;<br /> - &amp;quot;Vile witch screwed with our memories! Time for blood&amp;quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's pretty normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T08:04:04-08:00","id":779817,"title":"","content":"Do we know if a sleeper has a breaking point for every single spell cast, or is it limited to one per scene and they roll it at the end when they forget?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T08:33:02-08:00","id":779836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779817#post779817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know if a sleeper has a breaking point for every single spell cast, or is 