uote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779748#post779748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Save that school bus if kids by blasting the rampaging demon back into the Shadow? Great, you just ripped up their souls a bit and no one will remember your heroics (beyond maybe being the weirdo who ran into a bus and shot a wierd bear with a rocket launcher, or something).</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew bears with arms were a bad idea... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 12-04-2015, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T11:31:02-08:00","id":779978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I knew bears with arms were a bad idea... </div> </div> </div>Not at all. We just need good bear with arms to counter them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T11:35:45-08:00","id":779986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779978#post779978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not at all. We just need good bears with arms to counter them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's a Thyrsus character idea in there somewhere (or a very cool magath spirit) ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T12:47:37-08:00","id":780063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779432#post779432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now, back to begging for some spoilers about goetic familiars... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This confuses me, do they change how goetic familiar works in 2ed? In 1st you could only have a goetic familiar by finding the burning book in the astral that taught how to do it from the grimoire book. Do they change it?<br /> <br /> Also, anyone ever had a player who pick the merits, goetic familiar, multiple familiar and use goetic inversion from encounter of the abyss? You know, little evil and angel on your shoulders :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T13:00:27-08:00","id":780072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780063#post780063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This confuses me, do they change how goetic familiar works in 2ed? In 1st you could only have a goetic familiar by finding the burning book in the astral that taught how to do it from the grimoire book. Do they change it?<br /> <br /> Also, anyone ever had a player who pick the merits, goetic familiar, multiple familiar and use goetic inversion from encounter of the abyss? You know, little evil and angel on your shoulders :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Based on the spoilers, Dave's comments, the renewed focus on the Astral, and the need to comply with GMC's new ephemeral entity manifestation rules, mage familiars seem to have been completely revised in 2e.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T14:10:04-08:00","id":780113,"title":"","content":"&quot;Too cool to bother with the sidequest&quot; was basically my immediate thought on it when I read that book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T14:47:45-08:00","id":780150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779971#post779971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> After Hunter #2 suggested a witch altered their memories, wouldn't the Quiescence trigger again forcing more breaking point rolls and amnesia or rationalizations?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I knew bears with arms were a bad idea... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say only if they tried to remember what actually happened. Just suspecting/assuming that something was amiss without actually delving into what really happened should arguably be fine. Daves spoiler did say any 'serious' attempt to prod at their memories would result in another breaking point, so without going further into the 'well what really did happen?' line of questioning and actually attempting to remember I'd think it should be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T15:23:38-08:00","id":780171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=779803#post779803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that's pretty normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every sane and non-paranoid person would dismiss it and think they misremembered. But we're talking about Hunters, sane and non-paranoid isn't exactly typical for the occupation.<br /> <br /> @up: got the same impression. As long as they don't try too hard to remember it shouldn't provoke breaking points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","user":"Menace","date":". 12-04-2015, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T15:52:46-08:00","id":780187,"title":"","content":"See, there is a bit of a of Catch-22 here if you don't have the (possibly meta-)knowledge that focusing too hard and remembering things causes rewrites: if you don't pay any mind to the inconsistencies or gaps, you probably aren't bothering to investigate the target; but if you are going to pursue the gaps/inconsistent nature of memories, it is unlikely you aren't also going to try to figure out what made you forget. It is only basic human nature (think about anytime you know you forgot something that you know is important...did you just let it go?). Remember, sleepers don't know that simply seeing magic causes memory alterations (which is more common than just gaps, per Dave- memory gaps only occur if there is no way to explain away what was seen); they could easily assume someone used magic to make them forget to hide emir misdeeds or used the memory wiper device from MIB (or whatever) to make them forget something, and then go chasing down that rabbit hole of psychic harm and memory corruption again and again.<br /> <br /> It would only be if your group observed someone trying to recall and saw the damage unfold in front of them that you could get around this, as said group might note that learning too much causes a reset. But that is asking someone to undergo further mental harm for","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T16:19:59-08:00","id":780209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780187#post780187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, there is a bit of a of Catch-22 here if you don't have the (possibly meta-)knowledge that focusing too hard and remembering things causes rewrites: if you don't pay any mind to the inconsistencies or gaps, you probably aren't bothering to investigate the target; but if you are going to pursue the gaps/inconsistent nature of memories, it is unlikely you aren't also going to try to figure out what made you forget. It is only basic human nature (think about anytime you know you forgot something that you know is important...did you just let it go?). Remember, sleepers don't know that simply seeing magic causes memory alterations (which is more common than just gaps, per Dave- memory gaps only occur if there is no way to explain away what was seen); they could easily assume someone used magic to make them forget to hide emir misdeeds or used the memory wiper device from MIB (or whatever) to make them forget something, and then go chasing down that rabbit hole of psychic harm and memory corruption again and again.<br /> <br /> It would only be if your group observed someone trying to recall and saw the damage unfold in front of them that you could get around this, as said group might note that learning too much causes a reset. But that is asking someone to undergo further mental harm for</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think a lot will depend on the specific circumstances, as well as prior agreement between the ST and group about just how hard they want Quiescence to bite.<br /> <br /> However, that Hunter cell certainly will have their work cut out for them now that they know rocket launcher-carrying bears might be gunning for them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T17:41:31-08:00","id":780257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780209#post780209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think a lot will depend on the specific circumstances, as well as prior agreement between the ST and group about just how hard they want Quiescence to bite.<br /> <br /> However, that Hunter cell certainly will have their work cut out for them now that they know rocket launcher-carrying bears might be gunning for them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>True, but I meant from a story perspective, there would be no way for sleeper investigators who weren't taught by a mage or who specifically studied said effects would know.<br /> <br /> And you aren't going to let that poor word order go, huh? :P Well, I am glad to have said something memorable <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T17:59:18-08:00","id":780266,"title":"","content":"You don't need to be taught by a mage or to have personally studied the effects of Quiescence to know about it. Assuming a group of Hunters somewhere at some point in time has done the necessary tests to figure out exactly how these things work, chances are the information is going to be spread around for other groups to access it. So assuming we aren't talking about a completely green group of Hunters with literally no contact with any other group or access to even online sources at least the basics of this shouldn't be that much more obscure than the general weaknesses and powers of other supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T18:06:01-08:00","id":780271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780257#post780257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but I meant from a story perspective, there would be no way for sleeper investigators who weren't taught by a mage or who specifically studied said effects would know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> And you aren't going to let that poor word order go, huh? :P Well, I am glad to have said something memorable <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Let it go? Heck, no! I fully support the constitutional, god-given right to arm bears in the nWOD. In fact, I've been told the best way to stop bad, sanity-destroying mages is a good bear with gun.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I now fully intend to find some way to incorporate armed bears in my next mage campaign. They can be crytids, spirits or magath, goetia, strange shapeshfters, or something else, but nothing says &quot;don't f@uck with me&quot; like Smokey with heavy armaments. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T18:38:15-08:00","id":780290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780266#post780266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need to be taught by a mage or to have personally studied the effects of Quiescence to know about it. Assuming a group of Hunters somewhere at some point in time has done the necessary tests to figure out exactly how these things work, chances are the information is going to be spread around for other groups to access it. So assuming we aren't talking about a completely green group of Hunters with literally no contact with any other group or access to even online sources at least the basics of this shouldn't be that much more obscure than the general weaknesses and powers of other supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. I was thinking more along the lines of tier 1 and possibly some tier 2, which I could see at best having sketchy access. Remember, a lot of the Conspiracies who would know a lot aren't likely to share the info and would also probably cover it up (TFV, Aegis Kai Doru, etc.). So sure, some go into a conflict with mages with a good idea of what they would face, but many who are just starting off or lack access to resources are going to have to piece things together (if they live long enough).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T19:25:10-08:00","id":780314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780290#post780290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point. I was thinking more along the lines of tier 1 and possibly some tier 2, which I could see at best having sketchy access. Remember, a lot of the Conspiracies who would know a lot aren't likely to share the info and would also probably cover it up (TFV, Aegis Kai Doru, etc.). So sure, some go into a conflict with mages with a good idea of what they would face, but many who are just starting off or lack access to resources are going to have to piece things together (if they live long enough).</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, that's just how it is for new Hunters who don't quickly make contact with other more experiences groups/sources. But at that point it isn't really a Quiescence issue anymore. These are the guys that are going after vampires with garlic, crosses, and holy water. They're pretty much screwed across the spectrum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T19:55:48-08:00","id":780327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780314#post780314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, that's just how it is for new Hunters who don't quickly make contact with other more experiences groups/sources. But at that point it isn't really a Quiescence issue anymore. These are the guys that are going after vampires with garlic, crosses, and holy water. They're pretty much screwed across the spectrum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Luckily for those newbie Hunters, &quot;garlic, crosses, and holy water&quot; are actually banes to some vampires in Vampire 2e, but that's a whole other discussion... <br /> <br /> More importantly, it would be <i>very</i> advisable for Hunters to join together, share and pass down knowledge and resources, maybe form <i>compacts</i> of Hunters to fight the creatures of the night. Such a strategy may even permit them to challenge the powerful monsters like vampires, werewolves, and evil wizards. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T20:03:31-08:00","id":780335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780327#post780327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Luckily for those newbie Hunters, &quot;garlic, crosses, and holy water&quot; are actually banes to some vampires in Vampire 2e, but that's a whole other discussion... <br /> <br /> More importantly, it would be <i>very</i> advisable for Hunters to join together, share and pass down knowledge and resources, maybe form <i>compacts</i> of Hunters to fight the creatures of the night. Such a strategy may even permit them to challenge the powerful monsters like vampires, werewolves, and evil wizards. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Or in many cases, end up working for the creatures of the night to kill said beings rivals, completely none the wiser <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T20:18:50-08:00","id":780346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780335#post780335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or in many cases, end up working for the creatures of the night to kill said beings rivals, completely none the wiser <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indeed. I thought it was simply understood that most major monster leaders have their own hunter dupes. One does not become a chief monster without plausible deniability! <br /> <br /> What was the Hunter compact or conspiracy that was implied to work for the Seers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T20:21:51-08:00","id":780347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780346#post780346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was the Hunter compact or conspiracy that was implied to work for the Seers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Division Six works for Panopticon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T22:43:20-08:00","id":780406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780171#post780171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every sane and non-paranoid person would dismiss it and think they misremembered. But we're talking about Hunters, sane and non-paranoid isn't exactly typical for the occupation.<br /> <br /> @up: got the same impression. As long as they don't try too hard to remember it shouldn't provoke breaking points.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I mean is that eye witnesses are unreliable and will, with the full intention of being honest, give accounts that don't match up. It's a pretty well known effect that doesn't require magic at all, so yes Hunters could jump to a conclusion, but disparity in memory isn't a good way to try determining targets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T01:11:54-08:00","id":780446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780347#post780347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Division Six works for Panopticon.</div> </div> </div> </div>One Panopticon Seer, to be precise. Not the organisation as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T09:07:28-08:00","id":780580,"title":"","content":"Personally really liked the Reach and Paradox system. Even started using it for my current Mage chronicle. Also the whole working in of Breaking Points into Paradox. So good. I also really liked Yantras. Maybe I can retrofit that whole Yantra system and finally make it so that I could basically make Ascension.<br /> I also liked the Paths, and their alternative interpretations. That said, I've always liked Paths anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9947-blackwoodcoven","name":"BlackwoodCoven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T09:22:41-08:00","id":780585,"title":"","content":"I'm a huge fan of the new Obrimos writeup. Such evocative language, and the concept of &quot;Divinity is the rules of nature and fundaments of reality&quot; appeals to my sensibilities <i>hard</i>.<br /> <br /> In 1E I had an Obrimos named Discordia who was a conspiracy theorist and &quot;Truth is out there&quot; kind of activist. When she Awakened, she was horrified to discover how she couldn't just reveal the Truth to Sleepers, so she worked on how to bestow revelations to Sleepers. I was always worried that Obrimos wasn't the best Path based on the 1E writeup, but it's basically perfect by the 2E writeup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T11:10:01-08:00","id":780627,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the only thing I really don't like about it is that it isn't out yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T11:16:33-08:00","id":780632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackwoodCoven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780580#post780580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally really liked the Reach and Paradox system. Even started using it for my current Mage chronicle. Also the whole working in of Breaking Points into Paradox. So good. I also really liked Yantras. Maybe I can retrofit that whole Yantra system and finally make it so that I could basically make Ascension.<br /> I also liked the Paths, and their alternative interpretations. That said, I've always liked Paths anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Same here, i think with the reach system + the new unifying roll of magic (all roll, gnosis + arcanum) we finally got a separation between raw power and magical knowledge. Being able to make an obrimos who with high gnosis but only fraying who is really really good at fire ball but lack the more subtle aspects like switching gravity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T11:38:29-08:00","id":780640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780632#post780632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Same here, i think with the reach system + the new unifying roll of magic (all roll, gnosis + arcanum) we finally got a separation between raw power and magical knowledge. Being able to make an obrimos who with high gnosis but only fraying who is really really good at fire ball but lack the more subtle aspects like switching gravity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The &quot;speed bumps&quot; have been removed from all Forces, Life, and Matter spells in 2e. All types of forces can now be affected with the appropriate Practices. Your hypothetical Obrimos could indeed fray gravity in 2e with only 3 dots of Forces.<br /> <br /> Edit: I also think the elimination of the Arcana speed bumps is a fantastic improvement over 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":".  type 12-05-2015, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T12:25:58-08:00","id":780654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780640#post780640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The &quot;speed bumps&quot; have been removed from all Forces, Life, and Matter in 2e. All types of forces can now be affected with the appropriate Practices. Your hypothetical Obrimos could indeed fray gravity in 2e with only 3 dots of Forces.<br /> <br /> Edit: I also think the elimination of the Arcana speed bumps is a fantastic improvement over 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>The speed bumps always felt like a giant &quot;fuck you&quot; to Forces, not only was the majority of the Arcanum Vulgar in aspect, you couldn't even do half the stuff you wanted until a higher dot level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T13:20:07-08:00","id":780684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780654#post780654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The speed bumps always felt like a giant &quot;fuck you&quot; to Forces, not only was the majority of the Arcanum Vulgar in aspect, you couldn't even do half the stuff you wanted until a higher dot level.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As a fan of Obrimos, the artificial limiters on Forces were very annoying. Life and Matter were also needlessly hamstrung, particularly Life with the no permanent spells on living beings rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T13:40:18-08:00","id":780688,"title":"","content":"I sort of understand why they did it, but I understand 2e's stance of &quot;fuck that shit&quot; a lot more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T13:44:33-08:00","id":780691,"title":"","content":"If we're getting back to &quot;things we like about the new edition&quot;... almost everything, really. Yantras are great. The new Paradox system is great (I've mentioned a few times how happy the player with the Guardian, Death-focused Moros in my group is that he can actually use his primary Arcanum Covertly now). The Reach system meaning spells actually stick to their Practices now is great - you immediately know what dot level a spell is based on what the spell does (and with the Practice of Ruling being 2 dots in both editions, &quot;all spells to control things are 2 dots&quot; means even starting Mages are <i>scary</i>). The Reach system meaning Paradox is something you <i>want</i> to risk rather than a result of casting a prohibited spell is <i>excellent</i> - my ST is pleased about that one to know end, as he's been trying to tempt us with Abyssal stuff forever to very little success. Praxes are a wonderful new edition - we finally have &quot;signature spells&quot; that actually are <i>your</i> signature spells, rather than something invented by some hoary old Master in your Order and taught to you by them. The changes to Mage Sight and Nimbus are also super neat. I also like the changes to Legacies - getting into a Legacy at Gnosis 2 is pretty great, and I can't say no to 5 Attainments instead of 3.<br /> <br /> On the fluff side of things, I really like some of the changes/clarifications there, most of which I've mentioned before. I like that the cultish &quot;secret tenets&quot; Guardians from their Orderbook are expressly stated to be a minority, with the majority of Guardians being the ones presented in the original corebook. Likewise, I like that there's room for philosophical/ideological Banishers in the new edition - &quot;their souls are just broken and if they were like us they would believe what we do&quot; was far too neat and tidy a way of sidestepping the idea of there being Mages who believe that no, fallible humans <i>don't</i> deserve to have the powers of gods. I also like the redefining of the relationship between the Diamond and the Free Council, and the renewed emphasis on the Free Council as the Sleeper Culture Order rather than just hyper-modernist technomages. The Free Council being the one Order that saw value in the Fallen World and its works in and of themselves (rather than as &quot;scattered, surviving remnants of lost Truth&quot; was what drew me to them in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T14:07:43-08:00","id":780698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Juhn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780691#post780691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The changes to Mage Sight and Nimbus are also super neat. </div> </div> </div> </div>I'm anxious to see the new Nimbus rules, particularly since the very old spoilers indicated that some of the rules were still in flux.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T16:22:36-08:00","id":780761,"title":"","content":"Having a Nimbus actually mean something is going to be interesting. It'll definitely add to the feeling of a given Mage, since they sound like they're a &quot;Choose your own&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> I'm curious to see how the &quot;Nimbus leak&quot; thing turned out as well; if there'll be mechanics (or at least suggestions) for it or if it'll just be a bit of fluff. The notion that Mages are lightning rods for odd junk is a wonderful thing for so many reasons, not the least of which is &quot;Why are there so many plot hooks?&quot; being answered neatly. It also helps explain why curious mortals might start snooping around a Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T16:47:16-08:00","id":780781,"title":"","content":"For things I'm sad about - I hoped that Rote Skills will either disappear, or they will be more open and free to pick from. I really disliked 1ED Rote Skill propositions, and literally no player I played with had occasion to get that +1Rote Skill bonus; it ended up being like Mana, forgotten and never used, simply because players had other skill ideas in mind and favored rotes with different skills encoded in them. Sadly, looking at Seer Ministries, Rote Skills seem to still be &quot;here are 3 skills, take or leave&quot;. Kinda hope that there will be some option to customize them (though I would hate to pay merit points for something like this, because it's basically a penalty for not playing a cookie cutter basic archetype).<br /> If you really want to give each Order 3 rote skills, at least pick one from each skill category, so you can showcase typical physical, mental and social activities of typical Ordermember, instead of making me hate myself for playing mental oriented or physical oriented Ladder instead of Social one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 12-05-2015, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T16:57:26-08:00","id":780788,"title":"","content":"If you never use mana you were definitely doing something wrong because it's required for a good chunk of the spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T17:36:22-08:00","id":780813,"title":"","content":"All your mana problems in 1E were solved by taking 3 dot artifact which doubled as 1st dot out-of-arcanum-spell and more importantly, 11 mana pool battery that regenerates 3 points of mana per day. Or taking 2 dots in prime.<br /> Which meant that 5 person cabal had 3 people with artifacts, and 2 with prime. :P<br /> I'm not talking about mana management in 2nd; I really like the fact that mana seems to matter much more there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T17:54:33-08:00","id":780826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780813#post780813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A<br /> I'm not talking about mana management in 2nd; I really like the fact that mana seems to matter much more there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mana also seems to much more in demand in 2e, particularly for Mage Sight and Arcana and Legacy attainments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T18:29:57-08:00","id":780845,"title":"","content":"Mana in 1e was either incredibly rare (if you only had a Hallow, which usually meant all of 1 Mana per person per day, which often meant you couldn't reasonably expect to recharge at all during a story), or incredibly trivial (if you had an artifact, a familiar, or Prime).<br /> <br /> My group got a hell of a lot more use out of the &quot;Your Hallow reduces the Mana cost of any spell by 1 if you cast inside of it&quot; part (mostly to make use of their non-Ruling Arcana, or to cast sympathetically, or just getting day-long Mage Armors up) than we did the &quot;you can draw Mana from a Hallow&quot; aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T19:10:50-08:00","id":780855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Juhn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780845#post780845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mana in 1e was either incredibly rare (if you only had a Hallow, which usually meant all of 1 Mana per person per day, which often meant you couldn't reasonably expect to recharge at all during a story), or incredibly trivial (if you had an artifact, a familiar, or Prime).<br /> <br /> My group got a hell of a lot more use out of the &quot;Your Hallow reduces the Mana cost of any spell by 1 if you cast inside of it&quot; part (mostly to make use of their non-Ruling Arcana, or to cast sympathetically, or just getting day-long Mage Armors up) than we did the &quot;you can draw Mana from a Hallow&quot; aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It seems you guys forgot that Legacy oblations were also a source of mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T23:44:35-08:00","id":780965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780761#post780761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a Nimbus actually mean something is going to be interesting. It'll definitely add to the feeling of a given Mage, since they sound like they're a &quot;Choose your own&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> I'm curious to see how the &quot;Nimbus leak&quot; thing turned out as well; if there'll be mechanics (or at least suggestions) for it or if it'll just be a bit of fluff. The notion that Mages are lightning rods for odd junk is a wonderful thing for so many reasons, not the least of which is &quot;Why are there so many plot hooks?&quot; being answered neatly. It also helps explain why curious mortals might start snooping around a Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>And going insane? Not good. Basically it's like the sleeper Hunter crap. It will not end well for any sleeper and from the sounds of it supernaturals won't be happy either. <br /> <br /> As a mage you decide to make a point or get tired of the ignorant fool you're dealing with? You get pissed and here comes the Nimbus and the Tilts. It's not going to be good for anyone beyond said mage if then. <br /> <br /> It's basically Predators Touch/Anima but likely worse for all involved. Used with caution means a mage solves the situation with no magic and no paradox. Used wrong is huge trouble","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 12-06-2015, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T00:03:06-08:00","id":780971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780965#post780965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And going insane? Not good. Basically it's like the sleeper Hunter crap. It will not end well for any sleeper and from the sounds of it supernaturals won't be happy either.<br /> <br /> As a mage you decide to make a point or get tired of the ignorant fool you're dealing with? You get pissed and here comes the Nimbus and the Tilts. It's not going to be good for anyone beyond said mage if then.<br /> <br /> It's basically Predators Touch/Anima but likely worse for all involved. Used with caution means a mage solves the situation with no magic and no paradox. Used wrong is huge trouble</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe Axel was referring to the &quot;Long Term Nimbus&quot; when he referenced &quot;nimbus leak,&quot; which is different that the &quot;Immediate Nimbus&quot; that causes Tilts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/luminous-beings-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/luminous-beings-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\"> Luminous Beings [Mage: The Awakening] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/luminous-beings-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/luminous-beings-mage-the-awakening/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T00:22:13-08:00","id":780980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780971#post780971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh, yeah my guess is that will be when GoV' will unsheath the knives. It's why I'm concerned with how hard it seems raising Wisdom is going to be because it really is only an issue for low wisdom mages and the Mad.<br /> <br /> <br /> I believe Axel was referring to the &amp;quot;Long Term Nimbus&amp;quot; when he referenced &amp;quot;nimbus leak,&amp;quot; which is different that the &amp;quot;Immediate Nimbus&amp;quot; that causes Tilts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/luminous-beings-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/luminous-beings-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\"> Luminous Beings [Mage: The Awakening] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/luminous-beings-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/luminous-beings-mage-the-awakening/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see. I'm worried given it seems raising Wisdom is going to be serious work, Too much in my opinion Other then that I think it's really only going to be an issue for low wisdom mages or the Mad.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would only be an issue for low wisdom mages or the Mad. Though I'm not liking how hard raising wisdom seems to be It's ticket for players to just say &quot;fuck that noise&quot; and do whatever you wanted to in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T00:31:19-08:00","id":780984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780980#post780980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would only be an issue for low wisdom mages or the Mad. Though I'm not liking how hard raising wisdom seems to be It's ticket for players to just say &quot;fuck that noise&quot; and do whatever you wanted to in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like the &quot;Long Term Nimbus&quot; mechanic, even for mages with a decent Wisdom. It adds a little bit of supernatural style, character, and overall strangeness to a mage's life that's thematically appropriate to the setting and similar to many other wizards in horror and urban fantasy. The fact that it can scale-up with high Gnosis and/or low Wisdom just makes it more interesting and fun. It particularly reminds me of the anti-technology effects of wizards in the Dresden Files,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T05:44:24-08:00","id":781085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780980#post780980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would only be an issue for low wisdom mages or the Mad. Though I'm not liking how hard raising wisdom seems to be It's ticket for players to just say &amp;quot;fuck that noise&amp;quot; and do whatever you wanted to in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until your nimbus leaks somewhere you don't want it to, and you have to clean it up or things get worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T09:27:09-08:00","id":781169,"title":"","content":"It just has me worried not that it's very thematic or appropriate to the setting. It'll probably work just fine in play. It's not like most people play spree killers in actual games anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T10:33:09-08:00","id":781197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=780980#post780980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would only be an issue for low wisdom mages or the Mad. Though I'm not liking how hard raising wisdom seems to be It's ticket for players to just say &quot;fuck that noise&quot; and do whatever you wanted to in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, it isn't. Mages with high Wisdom <i>still</i> suffer the &quot;leak&quot; of their Nimbus. Shadow Names ground that leak in their mystical life, though, and the strength of it determines how closely connected one needs to be with the Mage for things to occur. What this means is, your average Mage is more likely to see odd things occurring. A high Wisdom Thyrsus might see their prayer site start to become a locus, attracting spirits; a low Wisdom Obrimos starts to attract street preachers to their usual subway route, who start proclaiming the glory of She Who Lies Beneath.<br /> <br /> Whatever the case, it sounds like it's largely narrative in origin, and that's a thing I like.<br /> <br /> As far as raising Wisdom goes, I think you're missing some of the point. Morality stats have tried previously to be a way to keep players moral, rather than enforce any style of gameplay; steal a wallet, develop schizophrenia, as the 1e maxim goes. In 2e, the stats are largely being shifted as a way towards showing consequences. Wisdom isn't an easy thing to hold and maintain; it's a representation of your restraint and self-control. If players decide &quot;Fuck that noise&quot; because they and their character believe that a given tenet of Wisdom just isn't worth maintaining, that's <i>good</i>; it means the mechanics have done their job to emphasize a theme; a theme that tells us that those who are willing to discard the concepts of knock-on effects and the rights of others are generally going to do so elsewhere as well.<br /> <br /> Mage should be a game where you are willing to look at Wisdom and say &quot;Fuck that noise&quot; if you sincerely disagree with it. You just have to consider and accept what saying that means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T10:53:25-08:00","id":781205,"title":"","content":"I feel like something that's being forgotten are that there are also benefits to having a higher Wisdom. Will you have more praxes, rotes, arcana or Gnosis than someone with a lower Wisdom? Maybe not, but you will have a better relationship with ephemeral entities and also be able to better maintain control over the effects of your Nimbus to keep it from causing &quot;radiation poisoning&quot; to those you care about. I assume that having your nimbus leak onto less stuff also means there are less sympathetic connections leading back to you that could be manipulated by your enemies and that's definitely a plus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T11:00:05-08:00","id":781208,"title":"","content":"It may be a non issue depending on which spells are going to be wisdom hits no matter what. In 1e it was &quot;way too many&quot;. It seems to me there may be a lot more flexibility concerning this in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T11:05:32-08:00","id":781212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=781205#post781205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like something that's being forgotten are that there are also benefits to having a higher Wisdom. Will you have more praxes, rotes, arcana or Gnosis than someone with a lower Wisdom? Maybe not, but you will have a better relationship with ephemeral entities and also be able to better maintain control over the effects of your Nimbus to keep it from causing &quot;radiation poisoning&quot; to those you care about. I assume that having your nimbus leak onto less stuff also means there are less sympathetic connections leading back to you that could be manipulated by your enemies and that's definitely a plus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dont forget that you roll Wisdom to contain paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T11:10:17-08:00","id":781214,"title":"","content":"Actually, I think that the Creative Thaumaturgy blog had a mention that Wisdom dots limit the amount of beats you can get from magically (self) imposed Conditions, probably over a certain period of time. If so, it could mean that a mage who takes the effort to keep Wisdom high can progress in power faster that a low Wisdom mage.<br /> <br /> One limitation was one beat per scene. I wonder what the Wisdom related numbers are... Unless Dave spoiled them and I missed it.<br /> <br /> Edit: I think a high Wisdom mage <i>avoids</i> causing paradox altogether (and overreaching by extension).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T11:22:07-08:00","id":781221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=781205#post781205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like something that's being forgotten are that there are also benefits to having a higher Wisdom. Will you have more praxes, rotes, arcana or Gnosis than someone with a lower Wisdom? Maybe not, but you will have a better relationship with ephemeral entities and also be able to better maintain control over the effects of your Nimbus to keep it from causing &quot;radiation poisoning&quot; to those you care about. I assume that having your nimbus leak onto less stuff also means there are less sympathetic connections leading back to you that could be manipulated by your enemies and that's definitely a plus.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not forgotten, I just didn't feel the need to bring it up; the chief benefits for high Wisdom are a better relation with spirits, better control over Paradox, and less Nimbus leakage. Someone who is high enough Wisdom to have that penalty is the sort that'd be respectful and rare in their dealings (as in, deal making) with spirits and rare in their Paradoxes to begin with. Sympathy, meanwhile, starts at Intimate <i>first</i> and works more distant, meaning your friends and loved ones get targeted first no matter how Wise you are... Unless you produce a Shadow Name and ground that in your mystic life, in which case, you've distinctly separated the two.<br /> <br /> I don't think it'll also create sympathetic links for you, either, unless I'm mistaken.<br /> <br /> That all brings me back to my point: The consequences for having low Wisdom are really self-inflicted: You only really start suffering from bargaining with spirits if you're a right evil bastard to begin with, at which point you're probably not bargaining with them anyway. The sort of person who needs Wisdom the most to absorb Paradox is the one who's casting the most vulgar spells (i.e. the unWise). The people whose Nimbus leaks beyond their immediate circle are the ones who are already likely casually casting spells on strangers because screw that guy for littering, now he has chlamydia.<br /> <br /> In other words, every possible benefit Wisdom can bring you fits this wonderful dynamic: Those who use their power sparingly and deliberately are <i>better</i> at it than those who throw it about mindlessly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T12:42:08-08:00","id":781266,"title":"","content":"I thought that lower Wisdom could leak past your shadow name to your real identity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T13:03:43-08:00","id":781283,"title":"","content":"I would also note that at lower Gnosis levels, the Nimbus effects appear generally mild and narrative, and at worst, a little annoying, regardless of Wisdom. The strength of Nimbus effects at high Gnosis, even with an accompanying high Wisdom, could become truly problematic, particularly for those closest to the mage. The Nimbus of a very low Wisdom, very high Gnosis mage could present a danger to everyone around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T15:15:17-08:00","id":781338,"title":"","content":"My personal thoughts on the Mage 2E.<br /> <br /> 1.) The reach system is inspired, and is really cool. <br /> 2.) Supernal Summoning. Lots of old myths and stories have magic-users commanding, summonings, and generally dealing with spirits and supernatural entities; you have the idea of demon summoning, the wizards summoning the djinn in arabian folklore, countless myths about invoking and calling down higher powers such as gods and spirits, and that's just scratching the surface. Any plenty of modern fiction about magic users has them invoking spirits and magical creatures as a regular thing, or even as the source of their power. (See the Bartimaeus trilogy, or Jonathan Strange and Mr. Norrell and that's just off the top of my head.) Mage: The awakening 1E never really was able to capture the feel of that &quot;mages are people who deal with spirits and magical creatures&quot; really well. Or rather, they could capture the feel of that well, but it wasn't flexible about it. Mages could be shamans and mediums, but they couldn't really be summoners. <br /> <br /> Let me explain. The Sprits of the nWoD, while very cool and works really well for the setting, tend to end up feeling somewhat limited in conceptual space. Summoners opened up the door somewhat, but never shook that problem of feel. Spirits were cool, giving Spirit magic (and the nWoD) it's own dark, creepy, alien feel. They made being a lowercase-s shaman be cool and dangerous, making breathing life in the idea of animist summoning, and making it feel part of the world of darkness. Ghosts were the same way, feeling creepy and alien and dangerous while still being ghosts. When Summoners brought up astral summoning, White wolf also did a really good job of making astral entities that felt odd and dangerous and inhuman but also like things of the soul and of the mind. And to people who wanted to be shamans, or deal speak with the dead, or futz around in the collective unconscious, those thing worked great.<br /> <br /> But none of those were demons. None of those felt like demons. You couldn't be a demon-summoner, or a man who called up the djinn to do serve him, a man dealt with fairies and the fey, or a man who invoked angels for strength and guidance. You couldn't call up the primal (but far from savage or animalistic) spirit guides of some Native american myths, you couldn't invoke the beaurucratic spirits and demons like the ones of Chinese and Bhuddist myth, or spirits like the ones of Japanese Shinto. You can't stand upon the banks of the river and scream out to the grim reaper, or the God of the Dead, or the judge of the Afterlife, to deal with him to bring your loved one back to life- or you could, but he had to be some spirit of death, or some thing of the Underworld, or the Astral spirit of death. Not something else, something magical, something mysterious. <br /> <br /> But with Supernal Summoning? Now you can. You can be whatever kind of summoner you want. Spirits of the shadow are free to be creepy animism spirits now, ghosts can be ghosts, and astral spirits can be the world inside all of our heads, and all those sorts of things are still playable. But Supernal spirits can be flexible and mysterious in a way none of those others can, magical in a way none of those others can match. They can be strange and weird and but still belong to magic, that mysterious supernal world, and be mysterious and strange in turn. It's made the supernal world closer in the coolest way.<br /> <br /> And it's simple. 3 dots, any any mage can summon these creatures. Imagine what that means. You don't have to build your character around summoning to being a summoner. You don't have to be a summoner to summon strange spirits, and deal with these things. You can send out spirits on missions to help you, do things, and still be able to do tons of other crap. I think it makes mages feel so much more like the sorcerers of myth, being able to do that. Mages could never really summon creatures of magic- their own magic- in 1E. It's given a spot for &quot;mages as summoners of magical otherworldly creatures&quot; a way to exist in the framework of the game that 1E never quite did. <br /> <br /> And imagine if something like 30 or 40 mages gathered together. Demons and totems and little angels running all over the place, serving their masters. Any place where you see a lot of mages gather or work is not just going to have people that do magic, but creatures that are magical serving them. Combine with the idea of the long term nimbus, and any place where mages gather and be mages is going to feel magical, full of strange otherworldly signs and otherworldly beings. It's cool.<br /> <br /> Before, mages could be mediums and modern day shaman and strange psychics. Now, they can also be summoners who deal with creatures of magic. And that's awesome.<br /> <br /> 3.) There's a stronger, clearer idea of what the practices are about, what the arcanum are, and what they can do, especially at low levels. I like this a lot, since it makes it so much easier to make new spells, and gives so much more an idea of what the arcanum can do. In 1E, compelling and ruling were sort of ill-defiend this way. But with 2E, whe have much better examples to work from as starting point. With matter Compelling can cause water to flow downhill towards the character. Ruling can make it flow up hill, into strange shapes, and into any way you want. Mind compelling? You can make a person do something they were inclined to do anyway- and that fits nicely into the &quot;emotional urge&quot; they had as ruling in Mage 1E, where you can make people feel an emotion of your choosing, regardless of inclination. So another compelling spell would be to make people sad if that were at a funeral of someone they knew, while another ruling spell could be to make a guy go for a bite to eat even if he isn't hungry.<br /> <br /> Also, people now get cooler stuff at low levels in some arcana that lacked them. Space 2 Ruling lets you blip somewhere you couldn't because of an obstruction. So Space 1 lets you teleport anywhere you could get too normally. Don't feel like climbing? Blip, and you're there. The expansion of time to the sense of time means time compelling spells can actually do something, and at ruling you can make time go faster or slower, which was something that wasn't in the corebook of 1E. <br /> <br /> In addition, putting Truth and revelations under Prime's purview gives quite a bit more flexibility with it. Prime 2 Ruling, you make someone believe something you believe is true and that is objectively true, no matter what. So Prime 1 compelling could do the same thing, but on a person who might of believed you anyway. Prime 1 knowing turns you into a lie detector than works even if they don't know they're lying, going by the same conditions of truth under the ruling spell from the spoiler. <br /> \u200b<br /> Veiling spells have similarly been explained. In the &quot;creative thaumurtagy&quot; spoiler, they gave a couple of examples? With time, you can make a person loose all sense of time. Which means you can do all sort of tricks with it. With matter? Make a building impossible to notice.<br /> <br /> So you could make a person invisible with forces, since you're using the light...or you could use life, since he's a living being you're hiding. You can make a building hard to notice with matter (since it's an object), or you could do it with mind (since you're using mind-tricks to hide the building). Space veiling can make an area hard to notice or remember. Time veiling can give people fits of lost time, by concealing that period of time. Super lying skills? Prime 2, hide the truth. Or misdirect, using the truth to life. Fate 2 Veiling let's you hide that you've broken an agreement, if fate 1 knowing lets you detect if someone's has fulfilled one. <br /> <br /> I remeber once that Stephen Lea Shepard analyzied the capabilities of mages by path, to get an idea of what they could do at each level. So that's what I'm going to do, just with more speculation and less systimatically.<br /> <br /> So, in 2E, In addition to what they could do from 1E,<br /> Acanthus can cause a person to loose all sense of time, and probably mess with people's sense of time in other ways as well. And that's in addition to what they could do before. <br /> They can also speed time up and slow it down. <br /> They can know when promises are fulfilled, and probably influence promises that way.<br /> They can stop Damage over Time effects. <br /> And that in addition to all the fate-fiddling and minor prophecy they could do before.<br /> <br /> In 2E,<br /> Mastigos can cause people or animals to do something that they would normally do, like eat if they're hungry, and can make them do/feel things they wouldn't be normally inclined to do, causing impulses, thoughts, emotions and the like.<br /> They can also teleporting/bypassing an obstruction on a local level, and presumably bamf about like cartoon characters, using compelling spells to blip to places they could go normally (so easy local teleports) and Ruling spells to achive a &quot;line of sight teleport&quot; effect to warp to spaces they can see, but too far away to get to. You'd probably require reach to get to places like the top of a hill you can't climb, or places that are too far away to get too and have some other sort of obstruction like a fence. <br /> I can easily also imagine a zoom in effect that is a sensory version of scrying. (&quot;You see that dot on the horizon? Now you see it better&quot;. <br /> <br /> In 2e,<br /> Obrimos can get people to believe the truth when they know it and are right, and probably act as living lie detectors and conceal truths on top of that. <br /> They can also futz around with any forces- light, heat, fire, gravity, motion- etc. to the exent of their power, right from the start. So they can probably make gravity pull more at lower levels, and definitely turn it off entirely by 3 dots. <br /> <br /> In 2e,<br /> Moros can make buildings and objects hard to notice. Or make them invsible. The could also probably move crap through telekineses, to a certain extent (if they can make water flow uphill, they can make air flow anywhere, they can make things with wheels roll uphill, and with enough reach they can probably throw around inanimate objects like a Obrimos can throw around anything else.) <br /> <br /> In 2E, <br /> Thryusus can change their appearance, and can probably hide people in any sorts of ways. Thrysus can also command people and animals like a mind mage could do with compelling and ruling, but wouldn't be able to alter memories or cap like at higher levels, and they probably couldn't change emotions flexibly, they'd just make people do stuff. They can also command around spirits real easily. <br /> <br /> So, looking at this...<br /> Acanthus could really easily futz with time in a serious way at low levels that wasn't apparent before. They can also explictly mess with people's sense of time, which is cool. They still have all the- &quot;I feel like prophesy at will&quot; stuff they have before. As for their powers affect mages daily life...well, they're lucky. Like all the time, and have perfect timing, and if something feels like it's taking forever or going by too quickly they can just mess with their own sense of time. Acanthus don't have to deal like petty things like &quot;boredom&quot;; they can just make the time seem to fly by!<br /> <br /> Mastigos, in addition to their advantages at understanding at manipulating people in 1E, are also a whole lot harder to keep out of everywhere without magical defenses. Doors, locks and walls mean virtually nothing. They can get into anyones house, easy. It really upsells the &quot;privacy is nothing&quot; angle. As for daily life, Mastigos can always know how everyone around them really felt, but now they can casually teleport on a local scale if they don't feel like moving around the normal way, and they could portal without being vulgar. That would make the idea of travel and getting around a lot more to deal with. It's easy go anywhere, get out of anywhere, and it's easy to escape if people catch you, either with &quot;don't notice me&quot; or just by warping into a closet, or behind them when they aren't looking. This lets you do all sorts of looney toons nonsense, and makes snooping absolutely trival. They can also get privacy for themselves trivally, by making themselves or their living area hard to notice. <br /> <br /> Obrimos always had all the little cool comfor spells- never to hot or cold, never to bright or dark. Now they can add &quot;living lie detector&quot; to they're resume, and don't really have to worry about people believing the truth of what they say; no Obrimos has to worry about being thought mad by their family or sleeper friends by believing in impossible things, they can just tell them! Being honest is always an option for these guys, no matter how much they lie otherwise so it would make being straightforward a lot more attractive. They can also tell when other people are lying to them, or just plain wrong and crazy. <br /> <br /> Moros can see dead people (duh). They can also talk to them, and know the presence of death around them, which is sobering stuff. They also get a whole level of cool things using matter ruling spells and compelling spells, like being able to cusing water to flow the way they want, make balls roll around, and cause all sorts of &quot;poltergiest effect&quot; sorts of things (plates falling of shelves? Matter ruling, baby!). This allows for all sorts of neat little fun with their power, like opening doors without touching them, start their car without their keys, and all sorts of neat little &quot;lazy telekinetic&quot; tricks normally reserved for Obrimos. They also have the ability to hide stuff, all the way up to buildings, so they're the easiest to have a &quot;secret retreat nobody can find&quot; right after mastigos. They can also hide objects, making them great thieves; when a moros doesn't want something found, it doesn't get found by normal people. So being a moros can be really sobering, but it's pretty trival to manipulate lots of stuff in you're environment. <br /> <br /> Thrysus are pobably going to be a lot better at manuvering animals and people, and can be incredibly sneaky simply because he can target himself with virtually any sort of concealment spell he wants, because he's a life pattern. hey can be another person, unoticible, or invisible, whichever one is best for him at the time.They don't need to be afraid of animals at all, either, since they can probably exert strong control over them with pretty simple, low-risk spells. Getting birds, cats, and other animals to do your chores is a distinct possbility now. As is understanding them, or even talking to them like Dr. Dolittle at a bit higher levels (Unveiling, target other, yeah sure!). They also have all the benefits they had last edition of being really healthy all the time, being able to purge poisions and stuff from their systems.<br /> <br /> So for 2E...<br /> Acanthus can cause weird time shit ALL THE TIME from awfully early, and never have to have time pass too fast or too slow, never have to worry about bad luck, and can always know both the outcome of a random event and it's impact upon her immediate future. Augury means that &quot;Is this a good idea?&quot; is a question you always have an answer too, at least with regards to yourself.<br /> <br /> Mastigos can go damn near wherever they please, screw security, locks, and probably other people, and probably the only thing to need to worry about are other wizards and video cameras. They always know how people really feel, and always know what people really care about by reading their sympathy. Hiding anything from them is going to be hard, and catching them is going to be damn near impossible. They can easily return home whenever they want, so &quot;getting lost&quot; and &quot;too far away to go back&quot; are concepts that no longer apply to these guys. Causal, paradox-free teleportation (even if it's short range until dot 4) promises to be amazingly fun.<br /> <br /> Moros can always see dead, people, talk to dead people, and probably move around objects without touching them. They can also play waterbender, earthbender, and airbender, and everything-but-firebender. They can proabably steal anything left unattended for too long with veiling/ruling spells to make it not noticible. I am betting they can also make give materials all sorts of crazy impossible properties, or do things like evaporate water at room temperature (or generally alter the phase of anything, to hell with melting temperatures). They'll probably loosing things like alter conductivity until 3 dots, though, when they get weaving spells, at which point you get all those property modifying spells. <br /> <br /> Obrimos never have to worry about being uncomfortable or about being believed. Like, ever. They can tell the craziest crap to people who don't know them, and if it's true, they can get their target to belive it. They may not want to, or try to lie to themselves after the fact, but never having to worry about the &quot;this is going to sound crazy, but...&quot; problem is awesome enough in it's own right. <br /> <br /> Thrysus don't have to worry about animals, and probably aren't afraid of even the most dangerous, since it's easy to control them. &quot;Being sick&quot; is something that happens to other people, and they can talk to virtually anything, or at least the spirit of virtually anything. <br /> <br /> So yeah, I'm excited.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8045-azunth","name":"Azunth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T15:46:54-08:00","id":781348,"title":"","content":"<b>@Azunth:</b> Your enthusiasm is most impressive. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And imagine if something like 30 or 40 mages gathered together. Demons and totems and little angels running all over the place, serving their masters. Any place where you see a lot of mages gather or work is not just going to have people that do magic, but creatures that are magical serving them. </div> </div> </div>I don't believe the intent of 2e is for supernal beings to be little more than servants. As with their portrayal in Summoners, they are generally powerful, wise and enigmatic creatures who may advise or assist, but are no mere servants. For instance, the inhabitants of the Aether are not &quot; little angels running all over the place,&quot; they are the living symbols of the fundamental forces of the universe and magic itself made manifest. They are not the smiling, chubby, benevolent creatures of Renaissance art, they more akin to the powerful, unwavering, and <i><b>very</b></i> judgmental beings that smote entire nations in the Old Testament.<br /> <br /> According to Dave, mages are also still limited to summons beings from their own Path realms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> no Obrimos has to worry about being thought mad by their family or sleeper friends by believing in impossible things, they can just tell them! Being honest is always an option for these guys, no matter how much they lie otherwise so it would make being straightforward a lot more attractive. They can also tell when other people are lying to them, or just plain wrong and crazy.<br /> <br /> * * *<br /> <br /> They can tell the craziest crap to people who don't know them, and if it's true, they can get their target to belive it. They may not want to, or try to lie to themselves after the fact, but never having to worry about the &quot;this is going to sound crazy, but...&quot; problem is awesome enough in it's own right. </div> </div> </div>If those family, friends, and other people are Sleepers, the Quiescence will make casting the relevant spells on or before them a dangerous and Unwise idea, as it will cause breaking points and memory loss. The Lie is not so easily denied.<br /> <br /> The other Paths face similar problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T15:52:44-08:00","id":781354,"title":"","content":"Moros can firebend too. Use flammable gas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T16:50:46-08:00","id":781386,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=781348#post781348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>@Azunth:</b> Your enthusiasm is most impressive. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't believe the intent of 2e is for supernal being to be little more than servants. As with their portrayal in Summoners, they are generally powerful, wise and enigmatic creatures who may advise or assist, but are no mere servants. For instance, the inhabitants of the Aether are not &quot; little angels running all over the place,&quot; they are the living symbols of the fundamental forces of the universe and magic itself made manifest. They are not the smiling, chubby, benevolent creatures of Renaissance art, they more akin to the powerful, unwavering, and <i><b>very</b></i> judgmental beings that smote entire nations in the Old Testament.<br /> <br /> According to Dave, mages are also still limited to summons beings from their own Path realms.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they probably would be more than servants, but you could still upon them to help you, and bargain to have them perform tasks on your behalf, and that sort of summoning was still much harder in previous editions. Mages being limited to summoning creatures of their path is something I was always okay with, so that's hardly a dealbreaker for me. And frankly, old-testament style weird angels were what I was imaging anyway, just scaled down a bit. And if that sort of &quot;call up minor entity&quot; is not possible, well, I'm really too psyched that this kind of summoning is happening at all in the corebook to care much<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=781348#post781348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>@Azunth:</b><br /> If those family, friends, and other people are Sleepers, the Quiescence will make casting the relevant spells on or before them a dangerous and Unwise idea, as it will cause breaking points and memory loss. The Lie is not so easily denied.<br /> <br /> The other Paths face similar problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't think that would negate the effect of the spell. One, I didn't think Words of Truth was obvious enough to trigger Quiescence. Unless you are actively telling people about the supernatural like &quot;Magic is real&quot; and &quot;That dude is a werewolf&quot;, or things they know/think can't possibly be true, such as &quot;I got that scar when got in a shootout in South America last yesterday&quot; when they saw you for breakfast and dinner on that day on a different continent. Barring wild cases like that, I didn't think it would be enough to trigger the curse of Quiesence, so you can get people to believe about most mundane things even if the wouldn't otherwise. Two, even if Quiescence triggered, I thought it wouldn't affect the resulting belief because the spell affects the words, and belief was a result of that effect on the truth. If a sleeper saw a spell that has levitated a car across a parking lot and destroyed it, it causes a car to falls and the sleeper to imagine they saw a crash, instead of teleporting the car back to it's original position. In the same way, even if Quiescence unravelled the spell and caused the target to forget he heard the mage speak with absolute truth, the belief would remain, merely rationalized differently. <br /> <br /> Being told magic is real using Words of Truth is definitely dangerous and stressful, and certainly causes a breaking point simply because of the nature of the truth, but the target doesn't forget or disbelieve what they've been told- they forget the spell that made them believe it. It may be dangerous and unwise, it may not be a good idea, and its certainly rough on the Sleeper's sanity, but ultimately an Obrimos can throw up her hands, say &quot;F*** it, I'm a wizard&quot;, and have it stick, no matter the situation, no matter the history. Other paths have a much, much harder time convincing people than that, and for them it may not be possible. But for an Obrimos, it's always an option, and that's probably a load off their mind, that they can tell the truth if the have too.<br /> <br /> Plus, if an Obrimos wants to be gentle, they can nudge a person into suspecting magic by doing some weird-but-not-obviously magic things, then use a compelling variant of Words of Truth to more gently get them to believe- and there's no way that would be obvious enough to trigger quiescence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8045-azunth","name":"Azunth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T18:47:35-08:00","id":781465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azunth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=781386#post781386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, they probably would be more than servants, but you could still upon them to help you, and bargain to have them perform tasks on your behalf, and that sort of summoning was still much harder in previous editions. Mages being limited to summoning creatures of their path is something I was always okay with, so that's hardly a dealbreaker for me. And frankly, old-testament style weird angels were what I was imaging anyway, just scaled down a bit. And if that sort of &quot;call up minor entity&quot; is not possible, well, I'm really too psyched that this kind of summoning is happening at all in the corebook to care much</div> </div> </div> </div>Hear me great and noble Seraphim. I compel you to strike at my enemies, for they forsake the Truth, indulge in wickedness and debauchery, and further the Lie. Smite them down with fire and brimstone lest they deny the awesome power of the Aether,... and when you're done, it would be great if you could pick-up some milk and eggs at the store, and don't forget to bring in the mail and newspaper...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T17:58:07-08:00","id":1058712,"title":"","content":"Perhaps we could agree that if a tier 1 cell went after a Mage with any real persistence and lack of preparation they would go crazy from all the breaking points, start indiscriminately targeting people due to their weakened integrity and grip on reality, then end up becoming slashers. Are slashers affected by the sleeping curse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T03:54:11-08:00","id":1058867,"title":"","content":"\u200bCons:<br /> 1. I liked it more when Atlantis was real, and mages <b>were </b><span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">heirs to it. I don't like &quot;maybe it is, maybe it's not&quot; approach to setting building - I like having answers, because then I can choose if I like them or don't like them and decide if I want to use them. Otherwise I just have to create setting on my own. I also liked it more when Supernal Realms were realms. I find argument &quot;but you can't travel to Biology&quot; really stupid. Yes, you can't, but it doesn't change the fact that it's much more easy to understand information in terms of spatial relations. &quot;Palaces of memory&quot; are built exactly on this trick.<br /> <br /> 2. Paths are bad. They aren't really interesting, and aren't really playing to stereotypes they try to convey, because: 1) you can understand those stereotypes differently (for example, &quot;witch&quot; for me strongly associates with potions and commanding animals and weather, so Matter/Forces/Life, not Fate/Time); 2) your character is bound to those stereotypes in choosing Arcana, and that's just sad. I think it would be great to include at least one small section to playing without Paths, instead of making you buy Storyteller's guide for that.<br /> <br /> 3. Wisdom is a </span></span>mess<span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">. I don't think there really is understanding what is is in-universe, how it works and what is it represents. This theme covers it up better than me: </span></span>http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887107-understand-wisdom<br /> <br /> 4. Withstand/Clash of Wills system. First of all, Withstand is a joke. Strong mages can easily burn right through it with Exceptional Success, which is easily achieved either by Praxis or ungodly dicepools of 10+. Incidentally, it makes every other splat Mages underdogs, because they literally can't defend themselves, at all. Unless you use Supernatural Tolerance as a bonus to Withstand, and then you just can't burn through, unless ES again. And because ability to protect yourself with Clash of Wills is so limited, every other splat (including all kinds of spirits) is just clay in mages hands, killing opportunity to every crossover. More than that, two Masters with different Arcana and without Shielding practice in other will just have mexican stand-off: either Life master destroys Pattern of Force Master, or Forces Master destroys Pattern of Life Master. They have no way to protect oneself against each other magic, and you can't have cool magical duels between different mages - it's just &quot;shot, shot, somebody collapses to dust&quot;. And that nicely ties to the next problem:<br /> <br /> 5. Mages don't have any other antagonists, except other mages. Every splat has &quot;out of context problem&quot;, something they can't really beat by their normal means: Vampire have Strix, werewolves have Idigam, and mages have... nothing. Quite literally: all kinds of ephemeral entities are either destroy mage outright, because he lacks the corresponding Arcana and can't interact with them, or he have it and they can't do much about him, and he can lord over them quite easily. I'd imagine that Rank 5 spirit, a fricking <b>minor god</b>, would be more than a match for Spirit Master, but not - you could bind it, reshape it and banish it easily, and all it can do is Withstand you with a Rank. Laughable.<br /> Okay, you are asking: what about the Abyss? Well: what about the Abyss? Acamoth and Gulmoth are treated like Goetia and spirits, respectively. You can use usual Arcana on them - all &quot;anti-magic&quot; jazz is part of the fluff, but not the crunch. Yes, they can warp reality - you can do that too. And by the rules, you are <b>better </b>at this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","user":"Dark Archon","date":". 03-06-2017, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T04:10:11-08:00","id":1058876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058867#post1058867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bCons:<br /> <br /> <br /> 4. Withstand/Clash of Wills system. First of all, Withstand is a joke. Strong mages can easily burn right through it with Exceptional Success, which is easily achieved either by Praxis or ungodly dicepools of 10+. Incidentally, it makes every other splat Mages underdogs, because they literally can't defend themselves, at all. Unless you use Supernatural Tolerance as a bonus to Withstand, and then you just can't burn through, unless ES again. And because ability to protect yourself with Clash of Wills is so limited, every other splat (including all kinds of spirits) is just clay in mages hands, killing opportunity to every crossover. More than that, two Masters with different Arcana and without Shielding practice in other will just have mexican stand-off: either Life master destroys Pattern of Force Master, or Forces Master destroys Pattern of Life Master. They have no way to protect oneself against each other magic, and you can't have cool magical duels between different mages - it's just &quot;shot, shot, somebody collapses to dust&quot;. And that nicely ties to the next problem:<br /> <br /> 5. Mages don't have any other antagonists, except other mages. Every splat has &quot;out of context problem&quot;, something they can't really beat by their normal means: Vampire have Strix, werewolves have Idigam, and mages have... nothing. Quite literally: all kinds of ephemeral entities are either destroy mage outright, because he lacks the corresponding Arcana and can't interact with them, or he have it and they can't do much about him, and he can lord over them quite easily. I'd imagine that Rank 5 spirit, a fricking <b>minor god</b>, would be more than a match for Spirit Master, but not - you could bind it, reshape it and banish it easily, and all it can do is Withstand you with a Rank. Laughable.<br /> Okay, you are asking: what about the Abyss? Well: what about the Abyss? Acamoth and Gulmoth are treated like Goetia and spirits, respectively. You can use usual Arcana on them - all &quot;anti-magic&quot; jazz is part of the fluff, but not the crunch. Yes, they can warp reality - you can do that too. And by the rules, you are <b>better </b>at this.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why, in general, Mage tends to work much better when working with plots that aren't centered around antagonists, and instead of fighting something, you focus on trying to unravel Mysteries. But yeah, I agree that Mage is Critical Existence Failure Tag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T04:39:16-08:00","id":1058888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058876#post1058876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you focus on trying to unravel Mysteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this setting have too many interesting antagonists. I love Seers. I didn't understand the Banishers before reading their book, but they work perfectly as mage-Hunters. And then there is Scelesti, Mad, Reapers... Setting don't have any fluff problems for me, but mechanics really don't support cool wizard duels and battles. There isn't even &quot;save-or-die&quot; in much of the situations, it's &quot;you shot first, you win&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T04:43:57-08:00","id":1058890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058712#post1058712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps we could agree that if a tier 1 cell went after a Mage with any real persistence and lack of preparation they would go crazy from all the breaking points, start indiscriminately targeting people due to their weakened integrity and grip on reality, then end up becoming slashers. Are slashers affected by the sleeping curse?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or just be killed? Because Mage. See below <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058867#post1058867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> More than that, two Masters with different Arcana and without Shielding practice in other will just have mexican stand-off: either Life master destroys Pattern of Force Master, or Forces Master destroys Pattern of Life Master. They have no way to protect oneself against each other magic, and you can't have cool magical duels between different mages - it's just &quot;shot, shot, somebody collapses to dust&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The state of mutually assured destruction is why you don't have Masters going around nuking people. It's the logic of the Cold War, and like in our world's history, what you do is have proxy wars and politicking. Proxies of these venerable Masters being player characters, or they at least deal with the mess it causes.<br /> Also I like the Duel Arcane if there are really two Masters who are on opposing sides of an argument but still want to have a place in the Consilium, and thus won't just go nuke.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058867#post1058867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> 5. Mages don't have any other antagonists, except other mages. Every splat has &quot;out of context problem&quot;, something they can't really beat by their normal means: Vampire have Strix, werewolves have Idigam, and mages have... nothing. Quite literally: all kinds of ephemeral entities are either destroy mage outright, because he lacks the corresponding Arcana and can't interact with them, or he have it and they can't do much about him, and he can lord over them quite easily. I'd imagine that Rank 5 spirit, a fricking <b>minor god</b>, would be more than a match for Spirit Master, but not - you could bind it, reshape it and banish it easily, and all it can do is Withstand you with a Rank. Laughable.<br /> Okay, you are asking: what about the Abyss? Well: what about the Abyss? Acamoth and Gulmoth are treated like Goetia and spirits, respectively. You can use usual Arcana on them - all &quot;anti-magic&quot; jazz is part of the fluff, but not the crunch. Yes, they can warp reality - you can do that too. And by the rules, you are <b>better </b>at this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? No out of context problems? <b>The Lie</b>, being the state of the entire world.<b> Exarchs</b>. Fine, technically may be oldtimey Mages, but are far beyond that now, the big gods to the minor ones you mentioned. Want an antagonist you can't just arbitrarily Unmake? There you go. Change the fundamental basics of the setting, fight the embodied symbols of tyranny. <br /> <br /> Or maybe just ignore that and focus on feeling good about being able to bind and banish minor gods if the big ones are too much.<br /> For that is what the Mages are, the starting form of gods. (for some definitions of that word, no need to go too deep into that, it's just a fluff sentence :P)<br /> Like the vampies focus on their politicking and such rather than think too much on the barely-detectable possessing shadow owls. (who are totally progenitors of vampirism, right? Embrace, Cruac? Maybe a thing for its own thread.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T04:45:23-08:00","id":1058893,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11880_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11880\" data-vbnamecard=\"11880\">Dark Archon</a> 1) The maybe it is maybe it isn't attitude the game takes toward Atlantis and other things doesn't in any way hinder your ability to choose what you do and don't like having as true in your setting. A lack of answers is supposed to make that ability easier for you and everyone else.<br /> <br /> 5) You are confusing the fact that though Abyssal creatures use the spirit and goetic templates, they are -not- spirits or goetia and thus are not necessarily affected by the arcana you're complaining about. Heck, you could whip up an Abyssal creature that isn't effected by any of the arcana and it would still use the goetia/spirit template.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T04:50:35-08:00","id":1058897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058890#post1058890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The state of mutually assured destruction is why you don't have Masters going around nuking people.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no MAD, you just have to be first to shoot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058890#post1058890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the logic of the Cold War, and like in our world's history, what you do is have proxy wars and politicking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actual ability of Masters to challenge each other and have interesting and cool wizard battles won't change that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058890#post1058890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? No out of context problems? <b>The Lie</b>, being the state of the entire world.<b> Exarchs</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't do anything about them. Period. Werewolves can beat Idigam, at least in theory. There is no way for any mage (not an archmage) to even inconvenience Exarch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","user":"Dark Archon","date":". 03-06-2017, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T04:51:46-08:00","id":1058898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058897#post1058897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't do anything about them. Period. Werewolves can beat Idigam, at least in theory. There is no way for any mage (not an archmage) to even inconvenience Exarch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Broken Diamond would disagree with that assertion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T04:51:58-08:00","id":1058899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058890#post1058890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The state of mutually assured destruction is why you don't have Masters going around nuking people. It's the logic of the Cold War</div> </div> </div> </div>An armed society is a polite society, and I imagine mages are VERY polite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T04:52:40-08:00","id":1058900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058893#post1058893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they are -not- spirits or goetia and thus are not necessarily affected by the arcana yo