Fallen and Supernal Realms counts, just like killing one or two servant-spirits of Idigam doesn't count as &quot;dealing with Idigam&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T05:35:04-08:00","id":1058921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058897#post1058897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no MAD, you just have to be first to shoot.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to presume a white room scenario. A Master doesn't just pop up out of nowhere, they have a place in the society, friends, allies, lovers, family, the Consilium with laws. So it's not just the president who pushes the button that you have to take out, it's everyone else too.<br /> <br /> And the nuking Master is still just human, 7 health boxes on average, 10 if you want, so even if non-Master mages can't insta-kill them, they have plenty of ways of taking them out. And for breaching the MAD (which I still posit exists, of course the offense being the killing of another Mage) the Consilium, the Guardians, they will take action.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058897#post1058897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actual ability of Masters to challenge each other and have interesting and cool wizard battles won't change that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Duel Arcane. The civil way of having cool wizard battles.<br /> Because they know they can both throw around ungodly amounts of lethal or aggravated damage and likely just go for instakill, just like two humans with guns at point blank range of one another. So you don't do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can't do anything about them. Period. Werewolves can beat Idigam, at least in theory. There is no way for any mage (not an archmage) to even inconvenience Exarch. </div> </div> </div>Sure you can. What do Masters do after they deal with whatever minor gods are inconveniencing them? Become archmasters and go for the Exarch's throat. Or at least a painful anklebite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11842,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","user":"Aeryes","date":".  Health box count edit. 03-06-2017, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T05:44:58-08:00","id":1058923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058921#post1058921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems to presume a white room scenario. A Master doesn't just pop up out of nowhere, they have a place in the society, friends, allies, lovers, family, the Consilium with laws. So it's not just the president who pushes the button that you have to take out, it's everyone else too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good thing that, as a Master, you too have society, friends, allies, lovers, family, the Consilium with laws and alike, which may as well be on your side. In case all those are even matter and you aren't just going to burn a local Seer pylon for their heresy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058921#post1058921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Duel Arcane. The civil way of having cool wizard battles.<br /> Because they know they can both throw around ungodly amounts of lethal or aggravated damage and likely just go for instakill, just like two humans with guns at point blank range of one another. So you don't do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there is no reason for wizard battles to be equivalent of two humans with guns, and not, let's say, two fencers with rapiers. Except second one is more interesting, both mechanically and story-wise.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058921#post1058921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure you can. What do Masters do after they deal with whatever minor gods are inconveniencing them? Become archmasters and go for the Exarch's throat. Or at least a painful anklebite.</div> </div> </div> </div> You, Mage, can't. Archmages aren't characters of MtAw 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T05:51:42-08:00","id":1058926,"title":"","content":"@Areyes Or they become slashers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T07:05:35-08:00","id":1058964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058923#post1058923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good thing that, as a Master, you too have society, friends, allies, lovers, family, the Consilium with laws and alike, which may as well be on your side. In case all those are even matter and you aren't just going to burn a local Seer pylon for their heresy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, my point exactly. You launch a nuke, you blow up a city. The country/consilium/ministry then retaliates. MAD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058923#post1058923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there is no reason for wizard battles to be equivalent of two humans with guns, and not, let's say, two fencers with rapiers. Except second one is more interesting, both mechanically and story-wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! Duel Arcane! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> That is if you mean fencers with protective gear, for points.<br /> With actual swords going for blood, it will either be to first blood, ending again with the first in initiative order, or it will go for a few more rounds, with advantage to the first in initiative order. Not sure that's much better really, but you can have the Duel Arcane do health boxes of damage if that's your thing. But fencers dueling to the death are about winning by their mastery of their art, which for Mages would be &quot;you're gone now.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058923#post1058923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b You, Mage, can't. Archmages aren't characters of MtAw 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, point. How about abyssal intruders? Those seem like they could pose a challenge, in a Mystery sort of way? <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13063_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13063\" data-vbnamecard=\"13063\">Lord Jub-Jub</a> Sure, if Mages are against killing or something. Or they find themselves home, with no memory of last night, or anything supernatural, and decided to take their teaching career more seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T07:13:52-08:00","id":1058969,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11842_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11842\" data-vbnamecard=\"11842\">Aeryes</a> you don't have to survive to become a Slasher. Freddy Krueger didn't make it out of the house fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T07:28:01-08:00","id":1058976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058964#post1058964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, my point exactly. You launch a nuke, you blow up a city. The country/consilium/ministry then retaliates. MAD.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because you can win this battle - there is no <b>assured </b>destruction. You can fight Consilium/Ministry and win. Not without losses on your side, of course, but there is no MAD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058964#post1058964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly! Duel Arcane! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> That is if you mean fencers with protective gear, for points.<br /> With actual swords going for blood, it will either be to first blood, ending again with the first in initiative order, or it will go for a few more rounds, with advantage to the first in initiative order. Not sure that's much better really, but you can have the Duel Arcane do health boxes of damage if that's your thing. But fencers dueling to the death are about winning by their mastery of their art, which for Mages would be &quot;you're gone now.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You kinda misunderstand me. I am saying that actual magical battle, Master against Master, to the death, need not to be mexican stand-off with two Unmaking spells. It could be made actual battle: with opening moves, gambits, feints, ruses and endgames, using all kinds of Practices. And that would be more interesting than that we have now.<br /> Duel Arcana mechanically is boring, there is even a thread about it: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057400-magic-duels-as-boring-as-they-seem\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...g-as-they-seem</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058964#post1058964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, point. How about abyssal intruders? Those seem like they could pose a challenge, in a Mystery sort of way?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they use rules for ephemeral entities <b>and </b>influenced by Arcana? No, they can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T07:30:07-08:00","id":1058978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058969#post1058969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11842_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11842\" data-vbnamecard=\"11842\">Aeryes</a> you don't have to survive to become a Slasher. Freddy Krueger didn't make it out of the house fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>A good point, a good point. On the other hand, he wasn't Unmade. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Or for more reasonable Mages, who can't just Unmake the Hunter in question, they can still kill him with one or two spells, not necessarily visible ones either.<br /> That is to say, I don't think the Hunter would get sufficiently broken in the short amount of time he would be dealt with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T07:38:29-08:00","id":1058984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058976#post1058976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they use rules for ephemeral entities <b>and </b>influenced by Arcana? No, they can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again just because they use the rules for ephemeral entities doesn't mean they actually are ephemeral entities or interact with the arcana in the usual way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T07:42:04-08:00","id":1058986,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11842_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11842\" data-vbnamecard=\"11842\">Aeryes</a> that's assuming the Mage even notices them. Could be he doesn't want to take the wisdom hit for killing them, teleports or turns invisible or some other magic mumbo jumbo to get away, the hunters get affected by the sleeping curse, go mad trying to remember what happens because Hunters. they start suspecting everyone of being witches because of the memory holes and such, end up targeting innocents then become slashers. All the while the Mage they went after in the first place was too busy dealing with some rival Mage or some order politics or dealing with the seers or whatever and never noticed that his actions lead to that cell of strange witchhunters becoming mad men. Not everyone a hunter goes after is necessarily evil, they could well have tried to go after a nice young Mage with stars in his eyes, maybe even freshly awakened and still kind of clinging to humanity and, through his inexperience, got too flashy and ended up making his own rouges gallery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T08:04:26-08:00","id":1058994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058984#post1058984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again just because they use the rules for ephemeral entities doesn't mean they actually are ephemeral entities or interact with the arcana in the usual way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Self-contradicting. If they use the rules for ephemeral entities, that means they use Arcana rules for interacting as such. If not, that needs to be clarified. And I stressed out <b>and </b>- if they are influenced by Arcana, mages can do whatever they want with them. As they are, they lack good writeup to be real antagonists. Strix and Idigam both got their own chapter with write-up and examples. Abyssal entities roughly got a sidebar and a note.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T08:10:29-08:00","id":1058998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058994#post1058994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Self-contradicting. If they use the rules for ephemeral entities, that means they use Arcana rules for interacting as such. If not, that needs to be clarified. And I stressed out <b>and </b>- if they are influenced by Arcana, mages can do whatever they want with them. As they are, they lack good writeup to be real antagonists. Strix and Idigam both got their own chapter with write-up and examples. Abyssal entities roughly got a sidebar and a note.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty clear they're supposed to be weird from the sidebar dedicated to them in ways that break the normal ephemeral rules. Those rules are a skeleton to build an Abyssal entity on, not a dictation for how they interact with the arcana. If you want example Abyssal stuff there's plenty of source material in the 1e stuff, but the category of Abyss covers a whole lot more territory than the Idigam and Strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T08:23:30-08:00","id":1059010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058998#post1058998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty clear they're supposed to be weird from the sidebar dedicated to them in ways that break the normal ephemeral rules. Those rules are a skeleton to build an Abyssal entity on, not a dictation for how they interact with the arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you prefer skeleton rules which you have to figure out by yourself, that's on you. I prefer clearly outlined rules with coulds and could-nots directly stated in the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058998#post1058998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want example Abyssal stuff there's plenty of source material in the 1e stuff, but the category of Abyss covers a whole lot more territory than the Idigam and Strix.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the more reason to give them their own space and better outline them, if they are truly the antagonist of the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T08:27:31-08:00","id":1059012,"title":"","content":"They're not necessarily -the- antagonist, they're just one of them. And the skeleton provided is pretty clear, you just need a little imagination to expand into making them as bizarre as they're supposed to be. You were talking earlier about liking to make up your own truths for a setting, the Abyssa ought to be your playground then instead of something to gripe about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T08:30:07-08:00","id":1059014,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13063_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13063\" data-vbnamecard=\"13063\">Lord Jub-Jub</a> Sounds about right for a new mage, nice nice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058976#post1058976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, because you can win this battle - there is no <b>assured </b>destruction. You can fight Consilium/Ministry and win. Not without losses on your side, of course, but there is no MAD.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can? The idea of a Mage cold war theme is that the Consilia don't want to go to war if it's not needed. The aggressor loses.<br /> <br /> You can kill a Master that pissed you off, but that makes you a criminal to your own Consilium. You can fight an entire Consilium and win? Lost me there.<br /> <br /> You plus your Consilium could win against the local branch of a Ministry, maybe, this is true,but with plenty of losses and with a greater war with the Seers initiated. Sure, there's place for a 'let loose the dogs of war' kind of chronicle, but in general your Consilium won't follow you into this crazy venture precisely because of the 'plenty of losses' part, because Mages aren't a dime a dozen.<br /> <br /> So it's not you and your Consilium. You will likely get a punishment for violating some Lex Magica thing. Though probably nobody likes the Seers so a reprimand. More significantly, you'll be expected to clean up your mess. Solo. (well, with your cabal) Assured? Well no. But highly likely? Yes. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You kinda misunderstand me. I am saying that actual magical battle, Master against Master, to the death, need not to be mexican stand-off with two Unmaking spells. It could be made actual battle: with opening moves, gambits, feints, ruses and endgames, using all kinds of Practices. And that would be more interesting than that we have now.<br /> Duel Arcana mechanically is boring, there is even a thread about it: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057400-magic-duels-as-boring-as-they-seem\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...g-as-they-seem</a> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't sure which version you meant, yes. <br /> <br /> The wizardly duel your propose falls into the same problems any kind of duel falls into: you want it to be dramatic and ceremonial, but the participants just want to win. If it's to the death, and you know your Unmaking can end it before it truly begins, ending any threat to you, why not use it? There's no greater honor in being barely alive over a dead foe than in a flawless victory. So we have the Duel Arcane. Because unless you think your opponent is such a horrible creature they deserve ending right there and then, you don't want to remove another Master from the world.<br /> <br /> My love for the Duel Arcane has started before I knew what it was, in reading Dave's Actual Play. It was glorious <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I sadly agree with the mechanics issue pointed out in the thread. It doesn't engage the mechanics-enthusiasts among us. But consider this, how would you mechanically portray a fencing match? Attacks and defenses, ripostes if you mange to defend well or the attacker attacks poorly. Mechanically not all that cool. But narratively great. Same for the Duel Arcane.<br /> <br /> Just ... maybe a bit more than &quot;attack or defend.&quot; Maybe each declared attack is matched with a declared defense, in contested rolls. And whichever one fails, that Arcanum can't be used again or takes a -1 like Defense does.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T08:42:34-08:00","id":1059018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1058994#post1058994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Self-contradicting. If they use the rules for ephemeral entities, that means they use Arcana rules for interacting as such. If not, that needs to be clarified. And I stressed out <b>and </b>- if they are influenced by Arcana, mages can do whatever they want with them. As they are, they lack good writeup to be real antagonists. Strix and Idigam both got their own chapter with write-up and examples. Abyssal entities roughly got a sidebar and a note.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree that a more detailed write up would be good, but I think the sidebars are reasonably explained considering the word count they got. In my opinion the side bars are excellent for describing a piece of the setting (and how to interact with it) despite lacking the word count for properly including it.<br /> And I want to point out that the Abyssal Entities sidebar doesn't say they use the <i>same </i>rules. They use <i>similar </i>rules.<br /> While MtA by nature suffers from ill explained rules (due to limited word count, limited QA (OPP is not exactly WotC) and featuring a very complex system) at a certain point I think the writers are entitled to assuming the reader uses their common sense when interpreting the text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T08:50:07-08:00","id":1059020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059014#post1059014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of a Mage cold war theme</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes, thank you for bringing up that kind of theme, which I dislike strongly, too. It's fine theme, but building mechanics around it so it is literally impossible to have magical &quot;hot war&quot; is a terrible game design.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059014#post1059014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can kill a Master that pissed you off, but that makes you a criminal to your own Consilium. You can fight an entire Consilium and win? Lost me there.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really not assured destruction, that highly depends on Master and Consilium.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059014#post1059014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You plus your Consilium could win against the local branch of a Ministry</div> </div> </div> </div>So, no MAD. End of story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059014#post1059014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wizardly duel your propose falls into the same problems any kind of duel falls into: you want it to be dramatic and ceremonial, but the participants just want to win. If it's to the death, and you know your Unmaking can end it before it truly begins, ending any threat to you, why not use it?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... a really, really strange question. If it's duel to the death, and you can just penertrate the heart of your enemy, why not just do it? Because you can't: he will block, or parry, or evade. Why can't Master just Unmake other Master? Because other Master will dispel, counter or evade his spell. Game mechanics won't allow this? Well, all the more reason to change mechanics so they would support cool magical duels to death, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059014#post1059014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My love for the Duel Arcane has started before I knew what it was, in reading Dave's Actual Play. It was glorious <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Can't share it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059014#post1059014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But consider this, how would you mechanically portray a fencing match?</div> </div> </div> </div>You need a list of systems in which you could do it, and it would be interesting?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","user":"Dark Archon","date":". 03-06-2017, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T09:33:18-08:00","id":1059036,"title":"","content":"Just ran my first session of Mage 2e yesterday and Down and Dirty Spellcasting is the best thing ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T09:56:02-08:00","id":1059049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059020#post1059020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, yes, thank you for bringing up that kind of theme, which I dislike strongly, too. It's fine theme, but building mechanics around it so it is literally impossible to have magical &quot;hot war&quot; is a terrible game design.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I was going to take you seriously, and then you trot out this, &quot;Oh, the game isn't designed to do something I want to do, so it's bad game design,&quot; and I'm like why bother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T09:57:47-08:00","id":1059050,"title":"","content":"Not to mention an untrue accusation to level at the game. A Cold War stance is encouraged and the accepted default of the setting, but Chronicles exist to change the status quo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T10:17:41-08:00","id":1059058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059049#post1059049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I was going to take you seriously, and then you trot out this, &quot;Oh, the game isn't designed to do something I want to do, so it's bad game design,&quot; and I'm like why bother.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, look at the name of the thread. Second, you are correct. This isn't a bad game design, but isn't a design I'd like. IMO, mechanics should support as many themes as possible, not just one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T10:22:35-08:00","id":1059060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059058#post1059058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, look at the name of the thread. Second, you are correct. This isn't a bad game design, but isn't a design I'd like. IMO, mechanics should support as many themes as possible, not just one.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no such thing as a game that does it all despite the numerous attempts to create one. It's a pointless complaint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T10:23:30-08:00","id":1059061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059060#post1059060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no such thing as a game that does it all despite the numerous attempts to create one. It's a pointless complaint.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a number of games which do it well enough for me to play them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T10:25:46-08:00","id":1059062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059020#post1059020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's... a really, really strange question. If it's duel to the death, and you can just penertrate the heart of your enemy, why not just do it? Because you can't: he will block, or parry, or evade. Why can't Master just Unmake other Master? Because other Master will dispel, counter or evade his spell. Game mechanics won't allow this? Well, all the more reason to change mechanics so they would support cool magical duels to death, right?<br /> <br /> You need a list of systems in which you could do it, and it would be interesting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a list of systems, just a way to do it in MtAw2E.<br /> And to do it in a way that doesn't take most of a session every time a handful of Mages meet enemy Mages. Also in a way that includes multiple combatants, because outside of a prepared setting like the Duel Arcane, there will be outside intervention.<br /> <br /> The themes and system design of 2E does seem to go against this kind of thing, so I can see why the writers didn't include Mages' systems for a magical fencing match.<br /> <br /> If you have a way of doing it that makes for some sort of balance, as this seems to be the sort of thing you want and Mage2E doesn't, do tell <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T10:30:09-08:00","id":1059063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059062#post1059062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have a way of doing it that makes for some sort of balance, as this seems to be the sort of thing you want and Mage2E doesn't, do tell <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>One really need to think it through, but as it is now, Mages are really need to have more ways to defend against spells reliably for that kind of magical battles. Something definitely needs to be done with Counterspell, for example. As it is now, it's non-option in one-on-one fights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T10:35:38-08:00","id":1059064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059061#post1059061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a number of games which do it well enough for me to play them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great, Mage isn't one of them. You're entitled to your opinion, but it's still a pointless complaint to level at Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T10:36:20-08:00","id":1059065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059060#post1059060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no such thing as a game that does it all despite the numerous attempts to create one. It's a pointless complaint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ascension did. You could run gritty down to earth or spaceship pirate battles on jupiter or something in between. There was even the storyteller guide which was a guide to shit on the setting and run steampunk adventure or pulp even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T10:37:12-08:00","id":1059066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059065#post1059065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ascension did. You could run gritty down to earth or spaceship pirate battles on jupiter or something in between. There was even the storyteller guide which was a guide to shit on the setting and run steampunk adventure or pulp even.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great, that's still not this version of Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T10:42:48-08:00","id":1059069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059066#post1059066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great, that's still not this version of Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>No reason why this version of Mage couldn't be done a little bit differently and support both &quot;cold war&quot; and &quot;hot war&quot; settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T10:45:47-08:00","id":1059072,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say it's pointless. It's fair to say &quot;I don't consider Mage 2nd ed to be thematically flexible enough in certain ways to attract me&quot; and that's, you know, a perfectly reasonable criticism and it does have a point of expressing a preference and stating that a game doesn't match it.<br /> <br /> Personally I don't agree, and even if I did, I like the somewhat cold war-ish element of Mage society, but regardless, it's not a pointless complaint. It's a con, in the eyes of some, and that's what this thread is about.<br /> <br /> As for my own opinion; I still like pretty much everything about Mage, with the notable exception of Wisdom. But yeah, it's a fantastic game overall. Quality setting and really the best freeform magic system I've ever seen, I think. It's still my preference not to use it with other CofD splats because honestly, I prefer the idea that Mages are the Vamps and Wolves of the setting when I play Mage (Liches and shapeshifters etc), but that's easy enough, just only use mage things!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T10:46:18-08:00","id":1059074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059065#post1059065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ascension did. You could run gritty down to earth or spaceship pirate battles on jupiter or something in between. There was even the storyteller guide which was a guide to shit on the setting and run steampunk adventure or pulp even.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many would argue that the Ascension <i><b>tried </b></i>to be a game that did it all, yet repeatedly fell well short edition after edition, up to and including M20.<br /> <br /> Usually when you try to do and be everything to all people, nothing is done particularly well.<br /> <br /> I've been a fan of both iterations of Mage since Ascension's release in the mid 1990's, but it would be foolish not to acknowledge the myriad of setting and mechanical problems with Ascension that are near legendary. Ascension was and still is a groundbreaking game, but that doesn't necessarily mean it was a well designed and easily playable game.<br /> <br /> I respect that some may not like all or part of Awakening because it's not designed to accomplish want they want in a ttrpg. However, the determination of whether a game is well designed is whether it accomplishes its <i>intended</i> goals and the fans enjoy it, not whether some people effectively want a different game entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":".  typos 03-06-2017, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T10:50:16-08:00","id":1059075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059069#post1059069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No reason why this version of Mage couldn't be done a little bit differently and support both &amp;quot;cold war&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;hot war&amp;quot; settings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it can, Chronicles exist to change the status who.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T10:56:52-08:00","id":1059078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059072#post1059072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say it's pointless. It's fair to say &quot;I don't consider Mage 2nd ed to be thematically flexible enough in certain ways to attract me&quot; and that's, you know, a perfectly reasonable criticism and it does have a point of expressing a preference and stating that a game doesn't match it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, at the end, it's what I mean. I love the setting; it's certain thematic mechanics (at least I think they are designed with theme in mind) which quirk me out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T11:30:48-08:00","id":1059088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059049#post1059049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I was going to take you seriously, and then you trot out this, &quot;Oh, the game isn't designed to do something I want to do, so it's bad game design,&quot; and I'm like why bother.</div> </div> </div> </div>However he does bring a good point, the game seems focused on a cold war setting wise but for the cold war to have any effect there has to be the danger of a hot war. There is a reason the &quot;doomsday clock&quot; is such a powerful image. Its not a con of the game the inability to run other genres (say high fantasy) but it is a con in the system not be able to run scenarios inside the genre it belongs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T12:14:16-08:00","id":1059108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059088#post1059088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However he does bring a good point, the game seems focused on a cold war setting wise but for the cold war to have any effect there has to be the danger of a hot war. There is a reason the &amp;quot;doomsday clock&amp;quot; is such a powerful image. Its not a con of the game the inability to run other genres (say high fantasy) but it is a con in the system not be able to run scenarios inside the genre it belongs.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is the threat of a hot war, anyone who goes too far is inviting the end of the standoff and the Pentacle and the Seers go to war without reservation. Then reality breaks again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T12:16:57-08:00","id":1059110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059108#post1059108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then reality breaks again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without Archmasters and Ascended going into the fray? No, it won't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T12:17:39-08:00","id":1059111,"title":"","content":"Cold War was full of armed conflicts, though. Cold Cold War where smallest aggression escalates everything into end of the days isn't particularly interesting, because it reinforces inaction and not-doing stuff, which isn't particularly interesting thing to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T12:56:53-08:00","id":1059138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059110#post1059110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without Archmasters and Ascended going into the fray? No, it won't.</div> </div> </div> </div>APs I've read beg to differ. People have told stories of Mages breaking reality without going up the tier that far. So the empirical evidence says you're wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T13:03:56-08:00","id":1059145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059138#post1059138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">APs I've read beg to differ. People have told stories of Mages breaking reality without going up the tier that far. So the empirical evidence says you're wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about which kind of empirical evidence you are talking about. Mages can't break the Tellurian - Archmages and Ascended Beings won't allow it. In fact, if we take Imperial Mysteries as canon, everything normal mages hardly matter - next Imperial Rite will overwrite reality one way or another. The fact that some players played differently in their game don't change that. The only &quot;hot war&quot; which can happen in setting is Ascension War, and it isn't started by normal mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T13:18:25-08:00","id":1059154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059138#post1059138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> APs I've read beg to differ. People have told stories of Mages breaking reality without going up the tier that far. So the empirical evidence says you're wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you are equating other people games, home game btw, as empirical evidence? There are many people that run vampire game in which diablere happen as a way to level up, is that empirical evidence that diablere that diablere is leveling up for all vampires? <br /> <br /> That some people take artistic liberties or just ran the game without caring for how the rules work in favor of fun doesnt equate empirical evidence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T13:34:43-08:00","id":1059167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059145#post1059145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about which kind of empirical evidence you are talking about. Mages can't break the Tellurian - Archmages and Ascended Beings won't allow it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They might not have a choice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only &quot;hot war&quot; which can happen in setting is Ascension War, and it isn't started by normal mages. </div> </div> </div>That's untrue. The core setting doesn't have a lot of Seer on Pentacle conflicts but they do happen. WHW had it. Even in a cold war there's plenty of armed conflicts. Tools and pawns war and get discarded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T13:43:44-08:00","id":1059171,"title":"","content":"Just imagine that Awakened's proxy wars equivalent is Cabals vs Cabals or Pylons vs Cabals (etc), where Consilia, Assemblies and Seers officially withdraw their support of the &quot;warring states&quot; but might allow volunteers to join in as long as they make sure to say they are flying their own colors, not whatever bigger organization they belong to (even if that organization told them to do so; plausible deniability).<br /> Of course, this doesn't change the fact that such conflicts can be ended by a barrage of &quot;shot first&quot; Direct Damage spells, but if you want to avoid that, add Withstand rating to them or rule that pile-up damage doesn't work due to stacking or whatever. This approach will allow you to still have small but intense dramatic conflicts while maintaining the cold war scenario.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Basically, if you want more freedom in conflicts, make sure that your local Law allows Pentacle to save face by having some mechanisms for saying &quot;can't be helped, they need to duke it out, lets not interfere and Oracles bless the just&quot;. This also handily shifts focus from &quot;big organizations hulking it out&quot; to &quot;individuals hulking it out while big organizations observe them looking for easy and heartless profit&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-06-2017, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T13:51:27-08:00","id":1059179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059167#post1059167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They might not have a choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beings that can rewrite a source code of reality might not have a choice?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059167#post1059167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's untrue. The core setting doesn't have a lot of Seer on Pentacle conflicts but they do happen. WHW had it. Even in a cold war there's plenty of armed conflicts. Tools and pawns war and get discarded.</div> </div> </div> </div>You see, those Seer on Pentacle conflicts are exactly that - proxy wars for Archmages and Ascended Beings. But they aren't &quot;hot war&quot; in any sense - they can't threaten basic nature of reality and it's masters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T14:02:48-08:00","id":1059188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059179#post1059179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beings that can rewrite a source code of reality might not have a choice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Archmasters are rarely of one mind. Even if one faction wants something to happen, another faction might want to opposite, and since open conflict/use of Imperial magic in the material world is forbidden, they'll probably need to use proxies to get things done, and those proxies are typically normal mages, who can fail at their given task just as easily as they can fail at anything else.<br /> <br /> This isn't even taking into consideration any of the other major players outside of the Archmages and what strange things they might seek to gain from something. So yes, sometimes they don't have a choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T14:06:42-08:00","id":1059192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059179#post1059179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beings that can rewrite a source code of reality might not have a choice?</div> </div> </div> </div>When there's an entire ocean of unreality that can take the choice from them, sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You see, those Seer on Pentacle conflicts are exactly that - proxy wars for Archmages and Ascended Beings. But they aren't &quot;hot war&quot; in any sense - they can't threaten basic nature of reality and it's masters. </div> </div> </div>They certainly can, there's plenty of seams ready to rip open, things like the Bound or Abyssal entities waiting to upset the balance with a word from a mortal.<br /> <br /> As for the hot wars, just because they're not apocalyptic doesn't mean they're not hot wars. What the Symbol of Fire feels about how things turned out doesn't matter to Jack the mage as he's getting the flesh seared from his bones because he didn't see the Banisher hiding behind a van.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of problems one can take from the game, but the only way 'nothing you do matters' comes into it is if you specifically decide that's how it works, while ignoring the rest of the setting saying otherwise.<br /> <br /> It's a problem that's only a problem when you make it one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T14:09:07-08:00","id":1059196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059145#post1059145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about which kind of empirical evidence you are talking about. Mages can't break the Tellurian - Archmages and Ascended Beings won't allow it. In fact, if we take Imperial Mysteries as canon, everything normal mages hardly matter - next Imperial Rite will overwrite reality one way or another. The fact that some players played differently in their game don't change that. The only &amp;quot;hot war&amp;quot; which can happen in setting is Ascension War, and it isn't started by normal mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>The empirical evidence is the fact that I've seen games that have done it. That ought to illustrate to you, unless you're being deliberately obtuse, that it can be done. Literally the only thing stopping you is that you think you can't do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T14:14:17-08:00","id":1059200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059196#post1059196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The empirical evidence is the fact that I've seen games that have done it. That ought to illustrate to you, unless you're being deliberately obtuse, that it can be done. Literally the only thing stopping you is that you think you can't do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can do game in which Initiate of Mind dominate Exarch of Mind and destroys Supernal Realm. It proves literally nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T14:16:20-08:00","id":1059202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059200#post1059200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can do game in which Initiate of Mind dominate Exarch of Mind and destroys Supernal Realm. It proves literally nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does actually prove that you could create a game that's a hot war, or where the Exarchs can be toppled by regular Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T14:17:55-08:00","id":1059204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059196#post1059196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The empirical evidence is the fact that I've seen games that have done it. That ought to illustrate to you, unless you're being deliberately obtuse, that it can be done. Literally the only thing stopping you is that you think you can't do it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are mistaking empirical evidence with anecdotal evidence. The former is more valid than the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T14:20:01-08:00","id":1059206,"title":"","content":"I think the problem is that one side is saying &quot;this can't be done within the confines of the rules and setting&quot; and the other side is saying &quot;this can be done if you ignore the rules and alter the setting.&quot; It is not the same argument, and therefore neither can ever come to any kind of resolution. Where do you go from there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T14:20:13-08:00","id":1059208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059188#post1059188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Archmasters are rarely of one mind. Even if one faction wants something to happen, another faction might want to opposite, and since open conflict/use of Imperial magic in the material world is forbidden, they'll probably need to use proxies to get things done, and those proxies are typically normal mages, who can fail at their given task just as easily as they can fail at anything else..</div> </div> </div> </div>And all this still happens in the Fallen reality, doesn't touch Supernal in the slightest and might be as well overdone by next Archmage which decide it's a good time to make Atlantis real again by rewriting history. How is this &quot;hot war&quot; again?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059192#post1059192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the hot wars, just because they're not apocalyptic doesn't mean they're not hot wars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please do recall that is Cold War in this case and what was the alternative. Hot war is apocalyptic conflict which threatens to wreck Tellurian beyond any repair, which is just not going to happen without Archmasters, Ascended beings and Rank 6+ spirits entering the fray, because anything their lessers do, they can undo.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059202#post1059202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does actually prove that you could create a game that's a hot war, or where the Exarchs can be toppled by regular Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not without completely ignoring the setting material on what Exarchs are and what they can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T14:37:01-08:00","id":1059214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059208#post1059208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And all this still happens in the Fallen reality, doesn't touch Supernal in the slightest and might be as well overdone by next Archmage which decide it's a good time to make Atlantis real again by rewriting history. How is this &quot;hot war&quot; again?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Supernal and Fallen aren't that disconnected. The Fallen influences the Supernal just as much as the Supernal influences it. Archmages still rely on the Fallen in order to Exalt their Omens, and if things change sufficiently, their Omens might become impossible. But with everyone having conflicting views on what's what, if someone changes something one way, another might change it back using their own Imperium Rite. So the state of the world is as important to Archmages as it is anyone, and they still aren't allows to use the full extent of their power to do what they want due to the Pax so they still need to work through proxies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T14:39:35-08:00","id":1059217,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Broken Diamond is as valid anecdotal evidence as Wyrd's tales of a bunch of Arcanum 4 mages one shotting a royal avatar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T14:45:18-08:00","id":1059219,"title":"","content":"Were any houserules used in Broken Diamond? Or any deviations from the setting as presented (as opposed to filling in blanks)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T15:33:14-08:00","id":1059236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059204#post1059204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are mistaking empirical evidence with anecdotal evidence. The former is more valid than the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually not, the question is, &quot;Can the game lead to hot war scenarios or to breaking the way the world currently is portrayed in Mage, or can Mages topple the Exarchs.&quot; If you count the games where it happens then you have empirical evidence that yes, those things can happen. It's at least a 1:0 point of evidence against your argument that status quo is god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T15:37:22-08:00","id":1059238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059236#post1059236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm actually not, the question is, &quot;Can the game lead to hot war scenarios or to breaking the way the world currently is portrayed in Mage, or can Mages topple the Exarchs.&quot; If you count the games where it happens then you have empirical evidence that yes, those things can happen. It's at least a 1:0 point of evidence against your argument that status quo is god.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was waiting on the answer to my question about Broken Diamond, but this was going to be my response as well.<br /> <br /> If a game can be run without houserules or explicit and significant deviation from the written setting where these activities are done then the statement 'A game cannot be run where you do these things' is EMPIRICALLY false. And yes that is the correct use of empirical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T15:39:43-08:00","id":1059242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059238#post1059238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was waiting on the answer to my question about Broken Diamond, but this was going to be my response as well.<br /> <br /> If a game can be run without houserules or explicit and significant deviation from the written setting where these activities are done then the statement 'A game cannot be run where you do these things' is EMPIRICALLY false. And yes that is the correct use of empirical.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Broken Diamond was straight by the book. Soul Cage is mostly by the book, the only real exception was the creation of a legacy, -but- it followed the rules for creating them, so it wasn't really house rules in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T15:42:47-08:00","id":1059245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059242#post1059242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe Broken Diamond was straight by the book. Soul Cage is mostly by the book, the only real exception was the creation of a legacy, -but- it followed the rules for creating them, so it wasn't really house rules in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree that wouldn't be a houserule in my mind either. I sadly haven't had time to read either of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T15:52:23-08:00","id":1059246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059219#post1059219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were any houserules used in Broken Diamond? Or any deviations from the setting as presented (as opposed to filling in blanks)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda. It used the story skeleton of Reign of the Exarchs which has a fairly loose idea of the rules; the regalia of the Dethroned Queen are pretty much pure narrative. They have some quantifiable effects, but lots of them are kinda handwavy.<br /> <br /> Actually, most of the chronicles do that. I get the impression that designers tend to assume people are willing to play pretty fast and loose with the setting. The same seemed to be true of Ascension back in the day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T15:57:24-08:00","id":1059252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059246#post1059246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kinda. It used the story skeleton of Reign of the Exarchs which has a fairly loose idea of the rules; the regalia of the Dethroned Queen are pretty much pure narrative. They have some quantifiable effects, but lots of them are kinda handwavy.<br /> <br /> Actually, most of the chronicles do that. I get the impression that designers tend to assume people are willing to play pretty fast and loose with the setting. The same seemed to be true of Ascension back in the day.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When it comes to NPCs and strange powers/items, that is something that is always expected. As long as it is consistent with the setting (which isn't hard since the core principle of the setting is 'no neat boxes') then that is still playing by RAW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T22:08:17-08:00","id":1059348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059088#post1059088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However he does bring a good point, the game seems focused on a cold war setting wise but for the cold war to have any effect there has to be the danger of a hot war. There is a reason the &quot;doomsday clock&quot; is such a powerful image. Its not a con of the game the inability to run other genres (say high fantasy) but it is a con in the system not be able to run scenarios inside the genre it belongs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly who is it that determines what games it's supposed to be able to run, here? You guys are literally <i>assigning</i> the game a genre and then being confused when it doesn't fit perfectly.<br /> <br /> And that's without addressing whether or not you're correct on any of those points. My issue here is that you're selecting a critical method that makes it impossible to fairly evaluate the game.<br /> <br /> To address those actual points? The game is not a cold war setting. This is not Demon: the Descent. (Which is hilarious because imagining what a &quot;hot war&quot; looks like in D:tD is literally the wrath of god smiting shit left and right possibly including timeline erasure as a quarantine measure.) This is Mage: the Awakening.<br /> <br /> It is a game about detectives qua academics. It is not a game about international politics and the consequences of secrecy and escalation. It is not a fighty game. It is not trying to be. It is a game about curiosity and its consequences, of what happens when a hard-boiled PI can't seem to stop solving mysteries even though it makes him depressed and hurts everyone he loves. It's about what happens when a professor thrashes his research assistants into staying the night and refusing to let them have lives because his research is the most important thing in the world. Sure, these people live in a society that's filled with such people and, if any of them so chose to figure out how, they could pull out a gun that let them murder perfectly from across the city without leaving a trace or even a suspicion. But none of those people <i>want</i> to do that: they have their pet projects that they <i>actually</i> care about and all the other thick-skulls are either helping or in the way. The petty bickering of sects is just a bunch of blowhards who are trying to do terrible things like &quot;keep all the Mages from killing each other&quot; and &quot;maybe let's help each other out with our research projects sometimes, eh?&quot; and &quot;hey are you down here's something you can believe in&quot; and all that other shit that just flies over our heads on the international stage anyways. Like, isn't there a famine in Somalia right now or something?<br /> <br /> Yes, I get it. You want mage fights where one side lobs fireballs and the other side does some chanting and dancing and the fireballs are canceled out by fucking soap water. Cool beans. Lots of people want that. Awakening 2e is not good at it. You can judge it for that and whine about how it's so hard to drive screws using a sledgehammer, or you can, y'know, move on with your life and actually play something that does what you want. Or you can ask for help in hacking the setting and the systems to make it do what you want. I mean, you can totally make a screwdriver out of a sledgehammer.<br /> <br /> But Mage: the Awakening, like most Chronicles of Darkness games, is about personal lives and personal situations. It's not about The Star And The Throne, Magical War To End All Wars. It's about you and your cabal and the shit they just wander into 60% by accident and 40% &quot;Oh, we know this is a bad idea, but I can't help it I gotta do this&quot; because shit happens everywhere and you keep finding out about it and it never stops. Really, the point of the whole political deadlock in the upper echelons is to make the consequences of your actions that much more terrible when you realize how many fingers were in the pie you just torched. It's not &quot;you dun fucked up, I'm going to take away your badge and your gun&quot;. It's &quot;you dun fucked up, now there are god-tyrants who want your head on a plate and the Hierarch is seriously thinking about just letting that happen because you ain't too popular in the Consilium either after that last fuck up so maybe your only useful purpose in life, to them, is being bait&quot;.<br /> <br /> This isn't a game where you play the Hierarch and try to figure out how to line up your toy soldiers to foil the Seers at every turn. This is a game about people who are high on themselves and, at their most self-aware, say, &quot;Sorry, man, I can't help it. That's just who I am.&quot; And the Seers and the Scelesti and the Liches swoop in and go, &quot;That's cool, man. Who you are is great. Hurting people is the best because we have a bullshit philosophy that makes it okay. And you can do it some more if you swear your life your loyalty your soul, yeah?&quot;<br /> <br /> If you want a play a different game using this setting and these rules, that's cool and hell, you can probably make it work with effort and dedication on the part of you and your fellow players. But you don't get to say it's badly designed if it doesn't because it ain't fair to Frank Lloyd Wright that his house isn't spaceworthy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T22:11:36-08:00","id":1059351,"title":"","content":"I am on vacation and clearly have way too much time on my hands now. Sorry about the wordbarf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T01:17:01-08:00","id":1059384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059204#post1059204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You are mistaking empirical evidence with anecdotal evidence. The former is more valid than the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are confused about standards of evidence here.<br /> Dark Archon posited the theory that is't impossible to play a game that features Mages breaking reality without Archmages/Exarchs getting involved.<br /> To disprove a theory requires no more than a single piece of evidence! Whether Mrmdubois provides a statistically relevant number of examples or just a single one us utterly inconsequential, because one always enough to scrap a theory.<br /> <br /> You can now try to argue whether those groups were only able to do that because they somehow went against established facts of the setting to do that, but you'll have to do more than just claim that, because just saying &quot;That some people take artistic liberties or just ran the game without caring for how the rules work in favor of fun doesnt equate empirical evidence&quot; is a No true Scotsman argument. But as Mrmdubois can't be asked to prove that those groups <i>didn't</i> in some way go beyond the bounds established by setting and rules (that would require him to prove a negative, which is impossible) it's on your shoulders to prove that they <i>did.</i><br /> <br /> Sorry, just a pet peeve of mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T01:46:14-08:00","id":1059391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059348#post1059348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Mage: the Awakening, like most Chronicles of Darkness games, is about personal lives and personal situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which somehow absolutely cannot include cool magical duels, we got it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T01:49:31-08:00","id":1059393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059384#post1059384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dark Archon posited the theory that is't impossible to play a game that features Mages breaking reality without Archmages/Exarchs getting involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>You forgot the part about &quot;and assuming that Exarchs are still essentially all-mighty Gods&quot;. If you change this part, then of course you can topple them. If you don't, then any game in which your mighty Mind Apprentice dismantles Iron Pyramid just shits on logic and common sense. Which you can absolutely do in your game, of course. But that proves nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","user":"Dark Archon","date":". 03-07-2017, 04:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T01:52:15-08:00","id":1059394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059393#post1059393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You forgot the part about &quot;and assuming that Exarchs are still essentially all-mighty Gods&quot;. If you change this part, then of course you can topple them. If you don't, then any game in which your mighty Mind Apprentice dismantles Iron Pyramid is just shit on logic and common sense. Which you can absolutely do in your game, of course. But that proves nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly they're not almighty or Mages wouldn't keep Awakening or Ascending, or thwarting their plans in the first place. Powerful? Obviously. Infallible? Hardly.<br /> <br /> You're creating assumptions about the setting that don't actually exist. No wonder nothing makes sense to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T02:07:54-08:00","id":1059397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059394#post1059394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly they're not almighty or Mages wouldn't keep Awakening or Ascending</div> </div> </div> </div>Awakening is part of their plans - every mage in a potential Seer. &quot;Keep Ascending&quot;? Now that's an assumption: that Ascensions happen regularly and not once in a blue moon. And even when it would hardly matter if there is more Ascended Seers than other Mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059394#post1059394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thwarting their plans in the first place</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't see mages thwarting their plans on a scale which would matter, given that we are speaking creatures which control reality. Killing that one Seer and taking Artifact isn't &quot;thwarting their plans&quot;. On that scale it's hardly even matters. After all, if it would be that important, Exarch would've sent an Ochema, and good luck dealing with that as a Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T02:17:19-08:00","id":1059401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059397#post1059397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awakening is part of their plans - every mage in a potential Seer. &quot;Keep Ascending&quot;? Now that's an assumption: that Ascensions happen regularly and not once in a blue moon. And even when it would hardly matter if there is more Ascended Seers than other Mages.<br /> <br /> Don't see mages thwarting their plans on a scale which would matter, given that we are speaking creatures which control reality. Killing that one Seer and taking Artifact isn't &quot;thwarting their plans&quot;. On that scale it's hardly even matters. After all, if it would be that important, Exarch would've sent an Ochema, and good luck dealing with that as a Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages can beat Ochema, it might be difficult but that doesn't preclude the possibility. The Exarchs have certainly been thwarted on the grand scale before as well, such as the forming of the Free Council. Plus victory against the tyrants of the universe is obviously going to be a long term guerrilla effort for regular Mages. It will matter to the Exarchs in the long run if they keep being beaten, and in the immediate moment it certainly matters to those Mages who have won their particular conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T02:47:22-08:00","id":1059407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059397#post1059397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awakening is part of their plans - every mage in a potential Seer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. &quot;Conquer the Watchtowers&quot; is a central tenet of the Seer creed. If they controlled everything they might still want Awakenings, but as things stand they don't control it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T04:40:17-08:00","id":1059435,"title":"","content":"You can have very exciting fights in Mage, and not all Mages, or even most, are academic detectives. Otherwise you wouldn't be able to play Adamantine Arrow shitkickers looking for a good fight to test themselves, and you totally can.<br /> <br /> The game has a cold war feel but hot wars break out here and there a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T09:48:24-08:00","id":1059576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059435#post1059435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can have very exciting fights in Mage, and not all Mages, or even most, are academic detectives. Otherwise you wouldn't be able to play Adamantine Arrow shitkickers looking for a good fight to test themselves, and you totally can.<br /> <br /> The game has a cold war feel but hot wars break out here and there a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Batman never kicks ass? Dick Tracy never kicks ass? &quot;Hi, I'm Downey Jr. playing Sherlock Holmes and I will methodically plan out how I break your mind in these ten easy steps!&quot; Sam Spade? What is it about &quot;academic detectives&quot; that can't kick ass, exactly? Kicking ass is half of how they all get in trouble!<br /> <br /> Also I'm seriously tired of people who can't describe the Arrow as doing anything except running around beating people up. I realize y'all are RPG aficionados and everything, but &quot;Existence is War&quot; doesn't mean &quot;I relate to the world by punching people&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T09:55:37-08:00","id":1059581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059576#post1059576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I'm seriously tired of people who can't describe the Arrow as doing anything except running around beating people up. I realize y'all are RPG aficionados and everything, but &quot;Existence is War&quot; doesn't mean &quot;I relate to the world by punching people&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;it's not enough to bash in heads, you've got to bash in minds&quot;? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (but seriously, the Arrow as the ones who directly challenge power structures and idea barriers-the ones who are medical scientists finding cures because they've chosen to fight disease, or the ones in government fighting oppression-these Arrows are <i>fucking cool to play</i>.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-07-2017, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T09:58:21-08:00","id":1059584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059351#post1059351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am on vacation and clearly have way too much time on my hands now. Sorry about the wordbarf.</div> </div> </div> </div>...............<br /> <br /> Do I even need to explain why you don't need to apologize?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T10:02:21-08:00","id":1059587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059576#post1059576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Batman never kicks ass? Dick Tracy never kicks ass? &quot;Hi, I'm Downey Jr. playing Sherlock Holmes and I will methodically plan out how I break your mind in these ten easy steps!&quot; Sam Spade? What is it about &quot;academic detectives&quot; that can't kick ass, exactly? Kicking ass is half of how they all get in trouble!<br /> <br /> Also I'm seriously tired of people who can't describe the Arrow as doing anything except running around beating people up. I realize y'all are RPG aficionados and everything, but &quot;Existence is War&quot; doesn't mean &quot;I relate to the world by punching people&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say all Arrow Mages are just thugs and no detective can ever get into a fight. At no point did I say that.<br /> <br /> I said that an Arrow shitkicker is playable in the game as is, and that not all or even most Mages are academic detectives. Which is true, and not what you are inferring my point to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","user":"Solar","date":". 03-07-2017, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T12:23:17-08:00","id":1059664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059584#post1059584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...............<br /> <br /> Do I even need to explain why you don't need to apologize?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something, something, would unfortunately be a Mage in real life, something obsession, something addiction, something Wisdom, something something Prospero.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059587#post1059587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say all Arrow Mages are just thugs and no detective can ever get into a fight. At no point did I say that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's cool. But you just <i>had</i> to use an Arrow example instead of a Guardian shitkicker or a Mysterium shitkicker or a Ladder shitkicker because HAHAHA stereotypes are so fun guys!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059587#post1059587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said that an Arrow shitkicker is playable in the game as is, and that not all or even most Mages are academic detectives. Which is true, and not what you are inferring my point to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is your point, then? If those were genuinely all you meant to say, then you said absolutely nothing that I didn't.<br /> <br /> At no point did I say that Arrow shitkickers were unplayable. That's all you.<br /> At no point did I say that every mage has to play an academic detective. That's all you.<br /> <br /> You are literally jamming words in my mouth and then complaining about what I said. Which I'm not surprised by, since it's what y'all are doing with the game.<br /> <br /> You guys keep pulling out this &quot;hot war&quot; term as if you had any idea what it means. You seem to think it means back-alley fisticuffs when what it actually means is napalm scorching the jungle in Vietnam or mustard gas soaking the air above the trenches in France. It means blanketing the world in a cloud of ash while explosions rip apart city centers and fry electronics for miles around while fallout slowly infects every bit of flora and fauna down the waterways. It means horsemen running down children in the desert and battlefields soaked with blood and gore and smoke. That's what this &quot;cold war&quot; &quot;hot war&quot; shit comes from.<br /> <br /> The entire point of a &quot;cold war setting&quot; is that everyone is so panicked and afraid of what happens in a hot war that they are willing to throw <i>everything</i> away, especially and even their humanity, to avoid it.<br /> <br /> And. That's. Not. What. Mage: the Awakening. Is.<br /> <br /> Again.<br /> <br /> Mage is a game about <i>curiosity</i> becoming <i>obsession</i>. If you don't want to play a game around that, and you still want to use M:tAw systems, then you're going to have disappointments, things won't work quite as well as you want them to, and you're going to have to hack it to get optimal gameplay. And. That's. Fine. You can play a cold war game if you want. But you don't get to accuse the game of not catering to your hack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T12:37:08-08:00","id":1059675,"title":"","content":"Oh for God's sake get off your high horse. I'm not engaging in stereotypes I gave an example of a character one can play in the game, and you can, and it works fine. It's not nothing to do with stereotypes it's just that the Arrow are the most (right there! In the book!) martial of the Orders by design, so it's the easiest and most front-supported example I came up with.<br /> <br /> As for what war is clearly we're all using it as a phrase which means active violence between Mages rather than a deliberate restriction of offensive activity in order to avoid widespread destruction. But hey, bang on about Vietnam and napalm and nukes all you like, not that it's got a single bloody thing to do with what we're talking about at all.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I've run and played Mage and had plenty of great fights right out of the mechanics in the book with no house rules, plenty of magical duels, plenty of moments where the cold war between opposed Mages has gone hot. I've not no disappointments with the Mage system. I never voiced any disappointments with the Mage system. In your ridiculous screed. with. all. stops. about what Mage is you've been yelling about why Mage will disappoint me if I want to use it for the game I've actually, at the table, used it for and not been disappointed at all.<br /> <br /> I haven't accused the game of not catering to my hack and I've got no issue with how it plays either, so why don't you dial your quite frankly bizarre attitude back a bit there, mate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T14:17:29-08:00","id":1059742,"title":"","content":"Wait, how did the arguments about Hot Wars and Cold Wars pop up when we're talking about the Arrows? Whose main philosophy is about Obsession over the <i>existential </i>conflict between the I and the World? Who use physical, martial, and sometimes military prowess as a highly recommended but not required means of expressing that conflict?<br /> <br /> Obsessing over literal war and all the violence in it is what the Praetorians do, not the Arrows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T15:26:41-08:00","id":1059783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059742#post1059742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, how did the arguments about Hot Wars and Cold Wars pop up when we're talking about the Arrows? Whose main philosophy is about Obsession over the <i>existential </i>conflict between the I and the World? Who use physical, martial, and sometimes military prowess as a highly recommended but not required means of expressing that conflict?<br /> <br /> Obsessing over literal war and all the violence in it is what the Praetorians do, not the Arrows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hot wars vs. cold wars was an earlier part of the discussion that had some carry over into a bit about the Arrows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T20:29:43-08:00","id":1059910,"title":"","content":"Well trolled, Solar. Sounds like I have nothing of further value to add to this thread, since you agree with everything I've said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T01:59:20-08:00","id":1059995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd?p=1059910#post1059910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well trolled, Solar. Sounds like I have nothing of further value to add to this thread, since you agree with everything I've said.</div> </div> </div> </div>No trolling at all pal. I just made a comment in this thread that wasn't even directed at you and got all up in arms about it. If you'd taken the time to actually read my posts you could have avoided being quite so ridiculous, really, and we wouldn't have had this embarrassing little back and forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T18:28:14-08:00","id":1060719,"title":"","content":"In general, I like local and low-power games much more than global high power games. Thankfully, in general all I needed in order to make Mage little more like that was restricting 90 percent of mages in the world to Gnosis 3 or less, making Gnosis 4 rare and anything beyond that equivalent of Archmastery. I suggest that for anyone complaining about Mage power level, especially in comparison to other splats.<br /> <br /> One thing that bothers me even at these levels of play is how powerful Shielding and Veiling spells are. But that's mostly because I find blanket immunities and blanket undetectibalities lame.Invisible zombie squads, invisible mages battling other invisible mages using invisible means, etc. So far my preferred fix for it was nerfing blanket can't be perceived to &quot;will be casually overlooked unless Exceptional Success&quot; and &quot;suffers Potency in penalty to be actively detected&quot;/&quot;gains Potency in bonus to avoid detection&quot; [player trying to sneak into a crowded building will gain bonus, player being sneaked upon will gain a penalty to their detection roll].","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T03:01:47-08:00","id":1060794,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> Can I steal your game settings as a plot-hook-effect of an emerging Exarch-aspirant?<br /> <br /> Also arrows and Arrows are pointy and are used both to point the way and poke people. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T03:14:40-08:00","id":1060797,"title":"","content":"Sure. I had a whole thread dedicated to our home settings, but I neglected because we focused on our L5R games wayyyyyyyyyyy more.<br /> <br /> As for Arrows, one of things on list to play some day or introduce as an NPC is Arrow detective who isn't interested in serving justice or protecting people or whatever, but finds the chase between the detective and the culprit to be ultimate expression of fight and war for your existence - if you get away you &quot;proved&quot; to be worthy of living and you were right to do whatever you did, and if Arrow catches you, they conquer your intelligence and show their intellectual superiority overriding your right to exist.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> ...Actually, I will pitch this to my GM as a rival character for my &quot;Too Wise for her own good&quot; Apostate Detective, because this would serve greatly as her dark mirror.<br /> <br /> EDIT 2<br /> ............it sounds like it would fit right in into a gallery of Phoenix Wright antagonists, huh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-10-2017, 06:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T06:27:45-08:00","id":1060841,"title":"","content":"Seems to fit in with shows like The Wire too, where McNulty and co are less pushed to catch the criminals of Baltimore due to a sense of justice, and more a sense of being intellectually offended by the idea of them outwitting the Po-lice, a battle of wits and cunning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}